  <row Id="1223904" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1223948" CreationDate="2009-08-03T18:32:05.857" Score="3" ViewCount="1495" Body="&lt;p&gt;In the past I have used a DCOM connection to call R functions from Excel and from VBA inside of Excel. I just got a new laptop and have been looking for the install files for the R add in for Excel. I find references to it all over the place but they all point to R (D)COM Server project's home page at &lt;a href=&quot;http://sunsite.univie.ac.at/rcom&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://sunsite.univie.ac.at/rcom&lt;/a&gt;. That URL has been down now for some time. Is there another way to get the same functionality with another method? Is there a new project page? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've never tried to use the DCOM server without the Excel Add-in. Is that a possibility?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="37751" LastActivityDate="2009-08-04T15:04:09.560" Title="Hooking R from within Excel - DCOM? R add in for Excel?" Tags="&lt;excel&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;dcom&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
