  <row Id="1252546" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1252684" CreationDate="2009-08-09T23:00:23.827" Score="18" ViewCount="8614" Body="&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;862 2006-05-19 6.241603 5.774208     &#xA;863 2006-05-20 NA       NA      &#xA;864 2006-05-21 NA       NA      &#xA;865 2006-05-22 6.383929 5.906426      &#xA;866 2006-05-23 6.782068 6.268758      &#xA;867 2006-05-24 6.534616 6.013767      &#xA;868 2006-05-25 6.370312 5.856366      &#xA;869 2006-05-26 6.225175 5.781617      &#xA;870 2006-05-27 NA       NA     &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a data frame x like above with some NA, which i want to fill using neighboring non-NA values like for 2006-05-20 it will be avg of 19&amp;amp;22 &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do it is the question?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="153440" LastEditorUserId="1129408" LastEditDate="2017-03-19T01:31:06.943" LastActivityDate="2019-10-08T13:04:20.760" Title="How to replace NA (missing values) in a data frame with neighbouring values" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;missing-data&gt;&lt;imputation&gt;&lt;locf&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="15" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
