  <row Id="1262911" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2009-08-11T21:04:53.483" Score="1" ViewCount="462" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am loading a table in which the first column is a URL and reading it into R using &lt;code&gt;read.table()&lt;/code&gt;.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It seems that R is dropping about 1/3 of the columns and does not return any errors.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The URLs do not contain any &lt;code&gt;#&lt;/code&gt; characters or tabs (my separator field), which I understand could be an issue.  If I convert the URLs to integer IDs first, the problem goes away.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there something about the field that might be causing R to drop the rows?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerDisplayName="Eytan" LastEditorUserId="1270695" LastEditDate="2015-12-17T05:49:52.463" LastActivityDate="2015-12-17T05:52:23.427" Title="Rows being dropped in R with read.table?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;read.table&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1265129" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1265157" CreationDate="2009-08-12T09:22:08.187" Score="13" ViewCount="2175" Body="&lt;p&gt;Let's say you have this data in R, and you want to post a question on stackoverflow. For others to best help you, it would be nice if they could have a copy of your object (dataframe, vector, etc) to work with.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let's say your data is in a data frame called site.data&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; site.data&#xA;    site year     peak&#xA;1  ALBEN    5 101529.6&#xA;2  ALBEN   10 117483.4&#xA;3  ALBEN   20 132960.9&#xA;8  ALDER    5   6561.3&#xA;9  ALDER   10   7897.1&#xA;10 ALDER   20   9208.1&#xA;15 AMERI    5  43656.5&#xA;16 AMERI   10  51475.3&#xA;17 AMERI   20  58854.4&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do you package it up so that the users can recreate the data exactly as you have it? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You want to do this without having people download a text file and import it.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Note: These data subsetted from an example of the REvolutions blog)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="23929" LastEditorUserId="23929" LastEditDate="2009-08-12T12:08:51.847" LastActivityDate="2010-08-12T09:30:53.437" Title="How to export the definition of an R object to plain text so that others can recreate it?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;export&gt;&lt;structure&gt;&lt;definition&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="12" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
