  <row Id="1319698" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1321491" CreationDate="2009-08-23T22:12:28.103" Score="22" ViewCount="1264" Body="&lt;p&gt;Call me lazy, but I just hate typing things like &lt;code&gt;paste(&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;,sep='')&lt;/code&gt; all the time. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I know that &quot;(t)his is R. There is no if, only how.&quot; (&lt;code&gt;library(fortunes);(fortune(109)&lt;/code&gt;). So, my follow up question is: Is it possible to easily change this behavior? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="143377" LastEditorUserId="5414452" LastEditDate="2015-12-26T11:53:42.460" LastActivityDate="2017-02-01T02:31:43.677" Title="Why doesn't &quot;+&quot; operate on characters in R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;syntax&gt;&lt;operators&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
