  <row Id="1385873" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1386227" CreationDate="2009-09-06T15:04:43.183" Score="1" ViewCount="1429" Body="&lt;p&gt;I guess there will be a very simple answer to this. But here goes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Data in long format. like this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;d &amp;lt;- data.frame(cbind(numbers = rnorm(10), &#xA;                         year = rep(c(2008, 2009), 5), &#xA;                         name = c(&quot;john&quot;, &quot;David&quot;, &quot;Tom&quot;, &quot;Kristin&quot;, &quot;Lisa&quot;,&quot;Eve&quot;,&quot;David&quot;,&quot;Tom&quot;,&quot;Kristin&quot;,&quot;Lisa&quot;)))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do I get a new dataframe only with rows for names that occur in both 2008 and 2009? (i.e. with only David, Kristin, Lisa and Tom).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks in advance&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="162832" LastEditorUserId="3768871" LastEditDate="2019-04-29T03:34:33.093" LastActivityDate="2019-04-29T03:34:33.093" Title="data.frame subset long format" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="3224" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3225" CreationDate="2008-08-06T09:38:15.417" Score="63" ViewCount="7584" Body="&lt;p&gt;CSS and Javascript files don't change very often, so I want them to be cached by the web browser. But I also want the web browser to see changes made to these files without requiring the user to clear their browser cache. Also want a solution that works well with a version control system such as Subversion.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Some solutions I have seen involve adding a version number to the end of the file in the form of a query string.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Could use the SVN revision number to automate this for you: &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2308/aspnet-display-svn-revision-number&quot;&gt;ASP.NET Display SVN Revision Number&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can you specify how you include the &lt;a href=&quot;http://svnbook.red-bean.com/en/1.4/svn.advanced.props.special.keywords.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Revision&lt;/a&gt; variable of another file? That is in the HTML file I can include the Revision number in the URL to the CSS or Javascript file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the &lt;a href=&quot;http://svnbook.red-bean.com&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Subversion book&lt;/a&gt; it says about Revision: &amp;quot;This keyword describes the last known revision in which this file changed in the repository&amp;quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Firefox also allows pressing &lt;kbd&gt;CTRL&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;R&lt;/kbd&gt; to reload everything on a particular page.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To clarify I am looking for solutions that don't require the user to do anything on their part.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="486" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditorDisplayName="Stu Thompson" LastEditDate="2020-06-20T09:12:55.060" LastActivityDate="2021-10-04T12:41:36.303" Title="How can I make the browser see CSS and Javascript changes?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;css&gt;&lt;http&gt;&lt;caching&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="6" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
