  <row Id="1395206" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2009-09-08T17:24:41.847" Score="3" ViewCount="2224" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have two vectors, &lt;code&gt;subject&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;target&lt;/code&gt;. I want to create a new vector based on comparisons between the two existing vectors, with elements being compared &lt;code&gt;lagged&lt;/code&gt;. I've solved this okay using the loop below, but I'm essentially wondering whether there's a more elegant solution using &lt;code&gt;apply&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;subject &amp;lt;- c(200, 195, 190, 185, 185, 185, 188, 189, 195, 200, 210, 210)&#xA;target &amp;lt;- c(subject[1], subject[1]-cumsum(rep(perweek, length(subject)-1)))&#xA;adjtarget &amp;lt;- target                                               &#xA;&#xA;for (i in 1:(length(subject)-1)) {&#xA;  if (subject[i] &amp;gt; adjtarget[i]) {                &#xA;    adjtarget[i+1] &amp;lt;- adjtarget[i]           &#xA;   } else {                                       &#xA;    adjtarget[i+1] &amp;lt;- adjtarget[i]-perweek  }&#xA;   }&#xA; }&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170048" LastEditorUserId="10068985" LastEditDate="2019-02-22T15:32:46.390" LastActivityDate="2019-02-22T15:32:46.390" Title="New vector based on comparing elements of two other vectors &quot;lagged&quot;?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="4052" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4139" CreationDate="2008-08-06T22:02:33.993" Score="18" ViewCount="16576" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to enable Full-text indexing in SQL Server 2005 Express. I am running this on my laptop with Vista Ultimate.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I understand that the standard version of SQL Server Express does not have full-text indexing. I have already downloaded and installed &quot;Microsoft SQL Server 2005 Express Edition with Advanced Services Service Pack 2&quot; (&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/details.aspx?FamilyID=5B5528B9-13E1-4DB9-A3FC-82116D598C3D&amp;amp;displaylang=en&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;download&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have also ensured that both the &quot;SQL Server (instance)&quot; and &quot;SQL Server FullText Search (instance)&quot; services are running on the same account which is &quot;Network Service&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have also selected the option to &quot;Use full-text indexing&quot; in the Database Properties &gt; Files area.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I can run the sql query &quot;SELECT fulltextserviceproperty('IsFulltextInstalled');&quot; and return 1.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem I am having is that when I have my table open in design view and select &quot;Manage FullText Index&quot;; the full-text index window displays the message... &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&quot;Creation of the full-text index is not available. Check that you have the correct permissions or that full-text catalogs are defined.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any ideas on what to check or where to go next?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="576" LastEditorUserId="2641576" LastEditorDisplayName="Nigel Campbell" LastEditDate="2014-11-25T20:40:52.483" LastActivityDate="2017-12-14T09:48:20.193" Title="How to enable Full-text Indexing in SQL Server 2005 Express?" Tags="&lt;sql-server&gt;&lt;sql-server-2