  <row Id="1395233" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1671716" CreationDate="2009-09-08T17:29:55.520" Score="7" ViewCount="753" Body="&lt;p&gt;Say I have the following function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;foo &amp;lt;- function(x, y = min(m)) {&#xA;    m &amp;lt;- 1:10&#xA;    x + y&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I run &lt;code&gt;foo(1)&lt;/code&gt;, the returned value is &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, as expected. However, I cannot run &lt;code&gt;foo(1, y = max(m))&lt;/code&gt; and receive &lt;code&gt;11&lt;/code&gt;, since lazy evaluation only works for default arguments. How can I supply an argument but have it evaluate lazily?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="143383" LastEditorUserId="415690" LastEditDate="2011-01-13T20:24:34.920" LastActivityDate="2015-05-13T14:20:35.503" Title="Lazy evaluation of supplied arguments" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;lazy-evaluation&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
