  <row Id="4556" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4562" CreationDate="2008-08-07T10:01:04.823" Score="13" ViewCount="7989" Body="&lt;p&gt;Which of the following has the best performance?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have seen method two implemented in JavaScript with huge performance gains, however, I was unable to measure any gain in C# and was wondering if the compiler already does method 2 even when written like method 1.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The theory behind method 2 is that the code doesn't have to access DataTable.Rows.Count on every iteration, it can simple access the int c.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Method 1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (int i = 0; i &amp;lt; DataTable.Rows.Count; i++) {&#xA;    // Do Something&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Method 2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (int i = 0, c = DataTable.Rows.Count; i &amp;lt; c; i++) {&#xA;    // Do Something&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="383" LastEditorUserId="2000557" LastEditDate="2013-10-17T19:44:11.380" LastActivityDate="2013-10-17T19:44:11.380" Title="DataTable Loop Performance Comparison" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;performance&gt;&lt;loops&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
