  <row Id="5087" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1158483" CreationDate="2008-08-07T18:17:22.323" Score="21" ViewCount="9150" Body="&lt;p&gt;My company is in the process of starting down the &lt;strong&gt;Grails&lt;/strong&gt; path. The reason for that is that the current developers are heavy on &lt;strong&gt;Java&lt;/strong&gt; but felt the need for a &lt;strong&gt;MVC-style language&lt;/strong&gt; for some future web development projects. Personally, I'm coming from the design/usability world, but as I take more &quot;front-end&quot; responsibilities I'm starting to feel the need for learning a language more intensively so I can code some logic but especially the front-end code for my UIs and stuff.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've been trying to get into &lt;strong&gt;Python/Django&lt;/strong&gt; personally, but just never invested too much time on it. Now that my company is &quot;jumping&quot; into Grails I bought the &quot;&lt;em&gt;Agile Web Development with Rails (3rd Ed - Beta)&lt;/em&gt;&quot; and I'm starting to get into &lt;strong&gt;RoR&lt;/strong&gt;. I'd still like to learn &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt; in the future or on the side, but my biggest question is: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Should I be learning RoR, and have a more versatile language in my &quot;portfolio&quot;, knowing that my RoR knowledge will be useful for my Grails needs as well??&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;-OR-&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Should I just skip RoR and focus on learning Grails that I'll be needing for work soon, and work on learning RoR/Django (Ruby/Python) later?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Basically the question revolves around the usefulness of Grails in a non-corporate setting and the similarities between Rails and Grails. (and this, while trying to avoid the centennial discussion of Python vs Ruby (on Rails) :))&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="682" LastEditorUserId="2173917" LastEditorDisplayName="Justin Standard" LastEditDate="2015-01-17T10:21:52.713" LastActivityDate="2019-11-25T18:18:01.577" Title="Learning Ruby on Rails any good for Grails?" Tags="&lt;ruby-on-rails&gt;&lt;ruby&gt;&lt;grails&gt;&lt;groovy&gt;" AnswerCount="15" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="6" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
