  <row Id="1413853" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1416912" CreationDate="2009-09-12T00:28:22.303" Score="5" ViewCount="1407" Body="&lt;p&gt;I love the Emacs ESS combination.  I love sending lines, functions, regions, and buffers of code to the command line for evaluation without using the mouse.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, I've noticed that the &lt;code&gt;Eval Function&lt;/code&gt; command in Emacs is much slower than simply running &lt;code&gt;source(&quot;fns.R&quot;)&lt;/code&gt;, where &lt;code&gt;fns.R&lt;/code&gt; is the file that contains the function I want to evaluate.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Why is this the case?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="84458" LastActivityDate="2009-09-13T05:14:35.170" Title="Emacs ESS: Eval region vs. source()" Tags="&lt;emacs&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;ess&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
