  <row Id="7269" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="46902" CreationDate="2008-08-10T18:06:04.820" Score="8" ViewCount="2092" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm part of a team that develops a pretty big Swing Java Applet. Most of our code are legacy and there are tons of singleton references. We've bunched all of them to a single &quot;Application Context&quot; singleton. What we now need is to create some way to separate the shared context (shared across all applets currently showing) and non-shared context (specific to each applet currently showing). &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, we don't have an ID at each of the locations that call to the singleton, nor do we want to propagate the ID to all locations. What's the easiest way to identify in which applet context we're running? (I've tried messing with classloaders, thread groups, thread ids... so far I could find nothing that will enable me to ID the origin of the call).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="931" OwnerDisplayName="Ran Biron" LastEditorUserId="407418" LastEditDate="2016-03-11T17:58:30.780" LastActivityDate="2016-03-11T17:58:30.780" Title="How can I identify in which Java Applet context running without passing an ID?" Tags="&lt;java&gt;&lt;swing&gt;&lt;applet&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1524088" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1525003" CreationDate="2009-10-06T07:34:10.973" Score="3" ViewCount="3554" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working on a script that creates a package in the current directory (using pdInfoBuilder from BioConductor), and I'd like to install it while the script is running. &lt;code&gt;install.packages()&lt;/code&gt; with repo=NULL seems like an obvious choice, but this seems to only except package directories tarballed and gzipped. Is there a way I can override this, since the &lt;code&gt;create.pkg()&lt;/code&gt; function doesn't create a *.tar.gz? Currently I am using:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;R CMD INSTALL package.name&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&#xA;Vince&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="147427" LastActivityDate="2009-10-06T13:09:28.207" Title="Installing a local package that's not a .tar.gz" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;bioconductor&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="7272" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-10T18:11:08.100" Score="3" ViewCount="1070" Body="&lt;p&gt;Alright, so maybe I shouldn't have shrunk this question sooo much... I have seen the post on &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/622/most-efficient-code-for-the-first-10000-prime-numbers&quot;&gt;the most efficient way to find the first 10000 primes&lt;/a&gt;.  I'm looking for &lt;strong&gt;all possible ways&lt;/strong&gt;.  The goal is to have a one stop shop for primality tests.  Any and all tests people know for finding prime numbers are welcome.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And so:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are all the different ways of finding primes?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="145" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:33:27.093" LastActivityDate="2011-04-05T18:34:47.393" Title="Of Ways to Count the Limitless Primes" Tags="&lt;language-agnostic&gt;&lt;primes&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ClosedDate="2015-07-13T05:32:39.367" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1528428" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2009-10-06T22:27:55.460" Score="2" ViewCount="968" Body="&lt;p&gt;Could anybody explain to me why&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;simulatedCase &amp;lt;- rbinom(100,1,0.5)&#xA;simDf &amp;lt;- data.frame(CASE = simulatedCase)&#xA;posterior_m0 &amp;lt;&amp;lt;- MCMClogit(CASE ~ 1, data = simDf, b0 = 0, B0 = 1)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;always results in a MCMC acceptance ratio of 0? Any explanation would be greatly appreciated!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="185281" LastEditorUserId="1315767" LastEditDate="2013-05-16T15:06:31.060" LastActivityDate="2013-05-16T15:06:31.060" Title="MCMClogit confusion" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;bayesian&gt;&lt;montecarlo&gt;&lt;markov-chains&gt;&lt;mcmc&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1529559" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1529601" CreationDate="2009-10-07T05:00:23.427" Score="3" ViewCount="423" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is there a more &quot;R-minded&quot; way to dichotomise efficiently? Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;y&amp;lt;-c(0,3,2,1,0,0,2,5,0,1,0,0);b&amp;lt;-vector()&#xA;&#xA;for (k in 1:length(y)) {&#xA;    if (y[k] == 0) b[k] = 0&#xA;    else&#xA;        b[k] = 1&#xA;}&#xA;y;b&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="182378" LastEditorUserId="1315767" LastEditDate="2013-05-16T15:05:11.960" LastActivityDate="2013-05-16T15:05:27.587" Title="How do I dichotomise efficiently" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;performance&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1530999" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2009-10-07T11:17:16.237" Score="2" ViewCount="1240" Body="&lt;p&gt;I use the package &lt;code&gt;languageR&lt;/code&gt; for mixed effect models with the syntax at the end of this posting. I can use &lt;code&gt;pvals.fnc&lt;/code&gt; to get &lt;em&gt;p&lt;/em&gt;-values for models 1 and 3 (&lt;code&gt;hd_lmer1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;hd_lmer2&lt;/code&gt;). Using this with model two gives the following error message:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;p2 = pvals.fnc(hd_lmer2)&#xA;  Error in pvals.fnc(hd_lmer2) : &#xA;    MCMC sampling is not yet implemented in lme4_0.999375&#xA;    for models with random correlation parameters&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would be grateful if any one could help me out on how to get p-values for such models.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Models:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;hd_lmer1 &amp;lt;- lmer(&#xA;  rot ~ time + group + sex + gen + (1 | subject) + (1 | rot.pre),&#xA;  data = data_long,&#xA;  REML = TRUE&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;hd_lmer2 &amp;lt;- lmer(&#xA;  rot ~ time + group + sex + gen + (time | subject) + (1 | rot.pre),&#xA;  data = data_long,&#xA;  REML = TRUE&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;hd_lmer3 &amp;lt;- lmer(&#xA;  rot ~ time * group + sex + gen + (1 | subject) + (1 | rot.pre),&#xA;  data = data_long,&#xA;  REML = TRUE&#xA;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="185556" LastEditorUserId="5436877" LastEditDate="2019-05-08T06:38:51.233" LastActivityDate="2019-05-08T06:38:51.233" Title="LanguageR/ lme4: any help on p-values for models with random correlation parameters?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;&lt;lme4&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="7277" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7292" CreationDate="2008-08-10T18:20:38.130" Score="8" ViewCount="3862" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm generating some XML documents and when it comes to the address part I have fragments that look like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Address&amp;gt;15 Sample St&#xA;Example Bay&#xA;Some Country&amp;lt;/Address&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The XSLT that I have for converting this to XHTML has some funky recursive template to convert newline characters within strings to &amp;lt;br/&amp;gt; tags.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is all working fine; but is it considered &quot;bad practice&quot; to rely on linebreaks within XML documents?  If so, is it recommended that I do this instead?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Address&amp;gt;&amp;lt;Line&amp;gt;15 Sample St&amp;lt;/Line&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;Line&amp;gt;Example Bay&amp;lt;/Line&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;Line&amp;gt;Some Country&amp;lt;/Line&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/Address&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Seems like it'd be really awkward to wrap every place where my text may be multiple lines with tags like that..&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="755" LastEditorUserId="2134" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris" LastEditDate="2008-09-26T20:20:08.893" LastActivityDate="2015-12-15T19:49:00.210" Title="Is it &quot;bad practice&quot; to be sensitive to linebreaks in XML documents?" Tags="&lt;xml&gt;&lt;xslt&gt;&lt;xhtml&gt;&lt;whitespace&gt;&lt;line-breaks&gt;" AnswerCount="12" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="7284" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7320" CreationDate="2008-08-10T18:41:02.300" Score="629" ViewCount="243923" Body="&lt;p&gt;What does the expression &quot;Turing Complete&quot; mean? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can you give a simple explanation, without going into too many theoretical details?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="198" LastEditorUserId="373539" LastEditDate="2012-06-23T00:22:15.250" LastActivityDate="2021-04-10T17:47:05.353" Title="What is Turing Complete?" Tags="&lt;theory&gt;&lt;turing-machines&gt;&lt;turing-complete&gt;" AnswerCount="14" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="205" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="7287" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7296" CreationDate="2008-08-10T18:49:53.920" Score="9" ViewCount="1773" Body="&lt;p&gt;Lately I had to change some code on older systems where not all of the code has unit tests.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Before making the changes I want to write tests, but each class created a lot of dependencies and other anti-patterns which made testing quite hard.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Obviously, I wanted to refactor the code to make it easier to test, write the tests and then change it.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Is this the way you'd do it? Or would you spend a lot of time writing the hard-to-write tests that would be mostly removed after the refactoring will be completed?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="573" LastEditorUserId="233076" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris Fournier" LastEditDate="2016-03-07T16:52:14.380" LastActivityDate="2016-03-07T16:52:14.380" Title="How do you test/change untested and untestable code?" Tags="&lt;unit-testing&gt;&lt;refactoring&gt;&lt;legacy&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="7348" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7351" CreationDate="2008-08-10T21:00:14.173" Score="9" ViewCount="7649" Body="&lt;p&gt;My requirements:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Support .NET Compact Framework 2.0 and Windows Mobile 6.0 devices.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Only need to unzip the contents to a directory on a storage card. Creation of zip files is not required.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Must be able to use in corporate/commercial software.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Can be open source, but not have GPL or other viral license.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've seen the &lt;a href=&quot;http://xceed.com/Zip_NET_CF_Intro.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Xceed Zip for CF&lt;/a&gt; library. What other options are there?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="636" LastEditorUserId="12870" LastEditorDisplayName="Oli" LastEditDate="2008-09-24T15:31:20.207" LastActivityDate="2011-03-08T13:07:51.157" Title="Zip library options for the Compact Framework?" Tags="&lt;windows-mobile&gt;&lt;compact-framework&gt;&lt;zip&gt;&lt;components&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="7364" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7455" CreationDate="2008-08-10T21:58:24.913" Score="86" ViewCount="133280" Body="&lt;p&gt;Does anyone know of a good method for editing PDFs in PHP? Preferably open-source/zero-license cost methods. :)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am thinking along the lines of opening a PDF file, replacing text in the PDF and then writing out the modified version of the PDF?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;On the front-end&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="277" LastEditorUserId="1420625" LastEditDate="2021-07-27T15:27:42.933" LastActivityDate="2021-07-27T15:27:42.933" Title="Edit PDF en PHP?" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;pdf&gt;" AnswerCount="9" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="50" ClosedDate="2014-09-08T17:16:40.013" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="7367" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7399" CreationDate="2008-08-10T22:06:49.670" Score="11" ViewCount="3885" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm looking for help setting a new default property value for an inherited control in Visual Studio:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;class NewCombo : System.Windows.Forms.ComboBox&#xA;{&#xA;  public NewCombo() { DropDownItems = 50; }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem is that the base class property &lt;code&gt;DropDownItems&lt;/code&gt; has a 'default' attribute set on it that is a different value (not 50).  As a result, when I drag the control onto a form, the designer file gets an explicit &lt;code&gt;mycontrol.DropDownItems = 50;&lt;/code&gt; line.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;At first, this doesn't matter.  But if later I change my inherited class to &lt;code&gt;DropDownItems = 45;&lt;/code&gt; in the constructor, this does not affect any of the controls on any form since all those designer files still have the value 50 hard-coded in them.  And the whole point was to have the value set in one place so I can deal with the customer changing his mind.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Obviously, if I were creating my own custom property in the subclass, I could give it its own designer default attribute of whatever I wanted.  But here I'm wanting to change the default values of properties in the base.  Is there any way to apply Visual Studio attributes to a base class member?  Or is there some other workaround to get the result I want?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="945" LastEditorUserId="567854" LastEditDate="2019-01-20T13:55:20.363" LastActivityDate="2019-01-20T13:55:20.363" Title="Visual Studio - new &quot;default&quot; property values for inherited controls" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;vb.net&gt;&lt;visual-studio&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="7398" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26994" CreationDate="2008-08-10T23:10:53.190" Score="9" ViewCount="1735" Body="&lt;p&gt;I haven't seen any questions relating to GNU autoconf/automake builds, but I'm hoping at least some of you out there are familiar with it.  Here goes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a project (I'll call it myproject) that includes another project (vendor).  The vendor project is a standalone project maintained by someone else.  Including a project like this is fairly &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.gnu.org/software/autoconf/manual/autoconf.html#Subdirectories&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;straightforward&lt;/a&gt;, but in this case there is a tiny snag: each project generates its own &lt;code&gt;config.h&lt;/code&gt; file, each of which defines standard macros such as PACKAGE, VERSION, etc.  This means that, during the build, when vendor is being built, I get lots of errors like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;... warning: &quot;VERSION&quot; redefined&#xA;... warning: this is the location of the previous definition&#xA;... warning: &quot;PACKAGE&quot; redefined&#xA;... warning: this is the location of the previous definition&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These are just warnings, for the time being at least, but I would like to get rid of them.  The only relevant information I've been able to turn up with a Google search is &lt;a href=&quot;http://sourceware.org/ml/automake/2004-03/msg00130.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;this&lt;/a&gt; thread on the automake mailing list, which isn't a whole lot of help.  Does anybody else have any better ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="737" LastEditorUserId="67579" LastEditDate="2015-10-08T01:10:35.300" LastActivityDate="2015-10-08T01:12:02.947" Title="How to avoid redefining VERSION, PACKAGE, etc" Tags="&lt;c&gt;&lt;linux&gt;&lt;unix&gt;&lt;autoconf&gt;&lt;automake&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1532535" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="6054174" CreationDate="2009-10-07T15:56:02.437" Score="10" ViewCount="7832" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've got a nice facet_wrap density plot that I have created with &lt;code&gt;ggplot2&lt;/code&gt;. I would like for each panel to have x and y axis labels instead of only having the y axis labels along the left side and the x labels along the bottom. What I have right now looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(ggplot2)&#xA;myGroups &amp;lt;- sample(c(&amp;quot;Mo&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Larry&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Curly&amp;quot;), 100, replace=T)&#xA;myValues &amp;lt;- rnorm(300)&#xA;df &amp;lt;- data.frame(myGroups, myValues)&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;p &amp;lt;- ggplot(df)  + &#xA;  geom_density(aes(myValues), fill = alpha(&amp;quot;#335785&amp;quot;, .6)) + &#xA;  facet_wrap(~ myGroups)&#xA;p&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Which returns:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/eGnAF.png&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/eGnAF.png&quot; alt=&quot;alt text&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;sub&gt;(source: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.cerebralmastication.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/10/3stooges.png&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;cerebralmastication.com&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It seems like this should be simple, but my Google Fu has been too poor to find an answer.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="37751" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2020-06-20T09:12:55.060" LastActivityDate="2019-07-24T16:36:54.927" Title="Showing multiple axis labels using ggplot2 with facet_wrap in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;&lt;facet-wrap&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="7440" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="20754" CreationDate="2008-08-11T00:05:36.590" Score="35" ViewCount="11448" Body="&lt;p&gt;The company I'm currently working for is using &lt;a href=&quot;http://selenium.openqa.org/&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Selenium&lt;/a&gt; for Uniting-Testing our User Interface. What do you use to Unit-Test your Web UI and how effective do you find it? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="889" LastEditorUserId="2134" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris Fournier" LastEditDate="2008-08-23T19:49:05.370" LastActivityDate="2018-06-28T11:10:56.510" Title="What do you use to Unit-Test your Web UI?" Tags="&lt;unit-testing&gt;&lt;user-interface&gt;&lt;selenium&gt;" AnswerCount="15" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="13" ClosedDate="2012-12-22T19:07:37.017" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="7470" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-11T01:32:16.090" Score="2" ViewCount="835" Body="&lt;p&gt;After a couple of hours fighting with the &lt;a href=&quot;http://gallery.menalto.com/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Gallery2&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://codex.gallery2.org/Gallery2:Modules:rss&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;RSS module&lt;/a&gt; and getting only the message, &quot;no feeds have yet been defined&quot;, I gave up.  Based on &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.google.com/search?q=%22no+feeds+have+yet+been+defined%22&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;a Google search for &quot;no feeds have yet been defined&quot;&lt;/a&gt;, this is a pretty common problem.  Do you have any tips and/or tricks for getting the Gallery2 RSS module to work?  Or any tips for a relatively-PHP-ignorant developer trying to debug problems with this PHP application?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="150" LastEditorUserId="6556397" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris Fournier" LastEditDate="2019-06-04T09:30:15.970" LastActivityDate="2019-06-04T09:30:15.970" Title="RSS feeds from Gallery2" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;web-applications&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="1533493" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1533577" CreationDate="2009-10-07T18:55:42.543" Score="17" ViewCount="33608" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm running into difficulties reshaping a large dataframe. And I've been relatively fortunate in avoiding reshaping problems in the past, which also means I'm terrible at it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My current dataframe looks something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;unique_id    seq   response    detailed.name    treatment &#xA;a            N1     123.23     descr. of N1     T1&#xA;a            N2     231.12     descr. of N2     T1&#xA;a            N3     231.23     descr. of N3     T1&#xA;...&#xA;b            N1     343.23     descr. of N1     T2&#xA;b            N2     281.13     descr. of N2     T2&#xA;b            N3     901.23     descr. of N3     T2&#xA;...&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And I'd like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;seq    detailed.name   T1           T2&#xA;N1     descr. of N1    123.23       343.23&#xA;N2     descr. of N2    231.12       281.13&#xA;N3     descr. of N3    231.23       901.23&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've looked into the reshape package, but I'm not sure how I can convert the treatment factors into individual column names. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: I tried running this on my local machine (4GB dual-core iMac 3.06Ghz) and it keeps failing with: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; d.tmp.2 &amp;lt;- cast(d.tmp, `SEQ_ID` + `GENE_INFO` ~ treatments)&#xA;Aggregation requires fun.aggregate: length used as default&#xA;R(5751) malloc: *** mmap(size=647168) failed (error code=12)&#xA;*** error: can't allocate region&#xA;*** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'll try running this on one of our bigger machines when I get a chance. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="147427" LastEditorUserId="147427" LastEditDate="2009-10-07T20:33:32.050" LastActivityDate="2017-03-05T06:40:22.547" Title="Reshaping data frame in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;&lt;reshape&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="17" ClosedDate="2017-08-24T21:56:45.863" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1535021" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1535433" CreationDate="2009-10-08T00:48:13.280" Score="58" ViewCount="6449" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is there a certain R-gotcha that had you really surprised one day? I think we'd all gain from sharing these.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here's mine: in list indexing, &lt;code&gt;my.list[[1]]&lt;/code&gt; is not &lt;code&gt;my.list[1]&lt;/code&gt;. Learned this in the early days of R.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="147427" LastEditorUserId="792066" LastEditDate="2017-03-05T17:05:07.360" LastActivityDate="2020-11-22T22:15:11.903" Title="What's the biggest R-gotcha you've run across?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;r-faq&gt;" AnswerCount="29" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="50" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="7472" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7479" CreationDate="2008-08-11T01:34:34.773" Score="11" ViewCount="3792" Body="&lt;p&gt;Can anyone point me to a good resource (or throw me a clue) to show me how to do DataBinding to controls (ComboBox, ListBox, etc.) in WPF?  I'm at a bit of a loss when all my WinForms niceities are taken away from me, and I'm not all that bright to start with...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="856" LastEditorUserId="1369235" LastEditDate="2013-01-29T12:25:02.847" LastActivityDate="2020-06-24T14:06:19.123" Title="WPF Databinding" Tags="&lt;wpf&gt;&lt;data-binding&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="7477" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7523" CreationDate="2008-08-11T01:43:13.493" Score="128" ViewCount="151770" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm currently working on an internal sales application for the company I work for, and I've got a form that allows the user to change the delivery address.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now I think it would look much nicer, if the textarea I'm using for the main address details would just take up the area of the text in it, and automatically resize if the text was changed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here's a screenshot of it currently.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/XK48E.png&quot; alt=&quot;ISO Address&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;@Chris&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A good point, but there are reasons I want it to resize. I want the area it takes up to be the area of the information contained in it. As you can see in the screen shot, if I have a fixed textarea, it takes up a fair wack of vertical space.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I can reduce the font, but I need address to be large and readable. Now I can reduce the size of the text area, but then I have problems with people who have an address line that takes 3 or 4 (one takes 5) lines. Needing to have the user use a scrollbar is a major no-no.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I guess I should be a bit more specific. I'm after vertical resizing, and the width doesn't matter as much. The only problem that happens with that, is the ISO number (the large &quot;1&quot;) gets pushed under the address when the window width is too small (as you can see on the screenshot).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It's not about having a gimick; it's about having a text field the user can edit that won't take up unnecessary space, but will show all the text in it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Though if someone comes up with another way to approach the problem I'm open to that too.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've modified the code a little because it was acting a little odd. I changed it to activate on keyup, because it wouldn't take into consideration the character that was just typed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;resizeIt = function() {&#xA;  var str = $('iso_address').value;&#xA;  var cols = $('iso_address').cols;&#xA;  var linecount = 0;&#xA;&#xA;  $A(str.split(&quot;\n&quot;)).each(function(l) {&#xA;    linecount += 1 + Math.floor(l.length / cols); // Take into account long lines&#xA;  })&#xA;&#xA;  $('iso_address').rows = linecount;&#xA;};&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="841" LastEditorUserId="10757987" LastEditorDisplayName="Mike" LastEditDate="2019-01-03T06:54:14.567" LastActivityDate="2020-03-09T14:10:06.593" Title="How to autosize a textarea using Prototype?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;css&gt;&lt;textarea&gt;&lt;prototypejs&gt;" AnswerCount="18" CommentCount="4" FavoriteCount="68" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="7489" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="13384" CreationDate="2008-08-11T02:50:09.113" Score="8" ViewCount="2307" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've made many different seperate parts of a GUI system for the Nintendo DS, like buttons and textboxes and select boxes, but I need a way of containing these classes in one Gui class, so that I can draw everything to the screen all at once, and check all the buttons at once to check if any are being pressed. My question is what is the best way organize all the classes (such as buttons and textboxes) into one GUI class?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here's one way I thought of but it doesn't seem right:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edit:&lt;/strong&gt; I'm using C++.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;class Gui {&#xA;    public:&#xA;        void update_all();&#xA;        void draw_all() const;&#xA;        int add_button(Button *button); // Returns button id&#xA;        void remove_button(int button_id);&#xA;    private:&#xA;        Button *buttons[10];&#xA;        int num_buttons;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This code has a few problems, but I just wanted to give you an idea of what I want.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="813" LastEditorUserId="2921691" LastEditorDisplayName="Jeremy Ruten" LastEditDate="2016-02-07T18:07:20.857" LastActivityDate="2017-12-17T03:51:26.807" Title="How do I make a GUI?" Tags="&lt;c++&gt;&lt;user-interface&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="1535086" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1535240" CreationDate="2009-10-08T01:12:24.270" Score="0" ViewCount="739" Body="&lt;p&gt;Hi we're trying to get R with the standard gui loaded onto CentOS 4, and under certain users R will not render certain graphics.  When logged in as root the graphics render, but under the restricted user they don't.  The graphics don't render with the error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; testdata &amp;lt;- rbind(c(1,2,3,4,5,6),c(3,4,5,4,6,2),c(3,6,7,2,2,1),c(5,4,9,8,9,1))&#xA;&amp;gt; pairs(testdata)&#xA;Error in text.default(x, y, txt, cex = cex, font = font) : &#xA; X11 font -adobe-helvetica-%s-%s-*-*-%d-*-*-*-*-*-*-*, face 1 at size 16 could not be loaded&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Anyone come across this one or have any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="176696" LastEditorUserId="143305" LastEditDate="2009-10-08T02:03:32.943" LastActivityDate="2015-07-09T08:33:29.590" Title="Problem with R rendering base Graphics in CentOS 4" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;x11&gt;&lt;centos&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1536486" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1537077" CreationDate="2009-10-08T08:44:56.563" Score="1" ViewCount="423" Body="&lt;p&gt;When in auctex and noweb-mode (using Sweave in emacs), I find it distracting when the screen recenters itself as I use next-line, previous-line, etc. (C-n, C-p, and mouse-1). Does anyone know how to turn it off? Thanks much!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="143476" LastActivityDate="2009-10-08T10:58:47.357" Title="emacs, auctex, noweb-mode - how to keep screen from recentering around point?" Tags="&lt;emacs&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;sweave&gt;&lt;auctex&gt;&lt;noweb&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="7492" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-11T03:00:26.957" Score="247" ViewCount="164175" Body="&lt;p&gt;In the past, I used Microsoft Web Application Stress Tool and Pylot to stress test web applications. I'd written a simple home page, login script, and site walkthrough (in an ecommerce site adding a few items to a cart and checkout).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Just hitting the homepage hard with a handful of developers would almost always locate a major problem. More scalability problems would surface at the second stage, and even more - after the launch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The URL of the tools I used were Microsoft Homer (aka &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/details.aspx?familyid=e2c0585a-062a-439e-a67d-75a89aa36495&amp;amp;displaylang=en&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Microsoft Web Application Stress Tool&lt;/a&gt;) and &lt;a href=&quot;https://code.google.com/archive/p/pylt/&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Pylot&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The reports generated by these tools never made much sense to me, and I would spend many hours trying to figure out what kind of concurrent load the site would be able to support. It was always worth it because the stupidest bugs and bottlenecks would always come up (for instance, web server misconfigurations).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What have you done, what tools have you used, and what success have you had with your approach? The part that is most interesting to me is coming up with some kind of a meaningful formula for calculating the number of concurrent users an app can support from the numbers reported by the stress test application.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="556" LastEditorUserId="1000551" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris" LastEditDate="2017-10-25T14:52:17.603" LastActivityDate="2018-08-30T15:01:26.923" Title="Performing a Stress Test on Web Application?" Tags="&lt;web-applications&gt;&lt;stress-testing&gt;&lt;performance&gt;&lt;webapplicationstresstool&gt;&lt;pylot&gt;" AnswerCount="30" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="174" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="7503" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="7512" CreationDate="2008-08-11T03:54:43.947" Score="12" ViewCount="43505" Body="&lt;p&gt;I know almost nothing about linq.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm doing this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var apps = from app in Process.GetProcesses()&#xA;    where app.ProcessName.Contains( &quot;MyAppName&quot; ) &amp;amp;&amp;amp; app.MainWindowHandle != IntPtr.Zero&#xA;    select app;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Which gets me all the running processes which match that criteria.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I don't know how to get the first one. The examples I can find on the net seem to imply I have to do this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var matchedApp = (from app in Process.GetProcesses()&#xA;    where app.ProcessName.Contains( &quot;MyAppName&quot; ) &amp;amp;&amp;amp; app.MainWindowHandle != IntPtr.Zero&#xA;    select app).First();&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;which strikes me as somewhat ugly, and also throws an exception if there are no matching processes. Is there a better way?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPDATE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm actually trying to find the first matching item, and call &lt;code&gt;SetForegroundWindow&lt;/code&gt; on it&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've come up with this solution, which also strikes me as ugly and awful, but better than above. Any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var unused = from app in Process.GetProcesses()&#xA;    where app.ProcessName.Contains( &quot;MyAppName&quot; ) &amp;amp;&amp;amp; app.MainWindowHandle != IntPtr.Zero&#xA;    select SetForegroundWindow( app.MainWindowHandle ); // side-effects in linq-query is technically bad I guess&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="234" LastEditorUserId="234" LastEditorDisplayName="Orion Edwards" LastEditDate="2008-08-11T04:07:29.787" LastActivityDate="2016-02-07T18:06:50.830" Title="Linq to objects - select first object" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;linq&gt;&lt;linq-to-objects&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
