  <row Id="7851" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-11T15:12:53.903" Score="8" ViewCount="4698" Body="&lt;p&gt;According to the &lt;a href=&quot;http://uk3.php.net/features.safe-mode&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;PHP Safe Mode Docs&lt;/a&gt; on safe_mode_gid:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;By default, Safe Mode does a UID compare check when opening files. If you want to relax this to a GID compare, then turn on safe_mode_gid. Whether to use UID (FALSE) or GID (TRUE) checking upon file access.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To a PHP script running on a web server, what is the difference between a UID (User Identifier) check and a GID (Group identifier) check?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="840" LastEditorUserId="6556397" LastEditorDisplayName="jodonnell" LastEditDate="2019-06-04T09:30:35.203" LastActivityDate="2019-06-04T09:30:35.203" Title="What is PHP Safe Mode GID?" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;unix&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
