  <row Id="1653710" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1654241" CreationDate="2009-10-31T07:39:46.847" Score="1" ViewCount="1191" Body="&lt;p&gt;Suppose we have the contents of tables x and y in two dataframes in R. Which is the suggested way to perform an operation like the following in sql:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Select x.X1, x.X2, y.X3&#xA;into z&#xA;from x inner join y on x.X1 = y.X1&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried the following in R. Is there a better way? &#xA;Thank you&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x&amp;lt;-data.frame(cbind('X1'=c(5,9,7,6,4,8,3,1,10,2),'X2'=c(5,9,7,6,4,8,3,1,10,2)^2))&#xA;y&amp;lt;-data.frame(cbind('X1'=c(9,5,8,2),'X3'=c('nine','five','eight','two')))&#xA;&#xA;z&amp;lt;-cbind(x[which(x$X1 %in% (y$X1)), c(1:2)][order(x[which(x$X1 %in% (y$X1)), c(1:2)]$X1),],y[order(y$X1),2])&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170792" LastActivityDate="2009-10-31T13:52:33.157" Title="r analogous to sql inner join selection" Tags="&lt;sql&gt;&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
