  <row Id="8651" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="8687" CreationDate="2008-08-12T10:37:50.107" Score="4" ViewCount="6715" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to load Linq on my .Net 3.5 enabled web server by adding the following to my .aspx page:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;%@ Import Namespace=&quot;System.Query&quot; %&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, this fails and tells me it cannot find the namespace.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;The type or namespace name 'Query' does not exist in the namespace 'System' &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have also tried with no luck:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Data.Linq&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Linq&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Xml.Linq&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I believe that .Net 3.5 is working because &lt;code&gt;var hello = &quot;Hello World&quot;&lt;/code&gt; seems to work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can anyone help please?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PS: I just want to clarify that I don't use Visual Studio, I simply have a &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ultraedit.com/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Text Editor&lt;/a&gt; and write my code directly into .aspx files.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="383" OwnerDisplayName="GateKiller" LastEditorUserId="623518" LastEditorDisplayName="GateKiller" LastEditDate="2012-04-25T15:08:24.523" LastActivityDate="2012-04-25T15:08:24.523" Title="Import Namespace System.Query" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;linq&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
