  <row Id="8950" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-12T15:17:47.217" Score="1" ViewCount="9251" Body="&lt;p&gt;We have a SharePoint WSS site and some of our users on on the Mac OSX platform.  Are there any tips or tricks to get a similar experience to Windows with document shares and calendars on the Mac?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: Browsing a SharePoint WSS site on a Mac, whether using Firefox or Safari, has a very similar look and feel as it does on Windows IE.  The similar experience I am looking for has to do with integrating the calendars, document shares, etc. into the desktop.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, with IE you can go to a calendar and select &quot;Actions -&gt; Connect to Outlook&quot; and it will make the calendar visible and manageable from within Outlook.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there any way to get the Mac to work similarly?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="509" OwnerDisplayName="SitWalkStand" LastEditorUserId="2432317" LastEditorDisplayName="SitWalkStand" LastEditDate="2013-12-02T13:36:05.777" LastActivityDate="2013-12-02T13:36:05.777" Title="SharePoint WSS 3.0 Integration with Mac OSX (either Safari or Firefox)" Tags="&lt;sharepoint&gt;&lt;macos&gt;&lt;wss&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
