  <row Id="9044" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="275353" CreationDate="2008-08-12T16:52:08.697" Score="16" ViewCount="11713" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a base class that represents a database test in TestNG, and I want to specify that all classes extending from this class are of a group &quot;db-test&quot;, however I have found that this doesn't seem possible.  I have tried the @Test annotation:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;@Test(groups = { &quot;db-test&quot; })&#xA;public class DBTestBase {&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, this doesn't work because the @Test annotation will try to make a bunch of methods into tests, and warnings/errors pop up in eclipse when the tests are run.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So I tried disabling the test, so at least the groups are assigned:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;@Test(enabled = false, groups = { &quot;db-test&quot; })&#xA;public class DBTestBase {&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but then any @BeforeTest (and other similar annotations) ALSO get disabled... which is of course not what I want.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would like some way to annotate a class as being of a particular type of group, but it doesn't quite seem possible in TestNG.  Does anyone have any other ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="122" OwnerDisplayName="Mike Stone" LastEditorUserId="6309" LastEditorDisplayName="VonC" LastEditDate="2008-11-08T22:51:50.377" LastActivityDate="2020-06-25T18:55:27.810" Title="Can I specify a class wide group on a TestNG test case?" Tags="&lt;java&gt;&lt;testng&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="9052" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="9054" CreationDate="2008-08-12T17:03:28.220" Score="10" ViewCount="26183" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working on a spec for a piece of software for my company and as part of the auditing system I think it would be neat if there was a way to grab the current Active Directory user.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hopefully something like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Dim strUser as String&#xA;strUser = ActiveDirectory.User()&#xA;MsgBox &quot;Welcome back, &quot; &amp;amp; strUser&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="428190" OwnerDisplayName="Andrew G. Johnson" LastEditorUserId="5640" LastEditorDisplayName="Rich B" LastEditDate="2009-03-09T23:02:29.063" LastActivityDate="2020-01-13T14:50:32.073" Title="Is there a way for MS Access to grab the current Active Directory user?" Tags="&lt;ms-access&gt;&lt;active-directory&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1710340" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1710387" CreationDate="2009-11-10T18:57:44.270" Score="16" ViewCount="3496" Body="&lt;p&gt;Sorry for the non-descriptive title but I don't know whether there's a word for what I'm trying to achieve.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let's assume that I have a list of names of different classes like&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;c( '1', '2', '3', '4')&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'd like to generate all possible permutation pairs out of this so that there are no reverse-duplicates. So what I'd like to have is something like&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;'1' '2'&#xA;'1' '3'&#xA;'1' '4'&#xA;'2' '3'&#xA;'2' '4'&#xA;'3' '4'&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that I don't have e.g. &lt;code&gt;'2' '1'&lt;/code&gt; because I already have &lt;code&gt;'1' '2'&lt;/code&gt;. Is there an easy way to achieve this in R?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="101419" LastEditorUserId="3588876" LastEditDate="2018-02-28T12:40:07.033" LastActivityDate="2018-02-28T12:40:07.033" Title="Generating non-duplicate combination pairs in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;combinations&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="9072" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="204732" CreationDate="2008-08-12T17:47:26.213" Score="6" ViewCount="1043" Body="&lt;p&gt;Question for YUI experts...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a table and I've made each cell of the first row draggable by &lt;a href=&quot;http://web.archive.org/web/20160728103125/https://developer.yahoo.com/yui/examples/dragdrop/dd-proxy.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;proxy&lt;/a&gt;. In IE, when the drag proxy is released, the original table cell actually jumps to wherever the release point was. How can I prevent this from happening? Essentially, I want to know where the proxy was dropped and handle my logic from there but I don't want the original to move.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="67" OwnerDisplayName="Rex M" LastEditorUserId="9780149" LastEditorDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditDate="2020-06-25T12:48:23.693" LastActivityDate="2020-06-25T12:48:23.693" Title="YUI drag&amp;drop proxy drag" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;drag-and-drop&gt;&lt;yui&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="1710853" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1710952" CreationDate="2009-11-10T20:10:25.560" Score="29" ViewCount="22795" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm running R 2.9 on a large EC2 Ubuntu instance, loaded with RAM, but without a terminal.  When I load a library that has display dependencies, such as the sqldf package, I receive the following error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(sqldf)&#xA;...&#xA;Loading required package: tcltk&#xA;Loading Tcl/Tk interface ... Error in fun(...) : couldn't connect to display &quot;localhost:11.0&quot;&#xA;Error : .onLoad failed in 'loadNamespace' for 'tcltk'&#xA;Error: package 'tcltk' could not be loaded&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This seems to be a general problem, and I'm wondering how others have solved it.  Installing an X11 server is not a desirable solution.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2002705" LastEditorUserId="5414452" LastEditDate="2016-01-04T09:29:41.013" LastActivityDate="2016-01-04T09:29:41.013" Title="How to run R on a server without X11, and avoid broken dependencies" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;x11&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="24" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1712316" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2009-11-11T00:56:18.210" Score="0" ViewCount="793" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm getting a weird error when training a glmnet regression.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;invalid class &quot;dgCMatrix&quot; object: length(Dimnames[[2]])' must match Dim[2] &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It only happens occasionally, and perhaps only under larger datasets.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm not sure whether it's consistent it happens given a certain dataset.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any clues?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="86684" LastActivityDate="2011-09-07T03:41:56.227" Title="Strange error when using sparse matrices and glmnet" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;matrix&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1714280" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1715488" CreationDate="2009-11-11T10:19:32.597" Score="48" ViewCount="69615" Body="&lt;p&gt;I want do fit some sort of multi-variate time series model using R. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here is a sample of my data:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;   u     cci     bci     cpi     gdp    dum1 dum2 dum3    dx  &#xA; 16.50   14.00   53.00   45.70   80.63  0   0    1     6.39 &#xA; 17.45   16.00   64.00   46.30   80.90  0   0    0     6.00 &#xA; 18.40   12.00   51.00   47.30   82.40  1   0    0     6.57 &#xA; 19.35   7.00    42.00   48.40   83.38  0   1    0     5.84 &#xA; 20.30   9.00    34.00   49.50   84.38  0   0    1     6.36 &#xA; 20.72   10.00   42.00   50.60   85.17  0   0    0     5.78 &#xA; 21.14   6.00    45.00   51.90   85.60  1   0    0     5.16 &#xA; 21.56   9.00    38.00   52.60   86.14  0   1    0     5.62 &#xA; 21.98   2.00    32.00   53.50   86.23  0   0    1     4.94 &#xA; 22.78   8.00    29.00   53.80   86.24  0   0    0     6.25 &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The data is quarterly, the dummy variables are for seasonality.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What I would like to do is to predict dx with reference to some of the others, while (possibly) allowing for seasonality. For argument's sake, lets say I want to use &quot;u&quot;, &quot;cci&quot; and &quot;gdp&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How would I go about doing this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="141789" LastEditorUserId="163053" LastEditDate="2010-03-05T14:41:01.307" LastActivityDate="2016-04-12T15:42:31.793" Title="Multivariate time series modelling in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;&lt;time-series&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="62" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="1714818" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1714901" CreationDate="2009-11-11T12:14:34.927" Score="2" ViewCount="3516" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to export biometric data from an analysis using the ROCR package.  Here is the code that I've done so far:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;pred = performance(Matching.Score,Distribution)&#xA;perf = prediction(pred,&quot;fnr&quot;, &quot;fpr&quot;)&#xA;&#xA;An object of class “performance”&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;x.name&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[1] &quot;False positive rate&quot;&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;y.name&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[1] &quot;False negative rate&quot;&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;alpha.name&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[1] &quot;Cutoff&quot;&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;x.values&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[[1]]&#xA;&#xA;[1] 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000&#xA;[15] 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000&#xA;  ......&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;y.values&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[[1]]&#xA;&#xA;[1] 1.00000 0.99999 0.99998 0.99997 0.99996 0.99995&#xA;[15] 0.99986 0.99985 0.99984 0.99983 0.99982 0.99981&#xA;    ......&#xA;&#xA;Slot &quot;alpha.values&quot;:&#xA;&#xA;[[1]]&#xA;&#xA;[1]  Inf      1.0427800 1.0221150 1.0056240 1.0032630 0.9999599&#xA;[12] 0.9644779 0.9633058 0.9628996 0.9626501 0.9607665 0.9605930&#xA;    .......&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This results in several Slots.  I would like to export the resulting values into a text file for Excel modification using: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;write(pred, &quot;filename&quot;)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, when I try to write the file, I get an error stating:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in cat(list(...), file, sep, fill, labels, append) : &#xA;  argument 1 (type 'S4') cannot be handled by 'cat'&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there any way around this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'd appreciate any advice.  Thank you! &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Matt Peterson&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="167584" LastE