  <row Id="1791164" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="1791274" CreationDate="2009-11-24T16:22:52.203" Score="2" ViewCount="968" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to normalize a big amount of Affymetrix CEL files using R. However, some of them appear to be truncated, so when reading them i get the error&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Cel file xxx does not seem to have the correct dimensions&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And the normalization stops. Manually removing the corrupted files and restart every time will take very long. Do you know if there is a fast way (in R or with a tool) to detect corrupted files?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PS I'm 99.99% sure I'm normalizing together CELs from the same platform, it's really just truncated files :-)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="209467" LastActivityDate="2009-11-24T16:53:09.727" Title="Fast assessment of corrupted Affymetrix CEL files" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;bioinformatics&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
