  <row Id="10524" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="718366" CreationDate="2008-08-14T00:24:43.320" Score="29" ViewCount="14919" Body="&lt;p&gt;The Entity Framework does not support the &lt;code&gt;Expression.Invoke&lt;/code&gt; operator.  You receive the following exception when trying to use it:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&quot;The LINQ expression node type 'Invoke' is not supported in LINQ to Entities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Has anyone got a workaround for this missing functionality? I would like to use the PredicateBuilder detailed &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.albahari.com/nutshell/predicatebuilder.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in an Entity Framework context.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edit 1&lt;/strong&gt; @marxidad - I like your suggestion, however it does baffle me somewhat. Can you give some further advice on your proposed solution?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edit 2&lt;/strong&gt; @marxidad - Thanks for the clarification.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="708" OwnerDisplayName="Brad" LastEditorUserId="24874" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris Fournier" LastEditDate="2011-01-12T05:55:41.417" LastActivityDate="2011-01-12T05:55:41.417" Title="Expression.Invoke in Entity Framework?" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;linq&gt;&lt;entity-framework&gt;&lt;linq-to-entities&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="11" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="10531" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-14T00:36:01.600" Score="5" ViewCount="1429" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working on some code to paste into the currently active &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenOffice.org&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;OpenOffice&lt;/a&gt; document directly from C#.  I can't include any of the OpenOffice libraries, because we don't want to package them, so we're using reflection to get access to the &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_Network_Objects&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;OpenOffice API&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My question involves using a dispatcher through reflection.  I can't figure out the correct parameters to pass to it, giving me a lovely &quot;TargetInvocationException&quot; due to mismatched types.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;object objframe = GetProperty&amp;lt;object&amp;gt;(objcontroller, &quot;frame&quot;);&#xA;if (objframe != null)&#xA;{&#xA;    object[] paramlist = new object[2] {&quot;.uno:Paste&quot;, objframe};&#xA;    InvokeMethod&amp;lt;object&amp;gt;(objdispatcher, &quot;executeDispatch&quot;, paramlist);&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can I fix it?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="859" OwnerDisplayName="David" LastEditorUserId="63550" LastEditDate="2010-03-15T13:10:15.493" LastActivityDate="2010-03-15T13:12:36.737" Title="Using C# with OpenOffice through reflection" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;reflection&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
