  <row Id="12428" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-15T16:09:37.783" Score="3" ViewCount="181" Body="&lt;p&gt;Once I have my renamed files I need to add them to my project's wiki page. This is a fairly repetitive manual task, so I guess I could script it but I don't know where to start.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The process is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Got to appropriate page on the wiki&#xA;&#xA;for each team member (DeveloperA, DeveloperB, DeveloperC)&#xA;{&#xA;    for each of two files ('*_current.jpg', '*_lastweek.jpg')&#xA;    {&#xA;        Select 'Attach' link on page&#xA;        Select the 'manage' link next to the file to be updated&#xA;        Click 'Browse' button&#xA;        Browse to the relevant file (which has the same name as the previous version)&#xA;        Click 'Upload file' button&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Not necessarily looking for the full solution as I'd like to give it a go myself.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Where to begin? What language could I use to do this and how difficult would it be?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="849" OwnerDisplayName="Klelky" LastEditorUserId="8791568" LastEditDate="2019-08-29T08:29:21.317" LastActivityDate="2019-08-29T08:29:21.317" Title="Automate adding entries to a wiki" Tags="&lt;scripting&gt;&lt;automation&gt;&lt;webautomation&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
