  <row Id="2075327" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-01-15T23:02:58.927" Score="6" ViewCount="2328" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've been trying to dig into what the time-hogs are in some R code I've written, so I'm using &lt;code&gt;Rprof&lt;/code&gt;.  The output isn't yet very helpful though:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; summaryRprof()&#xA;$by.self&#xA;                      self.time self.pct total.time total.pct&#xA;&quot;$&amp;lt;-.data.frame&quot;           2.38     23.2       2.38      23.2&#xA;&quot;FUN&quot;                      2.04     19.9      10.20      99.6&#xA;&quot;[.data.frame&quot;             1.74     17.0       5.54      54.1&#xA;&quot;[.factor&quot;                 1.42     13.9       2.90      28.3&#xA;...&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there some way to dig deeper and find out which specific invocations of &lt;code&gt;$&amp;lt;-.data.frame&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;FUN&lt;/code&gt; (which is probably from &lt;code&gt;by()&lt;/code&gt;), etc. are actually the culprits?  Or will I need to refactor the code and make smaller functional chunks in order to get more fine-grained results?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The only reason I'm resisting refactoring is that I'd have to pass data structures into the functions, and all the passing is by value, so that seems like a step in the wrong direction.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="169947" LastActivityDate="2010-01-18T16:19:02.087" Title="Getting more info from Rprof()" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;profiling&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
