  <row Id="13586" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="13605" CreationDate="2008-08-17T11:12:51.813" Score="5" ViewCount="1139" Body="&lt;p&gt;If there are any language designers out there (or people simply in the know), I'm curious about the methodology behind creating standard libraries for interpreted languages. Specifically, what seems to be the best approach? Defining standard functions/methods in the interpreted language, or performing the processing of those calls in the compiled language in which the interpreter is written?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What got me to thinking about this was the SO question about a stripslashes()-like function in Python. My first thought was &quot;why not define your own and just call it when you need it&quot;, but it raised the question: is it preferable, for such a function, to let the interpreted language handle that overhead, or would it be better to write an extension and leverage the compiled language behind the interpreter?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1344" OwnerDisplayName="Brian Warshaw" LastEditorUserId="578411" LastEditDate="2018-06-19T16:23:59.947" LastActivityDate="2018-06-19T16:23:59.947" Title="Interpreted languages - leveraging the compiled language behind the interpreter" Tags="&lt;performance&gt;&lt;language-agnostic&gt;&lt;language-features&gt;&lt;interpreted-language&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="13589" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="32081" CreationDate="2008-08-17T11:40:38.963" Score="2" ViewCount="5680" Body="&lt;p&gt;I wonder if someone knows if there is a pre-made solution for this: I have a List on an ASP.net Website, and I want that the User is able to re-sort the list through Drag and Drop. Additionally, I would love to have a second list to which the user can drag items from the first list onto.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So far, I found two solutions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The ReorderList from the &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.codeplex.com/AjaxControlToolkit&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Ajax Control Toolkit&lt;/a&gt;, which requires a bit of manual work to make sure changes &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.codeproject.com/KB/ajax/PersistentReorderList.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;are persisted&lt;/a&gt; into the database, and that does not support drag/drop between lists.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.telerik.com/DEMOS/ASPNET/Prometheus/Grid/Examples/Programming/DragAndDrop/DefaultCS.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;RadGrid&lt;/a&gt; from Telerik which does all I want, but is priced far far beyond my Budget.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Does anyone else have some ideas or at least some keywords/pointers to do further investigation on? Espectially the Drag/Drop between two lists is something I am rather clueless about how to do that in ASP.net.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Target Framework is 3.0 by the way.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="91" OwnerDisplayName="Michael Stum" LastActivityDate="2014-12-29T23:48:49.723" Title="ASP.net AJAX Drag/Drop?" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;ajax&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
