  <row Id="2123968" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2124033" CreationDate="2010-01-23T17:21:25.953" Score="13" ViewCount="15397" Body="&lt;p&gt;In python lists can be sliced like this &lt;code&gt;x[4:-1]&lt;/code&gt; to get from the fourth to the last element.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In R something similar can be accomplished for vectors with &lt;code&gt;x[4:length(x)]&lt;/code&gt; and for multidimensional arrays with something like &lt;code&gt;x[,,,,4:dim(x)[5],,,]&lt;/code&gt;.  Is this more elegant syntax for array slicing for a particular dimension from an element in the middle to the last element?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks    &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="198401" LastEditorDisplayName="user8389458" LastEditDate="2018-04-27T10:37:17.080" LastActivityDate="2018-04-27T10:37:17.080" Title="R array manipulation" Tags="&lt;arrays&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;slice&gt;&lt;sub-array&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="13893" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="526939" CreationDate="2008-08-17T20:03:22.600" Score="4" ViewCount="1067" Body="&lt;p&gt;For .net 3.5 SP1, Microsoft have the new client profile which installs only a subset of .net 3.5 SP1 on to Windows XP user's machines.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm aware of how to make my assemblies client-profile ready. And I've read the articles on how to implement an installer for &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc656916.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;ClickOnce&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc656819.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;MSI&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I've been using Inno Setup for my project so far and I'd like to continue to use it (as an Express user, I can't easily make MSIs), I need to know how to use the client-profile installer in a custom environment.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There is &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc656920.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;an article&lt;/a&gt; on a Deployment.xml schema, but no indication of how to write one, package it or anything else. Can someone explain this process? Finding the articles I linked to alone was a painful search experience.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="483" OwnerDisplayName="Nidonocu" LastEditorUserId="50776" LastEditDate="2012-01-10T19:15:33.840" LastActivityDate="2012-01-10T19:15:33.840" Title="How do I make a custom .net client profile installer?" Tags="&lt;deployment&gt;&lt;.net-3.5&gt;&lt;installation&gt;&lt;.net-client-profile&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
