  <row Id="15066" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="15071" CreationDate="2008-08-18T18:41:19.690" Score="5" ViewCount="2879" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a form in C# that has a button that, when clicked, I want the background image to cycle through a set of images (which I have as resources to the project).  The images are named '_1', '_2', etc. and each time I click the button I want its background image to increment to the next one and go back to &quot;_1&quot; when it gets to the highest.  Is there a way to do this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried getting &lt;code&gt;button1.BackgroundImage.ToString()&lt;/code&gt; but that yields &lt;code&gt;System.Drawing.Bitmap&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;Resources._1&lt;/code&gt; like I was thinking it would (in which case I could just get the last character and switch on that to change the background to the appropriate new image).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your help.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="271" OwnerDisplayName="Justin Bennett" LastEditorDisplayName="user2189331" LastEditDate="2008-08-18T21:15:25.370" LastActivityDate="2012-09-30T09:32:51.730" Title="Cycle Button Background Images in C#" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;winforms&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="15087" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-18T19:00:52.133" Score="3" ViewCount="3397" Body="&lt;p&gt;The company I work for has an old Access 2000 application that was using a SQL Server 2000 back-end.  We were tasked with moving the back-end to a SQL Server 2005 database on a new server.  Unfortunately, the application was not functioning correctly while trying to do any inserts or updates.  My research has found many forum posts that Access 2000 -&gt; SQL 2005 is not supported by Microsoft, but I cannot find any Microsoft documentation to verify that.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can anyone either link me to some official documentation, or has anyone used this setup and can confirm that this should be working and our problems lie somewhere else?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Not sure if it matters, but the app is an ADP compiled into an ADE. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1749" OwnerDisplayName="Mikey P" LastEditorUserId="2641576" LastEditorDisplayName="Michał Piaskowski" LastEditDate="2014-11-25T21:06:06.713" LastActivityDate="2014-11-25T21:06:06.713" Title="Access 2000 connecting to SQL Server 2005" Tags="&lt;sql-server&gt;&lt;ms-access&gt;&lt;sql-server-2005&gt;&lt;ms-access-2000&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
