  <row Id="15109" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="15286" CreationDate="2008-08-18T19:24:23.973" Score="4" ViewCount="1361" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a setup project created by Visual Studio 2005, and consists of both a C# .NET 2.0 project and C++ MFC project, and the C++ run time.  It works properly when run from the main console, but when run over a Terminal Server session on a Windows XP target, the install fails in the following way -&#xA;  When the Setup.exe is invoked, it immediately crashes before the first welcome screen is displayed.   When invoked over a physical console, the setup runs normally.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I figured I could go back to a lab machine to debug, but it runs fine on a lab machine over Terminal Server.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I see other descriptions of setup problems over Terminal Server sessions, but I don't see a definite solution.   Both machines have a nearly identical configuration except that the one that is failing also has the GoToMyPC Host installed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Has anyone else seen these problems, and how can I troubleshoot this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1743" OwnerDisplayName="Mike" LastEditorUserId="16587" LastEditorDisplayName="Gortok" LastEditDate="2009-03-09T23:43:06.843" LastActivityDate="2009-03-09T23:43:06.827" Title="Visual Studio 2005 Setup project install crashes over Terminal Server" Tags="&lt;visual-studio&gt;&lt;installation&gt;&lt;projects&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
