  <row Id="15486" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="15494" CreationDate="2008-08-19T01:23:04.340" Score="92" ViewCount="118728" Body="&lt;p&gt;So I came across an interesting problem today. We have a WCF web service that returns an IList. Not really a big deal until I wanted to sort it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Turns out the IList interface doesn't have a sort method built in. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I ended up using the &lt;code&gt;ArrayList.Adapter(list).Sort(new MyComparer())&lt;/code&gt; method to solve the problem but it just seemed a bit &quot;ghetto&quot; to me.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I toyed with writing an extension method, also with inheriting from IList and implementing my own Sort() method as well as casting to a List but none of these seemed overly elegant.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So my question is, does anyone have an elegant solution to sorting an IList&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="493" OwnerDisplayName="lomaxx" LastActivityDate="2020-05-19T12:43:13.500" Title="Sorting an IList in C#" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;generics&gt;&lt;sorting&gt;&lt;ilist&gt;" AnswerCount="15" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="16" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
