  <row Id="16402" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="16416" CreationDate="2008-08-19T15:26:40.287" Score="0" ViewCount="340" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a bunch of files that I need to be able to &lt;em&gt;transport&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;install&lt;/em&gt; quickly. My current method for doing so is moving a flash drive with a readme file of where stuff goes whenever I need to move stuff, which is rather inelegant and cumbersome.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My idea for a solution would be to write up a quick script to move files around that I could just click on. I've done some &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;bash&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; scripting before but &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;batch&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; scripting is a little odd to me. Does anyone have a good online reference guide I could use?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An alternative soulution I could accept would be a program that makes an installer for you, though I'm a bit against that as I would lose a lot of control. However, I'd be alright with it if it was extremely simple,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="652" OwnerDisplayName="Mike Sergio" LastEditorUserId="1773434" LastEditDate="2017-02-10T20:06:02.590" LastActivityDate="2017-02-10T20:06:02.590" Title="Easy installation method for windows/ Batch Reference needed?" Tags="&lt;windows&gt;&lt;batch-file&gt;&lt;installation&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="16403" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="16546" CreationDate="2008-08-19T15:27:31.470" Score="7" ViewCount="3455" Body="&lt;p&gt;One of my biggest typographical frustrations about HTML is the way that it mangles conjoined whitespace.  For example if I have:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;Following punctuation rules.  With two spaces after the period.  &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One of the two spaces following the period will be considered to be insignificant whitespace and be removed.  I can of course, force the whitespace to be significant with: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;Following punctuation rules.&amp;amp;nbsp; With two spaces after the period.  &amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but it just irks me to have to do that and I usually don't bother.  Does anyone out there automatically insert significant whitespace into external content submissions that are intended for a web page?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1948" OwnerDisplayName="Andrew" LastEditorUserId="540162" LastEditDate="2011-09-09T02:35:40.103" LastActivityDate="2012-07-31T16:03:34.743" Title="How do you handle white space in your HTML" Tags="&lt;html&gt;&lt;whitespace&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2012-08-01T16:20:19.077" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
