  <row Id="2349205" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2349320" CreationDate="2010-02-27T22:38:35.130" Score="28" ViewCount="203670" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a data file with this format:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Weight    Industry Type  &#xA;251,787   Kellogg  h  &#xA;253,9601  Kellogg  a  &#xA;256,0758  Kellogg  h  &#xA;....&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I read the data and try to draw an histogram with this commands:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; ce &amp;lt;- read.table(&quot;file.txt&quot;, header = TRUE)&#xA;&#xA; we = ce[,1]&#xA; in = ce[,2]&#xA; ty = ce[,3]&#xA;&#xA;hist(we)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I get this error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Error en hist.default(we) : 'x' must be numeric.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What do I need to do in order to draw histograms for my three variables ?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="157872" LastEditorUserId="680068" LastEditDate="2018-03-21T13:11:53.020" LastActivityDate="2018-03-21T13:13:04.607" Title="Can't draw Histogram, 'x' must be numeric" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;histogram&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="5" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
