 &quot;blah3&quot;, &quot;blah4&quot;, &quot;blah5&quot;, &quot;blah6&quot;, &quot;blah7&quot;, &quot;blah8&quot;, &quot;blah9&quot;)&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;&amp;gt; test_growth_series&#xA;  read_day series_id mean_od sd_od n_in_stat&#xA;1        0      p1s1     0.6  0.10         8&#xA;2        3      p1s1     0.9  0.20         8&#xA;3        9      p1s1     1.3  0.20         8&#xA;4        0      p1s2     0.3  0.10         8&#xA;5        3      p1s2     0.6  0.10         7&#xA;6        9      p1s2     1.0  0.30         5&#xA;7        0      p3s4     0.2  0.04         8&#xA;8        2      p3s4     0.5  0.10         7&#xA;9        8      p3s4     1.2  0.30         2&#xA;&amp;gt; test_growth_series_LUT&#xA;  series_id description&#xA;1      p1s1       blah1&#xA;2      p1s2       blah2&#xA;3      p3s4       blah3&#xA;4      p4s2       blah4&#xA;5      p5s2       blah5&#xA;6      p6s2       blah6&#xA;7      p7s4       blah7&#xA;8      p8s4       blah8&#xA;9      p9s4       blah9&#xA;&amp;gt; &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;this is what I'm trying to achieve:  &#xA;&amp;gt; new_test_growth_series&#xA;  read_day series_id mean_od sd_od n_in_stat        description&#xA;1        0      p1s1     0.6  0.10         8        blah1&#xA;2        3      p1s1     0.9  0.20         8        blah1&#xA;3        9      p1s1     1.3  0.20         8        blah1&#xA;4        0      p1s2     0.3  0.10         8        blah2&#xA;5        3      p1s2     0.6  0.10         7        blah2&#xA;6        9      p1s2     1.0  0.30         5        blah2&#xA;7        0      p3s4     0.2  0.04         8        blah3&#xA;8        2      p3s4     0.5  0.10         7        blah3&#xA;9        8      p3s4     1.2  0.30         2        blah3&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="207258" LastEditorUserId="1195557" LastEditDate="2016-04-11T19:57:07.877" LastActivityDate="2016-04-11T19:57:07.877" Title="How to merge two data.frames together in R, referencing a lookup table" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;merge&gt;&lt;datafra