  <row Id="2373334" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2374018" CreationDate="2010-03-03T17:09:20.757" Score="1" ViewCount="1986" Body="&lt;p&gt;It is very straight-forward to plot a tree using igraph in R&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(igraph)&#xA;plot(graph.tree(20, 2), layout=layout.reingold.tilford)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is it possible to &quot;turn the graph around&quot;, so that the root (node 0) is at the top of the plot? Or, alternatively, is it possible to put the root to middle left?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="216064" LastEditorUserId="216064" LastEditDate="2010-03-10T22:20:07.013" LastActivityDate="2010-03-10T22:20:07.013" Title="How can I draw a tree with igraph &quot;bottom-up&quot;?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;tree&gt;&lt;igraph&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
