  <row Id="17966" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26573" CreationDate="2008-08-20T13:38:53.833" Score="2" ViewCount="2022" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to include a link to my application in the Startup folder with a parameter passed to the program. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think it would work if I created the shortcut locally and then added it to my source. After that I could copy it to the Startup folder on first run.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;File.userDirectory.resolvePath(&quot;Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\startup.lnk&quot;);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, I am trying to get this to occur during install. I see there is are some settings related to the installation in app.xml, but nothing that lets me install it to two folders, or use a parameter.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;!-- The subpath of the standard default installation location to use. Optional. --&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;!-- &amp;lt;installFolder&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/installFolder&amp;gt; --&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&amp;lt;!-- The subpath of the Windows Start/Programs menu to use. Optional. --&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;!-- &amp;lt;programMenuFolder&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/programMenuFolder&amp;gt; --&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="26" OwnerDisplayName="modesty" LastEditorUserId="1215724" LastEditorDisplayName="sparkes" LastEditDate="2015-04-17T18:08:22.183" LastActivityDate="2015-04-17T18:08:22.183" Title="Add a shortcut to Startup folder with parameters in Adobe AIR" Tags="&lt;air&gt;&lt;adobe&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="17980" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="17989" CreationDate="2008-08-20T13:44:34.320" Score="5" ViewCount="3647" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've searched for this a little but I have not gotten a particularly straight answer. In C (and I guess C++), how do you determine what comes after the % when using &lt;code&gt;printf&lt;/code&gt;?. For example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;double radius = 1.0;&#xA;double area = 0.0;&#xA;area = calculateArea( radius );&#xA;printf( &quot;%10.1f     %10.2\n&quot;, radius, area );&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I took this example straight from a book that I have on the C language. This does not make sense to me at all. Where do you come up with &lt;code&gt;10.1f&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;10.2f&lt;/code&gt;? Could someone please explain this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2128" OwnerDisplayName="The.Anti.9" LastEditorUserId="1332690" LastEditDate="2012-04-26T00:34:18.687" LastActivityDate="2016-03-14T16:14:07.730" Title="What Comes After The %?" Tags="&lt;c&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
