  <row Id="2427279" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2430551" CreationDate="2010-03-11T17:41:29.180" Score="7" ViewCount="787" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to write an R function that accepts a formula as its first argument, similar to lm() or glm() and friends.  In this case, it's a function that takes a data frame and writes out a file in &lt;a href=&quot;http://svmlight.joachims.org/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;SVMLight&lt;/a&gt; format, which has this general form:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;line&amp;gt; .=. &amp;lt;target&amp;gt; &amp;lt;feature&amp;gt;:&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; &amp;lt;feature&amp;gt;:&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; ... &amp;lt;feature&amp;gt;:&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; # &amp;lt;info&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;target&amp;gt; .=. +1 | -1 | 0 | &amp;lt;float&amp;gt; &#xA;&amp;lt;feature&amp;gt; .=. &amp;lt;integer&amp;gt; | &quot;qid&quot;&#xA;&amp;lt;value&amp;gt; .=. &amp;lt;float&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;info&amp;gt; .=. &amp;lt;string&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;for example, the following data frame:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  result qid     f1     f2     f3     f4   f5     f6     f7     f8&#xA;1     -1   1 0.0000 0.1253 0.0000 0.1017 0.00 0.0000 0.0000 0.9999&#xA;2     -1   1 0.0098 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000 0.00 0.0316 0.0000 0.3661&#xA;3      1   1 0.0000 0.0000 0.1941 0.0000 0.00 0.0000 0.0509 0.0000&#xA;4     -1   2 0.0000 0.2863 0.0948 0.0000 0.34 0.0000 0.7428 0.0608&#xA;5      1   2 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000 0.4347 0.00 0.0000 0.9539 0.0000&#xA;6      1   2 0.0000 0.7282 0.9087 0.0000 0.00 0.0000 0.0000 0.0355&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;would be represented as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;-1 qid:1 2:0.1253 4:0.1017 8:0.9999&#xA;-1 qid:1 1:0.0098 6:0.0316 8:0.3661&#xA;1  qid:1 3:0.1941 7:0.0509&#xA;-1 qid:2 2:0.2863 3:0.0948 5:0.3400 7:0.7428 8:0.0608&#xA;1  qid:2 4:0.4347 7:0.9539&#xA;1  qid:2 2:0.7282 3:0.9087 8:0.0355&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The function I'd like to write would be called something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;write.svmlight(result ~ f1+f2+f3+f4+f5+f6+f7+f8 | qid, data=mydata, file=&quot;out.txt&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or even&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;write.svmlight(result ~ . | qid, data=mydata, file=&quot;out.txt&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I can't figure out how to use &lt;code&gt;model.matrix()&lt;/code&gt; and/or &lt;code&gt;model.frame()&lt;/code&gt; to know what columns it's supposed to write.  Are these the right things to be looking at?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any help much appreciated!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="169947" LastActivityDate="2012-06-03T23:27:10.120" Title="Extract information from conditional formula" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;formula&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="2427742" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2436738" CreationDate="2010-03-11T18:47:40.707" Score="8" ViewCount="3304" Body="&lt;p&gt;From the &lt;a href=&quot;http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.2.1/geom_bar.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;online bar chart guide&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;qplot(factor(cyl), data=mtcars, geom=&quot;bar&quot;, fill=factor(gear)) &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/T9H6N.png&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/T9H6N.png&quot; alt=&quot;barplot using &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;qplot&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; feature of &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;ggplot2&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do I get 5 to sit on the bottom, 4 above that, and 3 on top?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="264696" LastEditorUserId="1840471" LastEditDate="2016-07-18T00:13:15.983" LastActivityDate="2016-07-18T00:13:15.983" Title="How do I change the stacking order in a bar chart in ggplot2?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="5" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="18010" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="18027" CreationDate="2008-08-20T13:54:31.800" Score="24" ViewCount="7563" Body="&lt;p&gt;I asked a couple of coworkers about &lt;a href=&quot;http://ankhsvn.open.collab.net&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;AnkhSVN&lt;/a&gt; and neither one of them was happy with it. One of them went as far as saying that AnkhSVN has messed up his devenv several times.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What's your experience with AnkhSVN? I really miss having an IDE integrated source control tool.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="781" OwnerDisplayName="Esteban" LastEditorUserId="1332690" LastEditorDisplayName="dbr" LastEditDate="2012-04-25T18:32:59.950" LastActivityDate="2021-02-22T13:20:17.100" Title="Is AnkhSVN any good?" Tags="&lt;version-control&gt;&lt;ankhsvn&gt;" AnswerCount="12" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
