  <row Id="2436502" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2440346" CreationDate="2010-03-12T23:15:30.600" Score="1" ViewCount="7024" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is it possible, in the &lt;code&gt;expr&lt;/code&gt; expression of the &lt;code&gt;with()&lt;/code&gt; function, to access the &lt;code&gt;data&lt;/code&gt; argument directly?  Here's what I mean conceptually:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; print(df)&#xA;  result qid     f1     f2     f3&#xA;1     -1   1 0.0000 0.1253 0.0000&#xA;2     -1   1 0.0098 0.0000 0.0000&#xA;3      1   1 0.0000 0.0000 0.1941&#xA;4     -1   2 0.0000 0.2863 0.0948&#xA;5      1   2 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000&#xA;6      1   2 0.0000 0.7282 0.9087&#xA;&amp;gt; with(df, subset(.data, select=f1:f3))  # Doesn't work&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Of course the above example is kind of silly, but it would be handy for things like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;with(subset(df, f2&amp;gt;0), foo(qid, vars=subset(.data, select=f1:f3)))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried to poke around with &lt;code&gt;environment()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;parent.frame()&lt;/code&gt; etc., but didn't come up with anything that worked.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Maybe this is really a question about &lt;code&gt;eval()&lt;/code&gt;, since that's how &lt;code&gt;with.default()&lt;/code&gt; is implemented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="169947" LastEditorUserId="5414452" LastEditDate="2016-01-20T19:21:46.117" LastActivityDate="2016-01-20T19:21:46.117" Title="Accessing 'data' argument of with() function?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
