  <row Id="18448" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="18484" CreationDate="2008-08-20T17:55:34.247" Score="17" ViewCount="11310" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm looking for a simple way to encrypt my soap communication in my C# Web-Service.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I was looking into &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;amp;ct=res&amp;amp;cd=1&amp;amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.microsoft.com%2Fdownloads%2Fdetails.aspx%3Ffamilyid%3D018a09fd-3a74-43c5-8ec1-8d789091255d&amp;amp;ei=x1isSPTUO4bS0QXsjIzWAw&amp;amp;usg=AFQjCNHn7aOkIXoysM1woIgRBe20Ptu_6g&amp;amp;sig2=RTyvtw71nWYyoDGIEh0TlQ&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;WSE 3.0&lt;/a&gt; but it seems Microsoft dropped support for it, and therefore it's not straightforward to use.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;It seems WCF could've been an option but I prefer not to upgrade from .NET 2.0 .&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any &lt;strong&gt;simple&lt;/strong&gt;, straightforward encryption method?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1256645" OwnerDisplayName="dberlin" LastEditorUserId="305" LastEditorDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditDate="2008-08-31T01:44:37.317" LastActivityDate="2009-04-21T20:00:02.960" Title="Encryption in C# Web-Services" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;web-services&gt;&lt;security&gt;&lt;encryption&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
