  <row Id="18861" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="18884" CreationDate="2008-08-20T21:11:34.853" Score="4" ViewCount="661" Body="&lt;p&gt;So I am writing a registration form and I need the display name to be only numbers, letters and underscores. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Have a look at my code and tell me what I'm doing wrong.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;form method=&quot;post&quot; action=&quot;/&quot; onsubmit=&quot;return check_form()&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;display-name&quot; name=&quot;display-name&quot; maxlength=&quot;255&quot; /&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; /&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;!--&#xA;    var name_regex = /^([a-zA-Z0-9_])+/&#xA;&#xA;    function check_form()&#xA;    {&#xA;        if (!name_regex.test(document.forms[0].elements[0].value))&#xA;        {&#xA;            document.forms[0].elements[0].focus()&#xA;            alert(&quot;Your display name may only contain letters, numbers and underscores&quot;)&#xA;            return false&#xA;        }&#xA;    }&#xA;--&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It's obviously been trimmed down to not include anything not related to the problem but even this snippet doesn't work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="428190" OwnerDisplayName="Andrew G. Johnson" LastEditorUserId="1221792" LastEditDate="2018-05-02T06:37:46.523" LastActivityDate="2018-05-02T06:37:46.523" Title="What did I do wrong here? [Javascript Regex]" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;regex&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
