  <row Id="19409" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="19453" CreationDate="2008-08-21T06:20:08.233" Score="8" ViewCount="8573" Body="&lt;p&gt;This is kinda oddball, but I was poking around with the GNU assembler today (I want to be able to at least read the syntax), and was trying to get this little contrived example of mine to work. Namely I just want to go from 0 to 100, printing out numbers all the while. So a few minutes later I come up with this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;# count.s: print the numbers from 0 to 100. &#xA;    .text&#xA;string: .asciz &quot;%d\n&quot;&#xA;    .globl _main&#xA;&#xA;_main:&#xA;    movl    $0, %eax # The starting point/current value.&#xA;    movl    $100,   %ebx # The ending point.&#xA;&#xA;_loop:&#xA;    # Display the current value.&#xA;    pushl   %eax&#xA;    pushl   $string&#xA;    call     _printf&#xA;    addl     $8, %esp&#xA;&#xA;    # Check against the ending value.&#xA;    cmpl    %eax, %ebx&#xA;    je    _end&#xA;&#xA;    # Increment the current value.&#xA;    incl    %eax&#xA;    jmp _loop   &#xA;&#xA;_end:&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;All I get from this is 3 printed over and over again. Like I said, just a little contrived example, so don't worry too much about it, it's not a life or death problem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(The formatting's a little messed up, but nothing major).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="61" OwnerDisplayName="Bernard" LastEditorUserId="192221" LastEditorDisplayName="Bernard" LastEditDate="2012-05-02T04:21:36.033" LastActivityDate="2012-05-02T04:21:36.033" Title="Incrementing from 0 to 100 in assembly language" Tags="&lt;gnu-assembler&gt;&lt;assembly&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
