  <row Id="2547447" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2552083" CreationDate="2010-03-30T18:02:07.813" Score="48" ViewCount="3384" Body="&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R_%28programming_language%29&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;R&lt;/a&gt; is a statistics programming language.  Part of R is the use of Packages, which themselves are written in the R language.  Programming best practice includes the use of unit-testing to test the functions within these packages while they are being written and when they are used.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am aware of a few packages for unit testing within R, these being&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/RUnit/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;RUnit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/svUnit/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Svunit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/testthat/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Testthat&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm interested to know;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are there any other packages out there ?&#xA;Given peoples experience, do these packages excel at different things ?&#xA;What's the current state of the art in unit testing for R ?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="74658" LastEditorUserId="164901" LastEditDate="2010-04-01T01:59:28.920" LastActivityDate="2016-10-06T05:59:40.970" Title="What is the current state of Unit testing support in the R language" Tags="&lt;unit-testing&gt;&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="13" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
