  <row Id="2553108" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2554412" CreationDate="2010-03-31T13:07:38.237" Score="4" ViewCount="3059" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a dataframe which contains (among other things) a numeric column with a concentration, and a factor column with a status flag.  This status flag contains NA's.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here's an example&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;df&amp;lt;-structure(list(conc = c(101.769, 1.734, 62.944, 92.697, 25.091, 27.377, 24.343, 55.084, 0.335, 23.280), status = structure(c(NA, NA, NA, NA, NA, NA, 2L, NA, 1L, NA), .Label = c(&quot;&amp;lt;LLOQ&quot;, &quot;NR&quot;), class = &quot;factor&quot;)), .Names = c(&quot;conc&quot;, &quot;status&quot;), row.names = c(NA, -10L), class = &quot;data.frame&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to replace the concentration column with a string for some values of the flag column, or with the concentration value formatted to a certain number of significant digits.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I try this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;ifelse(df$status==&quot;NR&quot;,&quot;NR&quot;,df$conc)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The NA's in the status flag don't trigger either the true or false condition (and return NA) - as the documentation suggests it will.  I could loop over the rows and use IF then else on each one but this seems inefficient.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Am I missing something ?  I've tried as.character(df$status) as well which doesn't work.  My mojo must be getting low....&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="74658" LastEditorUserId="5414452" LastEditDate="2016-01-23T11:03:42.320" LastActivityDate="2016-01-23T11:03:42.320" Title="Replace values in a dataframe based on another factor which contains NA's in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
