  <row Id="20674" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="20746" CreationDate="2008-08-21T18:02:04.973" Score="17" ViewCount="16997" Body="&lt;p&gt;Other than &lt;code&gt;self.class.send :method, args...&lt;/code&gt;, of course.  I'd like to make a rather complex method available at both the class and instance level without duplicating the code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPDATE:&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;@Jonathan Branam: that was my assumption, but I wanted to make sure nobody else had found a way around.  Visibility in Ruby is very different from that in Java.  You're also quite right that &lt;code&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; doesn't work on class methods, though this will declare a private class method:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;class Foo&#xA;  class &amp;lt;&amp;lt;self&#xA;    private&#xA;    def bar&#xA;      puts 'bar'&#xA;    end&#xA;  end&#xA;end&#xA;&#xA;Foo.bar&#xA;# =&amp;gt; NoMethodError: private method 'bar' called for Foo:Class&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1190" OwnerDisplayName="Gaius" LastEditorUserId="38765" LastEditDate="2012-03-27T23:37:35.330" LastActivityDate="2019-04-03T02:43:23.053" Title="Is there a way to call a private Class method from an instance in Ruby?" Tags="&lt;ruby&gt;&lt;scope&gt;&lt;visibility&gt;&lt;class-method&gt;&lt;access-specifier&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
