  <row Id="20788" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-21T18:58:51.263" Score="31" ViewCount="20068" Body="&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/20702/whats-youra-good-limit-for-cyclomatic-complexity&quot;&gt;This question&lt;/a&gt; on &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclomatic_complexity&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Cyclomatic Complexity&lt;/a&gt; made me think more about &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Static_code_analysis&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;static code analysis&lt;/a&gt;.  Analyzing code complexity and consistency is occasionally useful, and I'd like to start doing it more.  What tools do you recommend (per language) for such analysis?  &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tools_for_static_code_analysis&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Wikipedia&lt;/a&gt; has a large list of tools, but which ones have people tried before?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edit:&lt;/strong&gt; As David points out, this is not a completely unasked question when it comes to &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2873/choosing-a-static-code-analysis-tool&quot;&gt;C/UNIX based tools&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2134" OwnerDisplayName="Chris Fournier" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:26:29.837" LastActivityDate="2018-12-22T12:25:52.100" Title="What tools do you use for static code analysis?" Tags="&lt;code-analysis&gt;" AnswerCount="13" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="22" ClosedDate="2014-05-19T08:48:21.380" CommunityOwnedDate="2008-12-27T21:02:11.907" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
