  <row Id="2632441" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2632557" CreationDate="2010-04-13T19:08:34.207" Score="6" ViewCount="9249" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am reading, on my own (not for HW) about programming, and one exercise involved programming Pascal's triangle in R.  My first idea was to make a list and then append things to it, but that didn't work too well.  Then I thought of starting with a vector, and making a list out of that, at the end.  Then I thought of making a matrix, and making a list out of that at the end.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Not sure which way to even approach this.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any hints?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="228220" LastEditorUserId="5414452" LastEditDate="2016-01-23T10:41:16.210" LastActivityDate="2016-01-23T10:41:16.210" Title="How would you program Pascal's triangle in R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;math&gt;&lt;combinatorics&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
