  <row Id="2819621" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2820326" CreationDate="2010-05-12T14:18:15.273" Score="0" ViewCount="1025" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to use xts as much as possible in my time series work as it seems to be the suggested way of doing things. However, I have getting a strange error.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;CPI.NSA and INT are xts objects.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(dynlm)&#xA;CPI.NSA.x &amp;lt;- CPI.NSA[dr1]&#xA;INT.x &amp;lt;- INT[dr1]&#xA;&#xA;CPI.NSA.z &amp;lt;- as.zoo(CPI.NSA.x)&#xA;INT.z &amp;lt;- as.zoo(INT.x)&#xA;&#xA;&amp;gt; dynlm(CPI.NSA.z ~ INT.z + L(CPI.NSA.z, 1))&#xA;&#xA;Time series regression with &quot;zoo&quot; data:&#xA;Start = 1953-02-01, End = 1971-06-01&#xA;&#xA;Call:&#xA;dynlm(formula = CPI.NSA.z ~ INT.z + L(CPI.NSA.z, 1))&#xA;&#xA;Coefficients:&#xA;    (Intercept)            INT.z  L(CPI.NSA.z, 1)  &#xA;     -0.0006795        1.0440174       -0.0869050  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&amp;gt; dynlm(CPI.NSA.x ~ INT.x + L(CPI.NSA.x, 1))&#xA;Error in `[.xts`(a, match0(indexes, attr(a, &quot;index&quot;)), , drop = FALSE) : &#xA;  i is out of range&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It was my understanding that whenever I have a function that takes zoo, I can pass it an xts and it should just work, but clearly that is not the case here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What's going on?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the help.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="318976" LastEditorUserId="271616" LastEditDate="2011-08-13T17:51:38.513" LastActivityDate="2011-08-13T17:51:38.513" Title="xts problem with dynlm" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;&lt;xts&gt;&lt;zoo&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
