  <row Id="25914" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-25T12:04:50.540" Score="1" ViewCount="470" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to setup CruiseControl.net webdashboard at the moment. So far it works nice, but I have a problem with the NAnt Build Timing Report.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Firstly, my current &lt;code&gt;ccnet.config&lt;/code&gt; file looks something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;project name=&quot;bla&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;...&#xA;&amp;lt;prebuild&amp;gt;&#xA; &amp;lt;nant .../&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/prebuild&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;tasks&amp;gt;&#xA; &amp;lt;nant .../&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/tasks&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;publishers&amp;gt;&#xA; &amp;lt;nant .../&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/publishers&amp;gt;&#xA;...&#xA;&amp;lt;/project&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As the build completes, NAnt timing report displays three duplicate summaries. Is there a way to fix this without changing the project structure?&#xA;­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1085" OwnerDisplayName="cordis" LastEditorUserId="7750640" LastEditorDisplayName="Prakash" LastEditDate="2017-07-19T17:26:19.790" LastActivityDate="2017-07-19T17:26:19.790" Title="CruiseControl.net duplicate NAnt timings" Tags="&lt;continuous-integration&gt;&lt;cruisecontrol.net&gt;&lt;nant&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="25921" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="25958" CreationDate="2008-08-25T12:14:39.580" Score="8" ViewCount="1107" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've been strictly in a C++ environment for years (and specialized statistical languages). Visual Studio until 2001, and Borland since. Mostly specialized desktop applications for clients. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm not remaining willfully ignorant of it, but over the years when I've dipped into other things, I've spent my time playing around with JavaScript, PHP, and a lot of Python. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASP.NET&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;ASP.NET&lt;/a&gt;&quot; the language? Is C# the language and &quot;ASP.NET&quot; the framework? What's a good answer to &quot;What is ASP.NET&quot;? Is there a correspondence between ASP.NET and anything I'd be familiar with in C++? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I know I can google the same title, but I'd rather see answers from this crowd. (Besides, in the future, I think that Google should point here for questions like that.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1179" OwnerDisplayName="Baltimark" LastEditorUserId="63550" LastEditorDisplayName="Steve M" LastEditDate="2010-02-26T22:20:31.067" LastActivityDate="2011-05-21T14:34:10.010" Title="What is ASP.NET?" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;glossary&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
