t is there, but invisible. I can highlight it and copy/paste it into notepad, where I can see it all -- but in the generated PDF only the first line of the left column of the footer is visible, the rest is invisible. Hence why I added the font color of black in the code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/LHZ96.png&quot; alt=&quot;screenshot of problem&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any ideas on how to correct this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="751" OwnerDisplayName="Adam" LastEditorUserId="1219121" LastEditDate="2012-04-01T09:21:43.570" LastActivityDate="2012-04-01T09:21:43.570" Title="Why is my PDF footer text invisible?" Tags="&lt;pdf&gt;&lt;coldfusion&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="26685" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26693" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:26:39.823" Score="47" ViewCount="108377" Body="&lt;p&gt;I found &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2056/what-are-mvp-and-mvc-and-what-is-the-difference&quot;&gt;What are mvp and mvc and what is the difference&lt;/a&gt; but it didn't really answer this question.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've recently started using MVC because it's part of the framework that myself and my work-partner are going to use. We chose it because it looked easy and separated process from display, are there advantages besides this that we don't know about and could be missing out on?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pros&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Display and Processing are seperated&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Cons&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;None so far&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1384652" OwnerDisplayName="Teifion" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditorDisplayName="Rob Cooper" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T10:31:20.830" LastActivityDate="2016-01-27T00:40:18.710" Title="What is MVC and what are the advantages of it?" Tags="&lt;model-view-controller&gt;&lt;design-patterns&gt;" AnswerCount="11" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="22" ClosedDate="2018-01-11T12:16:21.167" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="26688" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:28:54.810" Score="7" ViewCount="6255" Body="&lt;p&gt;Are there any good PL/SQL libraries for JSON that you've worked with and found useful?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.oracle.com/technology/tech/pl_sql/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;PL/SQL&lt;/a&gt;, I'm having to tediously hand code the return of &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.json.org/&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;JSON&lt;/a&gt; values to JavaScript functions. I found &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.erasme.org/pl-sql-library-for-JSON&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;one PL/SQL library&lt;/a&gt; for auto-generating JSON, but it doesn't do exactly everything I need it too. For example, I couldn't extend the base functions in the library to return a complex tree-like JSON data structure required by a JavaScript tree component I was using.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#xA;The system, which has been in production for 8+ years, was architected to use PL/SQL for the CRUDs and most of the business logic. The PL/SQL also generates 90% of the presentation layer (HTML/JavaScript), using mod PL/SQL. The other 10% is reported data done via Oracle Reports Builder.&#xA;­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerDisplayName="user290" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2020-06-20T09:12:55.060" LastActivityDate="2019-01-18T10:30:48.090" Title="What PL/SQL Libraries For Auto-Generating JSON Do You Recommend?" Tags="&lt;json&gt;&lt;plsql&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2014-12-21T14:58:03.007" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="26706" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26707" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:43:15.960" Score="6" ViewCount="579" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm a bit perplexed by drag and drop in wxPython (but perhaps this questions pertains to drag and drop in other GUI frameworks as well). The frameworks provides a couple of callbacks (OnEnter and OnDragOver) that purportedly allow me to inform the system whether the current mouse position is a valid place to drop whatever it is that is being dragged. From these methods I can return wx.DragNone, wx.DragCopy, etc. What baffles me is that from within these methods I am not allowed to call GetData, which means I am not allowed to examine the data that the user is dragging. If I cannot see the data, how am I supposed to know whether it is OK for the user to drop here?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1785" OwnerDisplayName="landon9720" LastEditorUserId="21632" LastEditorDisplayName="Adam Bellaire" LastEditDate="2008-10-08T17:23:30.857" LastActivityDate="2008-10-08T17:23:30.857" Title="wxpython: How do I examine dragged data in OnDragOver?" Tags="&lt;python&gt;&lt;user-interface&gt;&lt;drag-and-drop&gt;&lt;wxpython&gt;&lt;wxwidgets&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="26711" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26720" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:47:42.830" Score="3" ViewCount="3460" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to re-install a DLL in the GAC, everything seems to work fine but the web application accessing it still seems to be using the old one.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The old DLL is the same version as the new one with only a minor edit, it will be used by 50 different sites so changing the version then changing the reference in the web.config is not a &lt;em&gt;good&lt;/em&gt; solution.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Restarting the IIS server or the worker process isn't an option as there are already 50 sites running that must continue to do so.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;does anyone know what i'm doing wrong or what i can do to remedy this situation?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2847" OwnerDisplayName="John Boker" LastEditorUserId="1215724" LastEditDate="2015-04-17T18:12:03.960" LastActivityDate="2015-04-17T18:12:03.960" Title="Asp.net Reinstalling a DLL into the GAC" Tags="&lt;iis&gt;&lt;dll&gt;&lt;gac&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="26715" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26741" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:50:21.827" Score="12" ViewCount="11213" Body="&lt;p&gt;How does the new Microsoft asp.net mvc implementation handle partitioning your application - for example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;--index.aspx&#xA;--about.aspx&#xA;--contact.aspx&#xA;--/feature1&#xA;--/feature1/subfeature/action&#xA;--/feature2/subfeature/action&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I guess what I am trying to say is that it seems everything has to go into the root of the views/controllers folders which could get unwieldy when working on a project that if built with web forms might have lots and lots of folders and sub-folders to partition the application.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think I get the MVC model and I like the look of it compared to web forms but still getting my head round how you would build a large project in practice.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2041" OwnerDisplayName="john" LastEditorUserId="727208" LastEditorDisplayName="Orion Edwards" LastEditDate="2012-07-13T06:39:55.567" LastActivityDate="2012-07-13T06:39:55.567" Title="asp.net mvc - subfolders" Tags="&lt;asp.net-mvc&gt;&lt;directory-structure&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="26719" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="28915" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:51:31.260" Score="1" ViewCount="1298" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a set of multiple assemblies (one assembly is to be used as an API and it depends on other assemblies). I would like to merge all assemblies into one single assembly but prevent all assemblies except the API one to be visible from the outside.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I will then obfuscate this assembly with Xenocode. From what I have seen, it is impossible to internalize assembly with Xenocode.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have seen ILMerge from Microsoft, but was unable to figure if it can do what I want.&#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;http://research.microsoft.com/~mbarnett/ILMerge.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://research.microsoft.com/~mbarnett/ILMerge.aspx&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1508" OwnerDisplayName="Vincent" LastEditorUserId="49246" LastEditDate="2009-04-25T11:25:06.007" LastActivityDate="2012-06-09T16:43:57.667" Title="Internalize Class and Methods in .NET Assembly" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;vb.net&gt;&lt;assemblies&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="26721" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="27032" CreationDate="2008-08-25T19:52:07.173" Score="2" ViewCount="3012" Body="&lt;p&gt;When creating scrollable user controls with .NET and WinForms I have repeatedly encountered situations where, for example, a vertical scrollbar pops up, overlapping the control's content, causing a horizontal scrollbar to also be needed.  Ideally the content would shrink just a bit to make room for the vertical scrollbar.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My current solution has been to just keep my controls out of the far right 40 pixels or so that the vertical scroll-bar will be taking up.  Since this is still effectively client space for the control, the horizontal scroll-bar still comes up when it gets covered by the vertical scroll-bar, even though no controls are being hidden at all.  But then at least the user doesn't actually need to &lt;strong&gt;use&lt;/strong&gt; the horizontal scrollbar that comes up.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there a better way to make this all work?  Some way to keep the unneeded and unwanted scrollbars from showing up at all?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2729" OwnerDisplayName="Turbulent Intellect" LastEditorUserId="1215724" LastEditDate="2015-04-17T18:10:57.863" LastActivityDate="2015-04-17T18:10:57.863" Title="How can I make sure scrollbars don't overlap content?" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;winforms&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="2889613" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2889795" CreationDate="2010-05-22T20:18:44.180" Score="5" ViewCount="769" Body="&lt;p&gt;As an example, here is a way to get a matrix of all possible outcomes of rolling 4 (fair) dice.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;z &amp;lt;- as.matrix(expand.grid(c(1:6),c(1:6),c(1:6),c(1:6)))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As you may already have understood, I'm trying to work out &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2867456/probability-of-subset-sum-after-rolling-dice-4-times-closed&quot;&gt;a question that was closed&lt;/a&gt;, though, in my opinion, it's a challenging one. I used counting techniques to solve it (I mean by hand) and I finaly arrived to a number of outcomes, with a sum of subset being 5, equal to 1083 out of 1296. That result is consistent with the answers provided to that question, before it was closed. I was wondering how could that subset of outcomes (say z1, where dim(z1) = [1083,4] ) be generated using R. Do you have any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="299077" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:18:35.920" LastActivityDate="2010-05-22T21:16:02.180" Title="How can I find out how many rows of a matrix satisfy a rather complicated criterion (in R)?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;indexing&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;&lt;matrix&gt;&lt;probability&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
