  <row Id="26800" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="26805" CreationDate="2008-08-25T20:32:36.170" Score="12" ViewCount="9285" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm using XPath in .NET to parse an XML document, along the lines of:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;lang-cs prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;XmlNodeList lotsOStuff = doc.SelectNodes(&quot;//stuff&quot;);&#xA;&#xA;foreach (XmlNode stuff in lotsOStuff) {&#xA;   XmlNode stuffChild = stuff.SelectSingleNode(&quot;//stuffChild&quot;);&#xA;   // ... etc&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The issue is that the XPath Query for &lt;code&gt;stuffChild&lt;/code&gt; is always returning the child of the first &lt;code&gt;stuff&lt;/code&gt; element, never the rest. Can XPath not be used to query against an individual &lt;code&gt;XMLElement&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1965" OwnerDisplayName="Jonathan Holland" LastEditorUserId="3641067" LastEditDate="2017-04-28T12:33:36.277" LastActivityDate="2017-04-28T12:33:36.277" Title="XPath and Selecting a single node" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;xpath&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
