  <row Id="27071" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="27326" CreationDate="2008-08-25T22:55:48.213" Score="1" ViewCount="6008" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have an old C library with a function that takes a void**:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;oldFunction(void** pStuff);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to call this function from managed C++ (m_pStuff is a member of the parent ref class of type void*):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;oldFunction( static_cast&amp;lt;sqlite3**&amp;gt;(  &amp;amp;m_pStuff ) );&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This gives me the following error from Visual Studio:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;error C2440: 'static_cast' : cannot convert from 'cli::interior_ptr' to 'void **'&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm guessing the compiler is converting the void* member pointer to a cli::interior_ptr behind my back.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any advice on how to do this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="39040" OwnerDisplayName="Danielb" LastEditorUserId="1136709" LastEditorDisplayName="Josh" LastEditDate="2012-12-04T08:40:01.927" LastActivityDate="2012-12-04T08:40:01.927" Title="Pointer to Pointer Managed C++" Tags="&lt;pointers&gt;&lt;managed-c++&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="2908822" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-05-25T21:55:36.810" Score="203" ViewCount="100666" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a big performance problem in R. I wrote a function that iterates over a &lt;code&gt;data.frame&lt;/code&gt; object. It simply adds a new column to a &lt;code&gt;data.frame&lt;/code&gt; and accumulates something. (simple operation). The &lt;code&gt;data.frame&lt;/code&gt; has roughly 850K rows. My PC is still working (about 10h now) and I have no idea about the runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;dayloop2 &amp;lt;- function(temp){&#xA;    for (i in 1:nrow(temp)){    &#xA;        temp[i,10] &amp;lt;- i&#xA;        if (i &amp;gt; 1) {             &#xA;            if ((temp[i,6] == temp[i-1,6]) &amp;amp; (temp[i,3] == temp[i-1,3])) { &#xA;                temp[i,10] &amp;lt;- temp[i,9] + temp[i-1,10]                    &#xA;            } else {&#xA;                temp[i,10] &amp;lt;- temp[i,9]                                    &#xA;            }&#xA;        } else {&#xA;            temp[i,10] &amp;lt;- temp[i,9]&#xA;        }&#xA;    }&#xA;    names(temp)[names(temp) == &quot;V10&quot;] &amp;lt;- &quot;Kumm.&quot;&#xA;    return(temp)&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any ideas how to speed up this operation?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="350373" LastEditorUserId="5215474" LastEditDate="2018-07-14T19:17:17.783" LastActivityDate="2020-09-13T11:05:57.223" Title="Speed up the loop operation in R" Tags="&lt;performance&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;loops&gt;&lt;rcpp&gt;&lt;r-faq&gt;" AnswerCount="10" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="269" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
