  <row Id="2923092" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="2923190" CreationDate="2010-05-27T16:49:03.300" Score="9" ViewCount="6322" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've got a data frame with far too many rows to be able to do a spatial correlogram. Instead, I want to grab 40 rows for each species and run my correlogram on that subset.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I wrote a function to subset a data frame as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;    samp &amp;lt;- function(dataf)&#xA;{&#xA;    dataf[sample(1:dim(dataf)[1], size=40, replace=FALSE),]&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now I want to apply this function to each species in a larger data frame.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I try something like&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;culled_data = ddply (larger_data, .(species), subset, samp)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I get this error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in subset.data.frame(piece, ...) : &#xA;  'subset' must evaluate to logical&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Anyone got ideas on how to do this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="313163" LastActivityDate="2010-05-29T22:00:05.063" Title="How do I sub sample data by group using ddply?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;plyr&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
