  <row Id="27921" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="27938" CreationDate="2008-08-26T12:47:35.123" Score="23" ViewCount="26463" Body="&lt;p&gt;Story:  The user uploads an image that will be added to a photo gallery.  As part of the upload process, we need to A) store the image on the web server's hard drive and B) store a thumbnail of the image on the web server's hard drive.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Best&quot; here is defined as &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Relatively easy to implement, understand, and maintain&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Results in a thumbnail of reasonable quality&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Performance and high-quality thumbnails are secondary.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="308" OwnerDisplayName="Brad Tutterow" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2008-09-10T00:13:45.233" LastActivityDate="2017-11-30T19:28:27.900" Title="What is the &quot;best&quot; way to create a thumbnail using ASP.NET?" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;image&gt;&lt;thumbnails&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="22" ClosedDate="2017-11-30T19:38:45.880" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="2954008" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-06-01T23:15:58.603" Score="1" ViewCount="496" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have some data that I am trying to plot faceted by its Type with a smooth (Loess, LM, whatever) superimposed.  Generation code is below:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;testFrame &amp;lt;- data.frame(Time=sample(20:60,50,replace=T),Dollars=round(runif(50,0,6)),Type=sample(c(&quot;First&quot;,&quot;Second&quot;,&quot;Third&quot;,&quot;Fourth&quot;),50,replace=T,prob=c(.33,.01,.33,.33)))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have no problem either making a faceted plot, or plotting the smooth, but I cannnot do both.  The first three lines of code below work fine.  The fourth line is where I have trouble:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;qplot(Time,Dollars,data=testFrame,colour=Type)&#xA;qplot(Time,Dollars,data=testFrame,colour=Type) + geom_smooth()&#xA;qplot(Time,Dollars,data=testFrame) + facet_wrap(~Type)&#xA;qplot(Time,Dollars,data=testFrame) + facet_wrap(~Type) + geom_smooth()&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It gives the following error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Error in &lt;code&gt;[&amp;lt;-.data.frame&lt;/code&gt;(&lt;code&gt;*tmp*&lt;/code&gt;, var, value = list(&lt;code&gt;NA&lt;/code&gt; = NULL)) : &#xA;   missing values are not allowed in subscripted assignments of data frames&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What am I missing to overlay a smooth in a faceted plot?  I could have sworn I had done this before, possibly even with the same data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="260533" LastEditorUserId="168747" LastEditDate="2010-06-09T10:34:26.927" LastActivityDate="2010-06-09T10:34:26.927" Title="Smooth Error in qplot from ggplot2" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;smooth&gt;&lt;facet&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
