  <row Id="28301" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="28494" CreationDate="2008-08-26T15:11:27.383" Score="3" ViewCount="893" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm unsure whether the following code would ensure all conditions given in Comparator's Javadoc. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;class TotalOrder&amp;lt;T&amp;gt; implements Comparator&amp;lt;T&amp;gt; {&#xA;&#xA;    public boolean compare(T o1, T o2) {&#xA;        if (o1 == o2 || equal(o1, o2)) return 0;&#xA;&#xA;        int h1 = System.identityHashCode(o1);&#xA;        int h2 = System.identityHashCode(o2);&#xA;&#xA;        if (h1 != h2) {&#xA;            return h1 &amp;lt; h2 ? -1 : 1;&#xA;        }&#xA;&#xA;        // equals returned false but identity hash code was same, assume o1 == o2&#xA;        return 0;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    boolean equal(Object o1, Object o2) {&#xA;        return o1 == null ? o2 == null : o1.equals(o2);&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Will the code above impose a total ordering on all instances of any class, even if that class does not implement Comparable?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3071" OwnerDisplayName="Cagatay" LastActivityDate="2013-05-18T01:24:35.683" Title="Impose a total ordering on all instances of *any* class in Java" Tags="&lt;java&gt;&lt;algorithm&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
