  <row Id="3003527" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3003657" CreationDate="2010-06-09T06:28:57.917" Score="6" ViewCount="3429" Body="&lt;p&gt;As in the example, I am trying to &lt;code&gt;substring&lt;/code&gt; the Video_full column in a &lt;code&gt;data.frame&lt;/code&gt; (video_data_2) I am working on. I want to keep all the characters after the period. The period is always present, there is only one period and it is in a different position in each value for the column. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;     Date                     Video_full      Instances   &#xA;1 Apr 1, 2010  installs/AA.intro_video_1      546         &#xA;2 Apr 1, 2010  installs/ABAC.intro_video_2    548      &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I got substring to work:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;video_data_2$Video_full &amp;lt;- substring(video_data_2$Video_full,11)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And &lt;code&gt;strsplit&lt;/code&gt; also:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;strsplit(&quot;installs/AA.intro_video_1 &quot;,'[.]')&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm just not able to figure out how to start the &lt;code&gt;substring&lt;/code&gt; in a dynamic position or only keep the second value returned by &lt;code&gt;strsplit&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks for any help you can offer for a simple question. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="302274" LastEditorUserId="168747" LastEditDate="2010-09-14T08:45:32.740" LastActivityDate="2010-09-14T08:45:32.740" Title="How do I specify a dynamic position for the start of substring?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
