  <row Id="3063243" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3063367" CreationDate="2010-06-17T15:41:13.563" Score="2" ViewCount="607" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a series of value that include the empty string&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;levels(mydata$phone_partner_products)&#xA;    &quot;&quot;                     &quot;dont_know&quot;            &quot;maybe_interesting&quot;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;    &quot;not_interesting&quot;      &quot;very_interesting&quot;     &quot;very_not_interesting&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If I make a frequencies table I get this&#xA;table(mydata$phone_partner_products)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;                            dont_know    maybe_interesting &#xA;            3752                  226                 2907 &#xA; not_interesting     very_interesting very_not_interesting &#xA;            1404                 1653                 1065&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can I reorder the columns in a more meaningful way?&#xA;How can I rename the empty string &quot;&quot; level?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you a lot in advance.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1264096" LastActivityDate="2010-06-18T18:48:42.307" Title="R table column order when including the empty string" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
