  <row Id="29760" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="29772" CreationDate="2008-08-27T08:52:35.087" Score="2" ViewCount="2045" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've got a problem here with an MSI deployment that I'm working on (using &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InstallShield&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;InstallShield&lt;/a&gt;). We have a program running in the background that needs to run per-user, and it needs to start automatically without user intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem is with &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_Policy#Operation&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Group Policy Object&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Active_Directory&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Active Directory&lt;/a&gt; (GPO/AD) deployment the application is started in the SYSTEM context before anyone is logged in rather than as the user who is about to log in. The application can only run once per user, and it seems that the SYSTEM process prevents the USER process from starting. This means the PCs need to be rebooted twice before the software can be deployed to the users. How do we to stop this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Basically the current workflow is: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Installation/upgrade runs... kill background application&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Install new files&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Startup background application&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This works for published applications and interactive &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Installer&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;MSI&lt;/a&gt; installations - it's only 'assigned' applications that seem to have the problem. As step 3 happens in the SYSTEM context rather than the user context :(&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Ideally, I'd have the development team patch the EXE file to prevent launching in the SYSTEM context, but that's a release cycle away, and I'm looking for an installer-based solution for the interim.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(I don't know Installscript... So I'm guessing &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VBScript&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;VBScript&lt;/a&gt; is probably the way to go if there's no native InstallShield stuff I can use.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="592" OwnerDisplayName="sascha" LastEditorUserId="63550" LastEditorDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditDate="2013-06-21T11:43:52.620" LastActivityDate="2014-07-18T18:50:13.393" Title="Stopping MSI from launching an EXE in the SYSTEM context" Tags="&lt;installation&gt;&lt;windows-installer&gt;&lt;installshield&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="3073746" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3073898" CreationDate="2010-06-18T23:53:42.900" Score="1" ViewCount="3968" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm getting a strange error when I run the following function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;TypeIDs=c(18283,18284,17119,17121,17123,17125,17127,17129,17131,17133,18367,18369,18371,18373,18375,18377,18379)&#xA;&#xA;featsave&amp;lt;-function(featfile,TypeIDs=TypeIDs) {&#xA;    mydata1&amp;lt;-read.table(featfile,header=TRUE)&#xA;    mydata2&amp;lt;-subset(mydata1,TypeID %in% TypeIDs)&#xA;&#xA;    mydata&amp;lt;-as.data.frame(cast(mydata2, Feat1 + Feat2 + ID ~ TypeID,value=&quot;value&quot;))&#xA;    save(mydata,file=&quot;mydatafile.Rdata&quot;,compress=TRUE)&#xA;    return(mydata)&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;with the following data:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Feat1   Feat2   ID  Feat3   Feat4   TypeID  value&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 18283   280.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 18284   20.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 18285   0.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17116   0.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17117   0.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17118   0.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17119   68.75&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17120   0.00&#xA;1   1   1   6   266 17121   1.26&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The error I get is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in inherits(x, &quot;factor&quot;) : &#xA;  promise already under evaluation: recursive default argument reference or earlier problems?&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This error occurs on the &lt;code&gt;mydata2&lt;/code&gt; line where I take a subset of the data. I can't seem to debug it because if I instead run each line of the function in the interpreter, I no longer get the error. What gives?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="208704" LastActivityDate="2010-06-19T00:50:18.373" Title="R error promise already under evaluation when using subset in function but no error in script" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;subset&gt;&lt;d