  <row Id="30302" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="30551" CreationDate="2008-08-27T14:38:39.327" Score="12" ViewCount="10470" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to ignore multiple wildcard routes.  With asp.net mvc preview 4, they ship with:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;RouteTable.Routes.IgnoreRoute(&quot;{resource}.axd/{*pathInfo}&quot;);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'd also like to add something like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;RouteTable.Routes.IgnoreRoute(&quot;Content/{*pathInfo}&quot;);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but that seems to break some of the helpers that generate urls in my program.  Thoughts?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3085" OwnerDisplayName="Jim Geurts" LastEditorUserId="9020340" LastEditDate="2019-04-25T11:44:46.430" LastActivityDate="2019-04-25T11:44:46.430" Title="Asp.Net Routing: How do I ignore multiple wildcard routes?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;asp.net-mvc&gt;&lt;routing&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="30307" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="30313" CreationDate="2008-08-27T14:40:38.853" Score="-1" ViewCount="1351" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm doing some PHP stuff on an Ubuntu server.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The path I'm working in is &lt;strong&gt;/mnt/dev-windows-data/Staging/mbiek/test_list&lt;/strong&gt; but the PHP call &lt;code&gt;getcwd()&lt;/code&gt; is returning &lt;strong&gt;/mnt/dev-windows/Staging/mbiek/test_list&lt;/strong&gt; (notice how it's dev-windows instead of dev-windows-data).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There aren't any symbolic links anywhere. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are there any other causes for &lt;code&gt;getcwd()&lt;/code&gt; returning a different path from a local &lt;code&gt;pwd&lt;/code&gt; call?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Edit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I figured it out.  The &lt;strong&gt;DOCUMENT_ROOT&lt;/strong&gt; in PHP is set to &lt;strong&gt;/mnt/dev-windows&lt;/strong&gt; which throws everything off.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="305" OwnerDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditorUserId="567854" LastEditorDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditDate="2019-01-18T11:14:08.100" LastActivityDate="2019-01-18T11:14:08.100" Title="Why would getcwd() return a different directory than a local pwd?" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;directory&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
