  <row Id="31708" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="31710" CreationDate="2008-08-28T05:21:26.943" Score="17" ViewCount="54338" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am using LINQ to query a generic dictionary and then use the result as the datasource for my ListView (WebForms).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Simplified code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Dictionary&amp;lt;Guid, Record&amp;gt; dict = GetAllRecords();&#xA;myListView.DataSource = dict.Values.Where(rec =&amp;gt; rec.Name == &quot;foo&quot;);&#xA;myListView.DataBind();&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I thought that would work but in fact it throws a &lt;strong&gt;System.InvalidOperationException&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;ListView with id 'myListView' must&#xA;  have a data source that either&#xA;  implements ICollection or can perform&#xA;  data source paging if AllowPaging is&#xA;  true.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In order to get it working I have had to resort to the following:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Dictionary&amp;lt;Guid, Record&amp;gt; dict = GetAllRecords();&#xA;List&amp;lt;Record&amp;gt; searchResults = new List&amp;lt;Record&amp;gt;();&#xA;&#xA;var matches = dict.Values.Where(rec =&amp;gt; rec.Name == &quot;foo&quot;);&#xA;foreach (Record rec in matches)&#xA;    searchResults.Add(rec);&#xA;&#xA;myListView.DataSource = searchResults;&#xA;myListView.DataBind();&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there a small gotcha in the first example to make it work?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Wasn't sure what to use as the question title for this one, feel free to edit to something more appropriate)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="202" OwnerDisplayName="Christian Hagelid" LastEditorUserId="1414" LastEditorDisplayName="travis" LastEditDate="2008-08-28T05:23:24.957" LastActivityDate="2016-08-08T11:30:34.143" Title="How can I convert IEnumerable&lt;T&gt; to List&lt;T&gt; in C#?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;linq&gt;&lt