  <row Id="3171426" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3172398" CreationDate="2010-07-03T12:04:25.867" Score="190" ViewCount="389337" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have the following 2 data.frames:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;a1 &amp;lt;- data.frame(a = 1:5, b=letters[1:5])&#xA;a2 &amp;lt;- data.frame(a = 1:3, b=letters[1:3])&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to find the row a1 has that a2 doesn't.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there a built in function for this type of operation?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(p.s: I did write a solution for it, I am simply curious if someone already made a more crafted code)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here is my solution:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;a1 &amp;lt;- data.frame(a = 1:5, b=letters[1:5])&#xA;a2 &amp;lt;- data.frame(a = 1:3, b=letters[1:3])&#xA;&#xA;rows.in.a1.that.are.not.in.a2  &amp;lt;- function(a1,a2)&#xA;{&#xA;    a1.vec &amp;lt;- apply(a1, 1, paste, collapse = &quot;&quot;)&#xA;    a2.vec &amp;lt;- apply(a2, 1, paste, collapse = &quot;&quot;)&#xA;    a1.without.a2.rows &amp;lt;- a1[!a1.vec %in% a2.vec,]&#xA;    return(a1.without.a2.rows)&#xA;}&#xA;rows.in.a1.that.are.not.in.a2(a1,a2)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="256662" LastActivityDate="2021-06-22T13:02:46.283" Title="Compare two data.frames to find the rows in data.frame 1 that are not present in data.frame 2" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;merge&gt;&lt;compare&gt;&lt;rows&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="14" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="94" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="31794" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="31796" CreationDate="2008-08-28T07:31:48.580" Score="6" ViewCount="2639" Body="&lt;p&gt;In .net frameworks 1.1, I use &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Configuration.ConfigurationSettings.AppSettings[&quot;name&quot;];&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;for application settings.  But in .Net 2.0, it says ConfigurationSettings is obsolete and to use ConfigurationManager instead. So I swapped it out with this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager.AppSettings[&quot;name&quot;];&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem is, ConfigurationManager was not found in the System.Configuration namespace.  I've been banging my head against the wall trying to figure out what I'm doing wrong.  Anybody got any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2121" OwnerDisplayName="sandats522" LastEditorUserId="905" LastEditorDisplayName="Keith" LastEditDate="2008-08-28T09:15:50.267" LastActivityDate="2009-03-09T17:46:54.703" Title="Help accessing application settings using ConfigurationManager" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;.net-2.0&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
