  <row Id="3212540" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3212852" CreationDate="2010-07-09T12:28:50.637" Score="6" ViewCount="361" Body="&lt;p&gt;When debugging a function I usually use &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(debug)&#xA;mtrace(FunctionName)&#xA;FunctionName(...)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And that works quite well for me.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, sometimes I am trying to debug a complex function that I don't know.  In which case, I can find that inside that function there is another function that I would like to &quot;go into&quot; (&quot;debug&quot;) - so to better understand how the entire process works.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So one way of doing it would be to do:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(debug)&#xA;mtrace(FunctionName)&#xA;FunctionName(...)&#xA;# when finding a function I want to debug inside the function, run again:&#xA;mtrace(FunctionName.SubFunction)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The question is - &lt;strong&gt;is there a better/smarter way to do interactive debugging (as I have described) that I might be missing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;p.s: I am aware that there where various questions asked on the subject on SO (see &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=[r]+debugging&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;).  Yet I wasn't able to come across a similar question/solution to what I asked here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="256662" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T11:55:16.640" LastActivityDate="2010-07-16T05:49:18.853" Title="Recommendations for &quot;Dynamic/interactive&quot; debugging of functions in R?" Tags="&lt;debugging&gt;&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3215783" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3215843" CreationDate="2010-07-09T19:08:48.063" Score="4" ViewCount="4387" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to parse the XML file in R, so that I can analysis the data. I am trying to get the mean and standard deviation of the price. Also I would like to be able to get the rate of change in the time of the share price changing. I have tried entering the data by hand but am having problems with the date structure ( I have tried the following: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;z &amp;lt;- strptime (&quot;HH:MM:SS.ms, &quot;%H:%m:%S.%f&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but it failed to work). I know the XML file only has a small few numbers but is it a process that could be automated and if so what packages would I need? (I am new to R). Any help would be much appreciated.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&#xA;Anthony.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;?xml version = &quot;1.0&quot;?&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Company &amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:01&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  25.02&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:02&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  15&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:025&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  15.02&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:031&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  18.25&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:039&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  18.54&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:00:050&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt; 16.52&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;   &amp;lt;shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;timeStamp&amp;gt; 12:00:01:01&amp;lt;/timeStamp&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;Price&amp;gt;  17.50&amp;lt;/Price&amp;gt;&#xA;   &amp;lt;/shareprice&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/Company&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="386448" LastActivityDate="2010-07-09T20:01:00.143" Title="How would I parse the XML file in R and carry out basic Statistics Analysis on the data" Tags="&lt;xml&gt;&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="6" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
