  <row Id="3301078" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4604358" CreationDate="2010-07-21T15:37:17.097" Score="2" ViewCount="198" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've been working on code to create a parallel lapply() type function that uses Amazon's Elastic Map Reduce engine as the 'grid' for processing (yes, it's a mapper with no reducer). After I get the code stable I'll abstract it as a foreach backend. But first I need to build tests to test the code I have. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What would be some good test cases for this function? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My canonical test case right now is the following:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;myList &amp;lt;- NULL&#xA;set.seed(1)&#xA;for (i in 1:10){&#xA;  a &amp;lt;- c(rnorm(999), NA)&#xA;  myList[[i]] &amp;lt;- a&#xA;}&#xA;outputLocal &amp;lt;- lapply(myList, mean, na.rm=T)&#xA;outputEmr   &amp;lt;- emrlapply(myList, mean, myCluster, na.rm=T)&#xA;all.equal(outputEmr, outputLocal) &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This test case makes sure the optional argument &lt;code&gt;na.rm=T&lt;/code&gt; is passed properly to the remote machines. What are some other test cases that I could be using? I don't currently support &lt;code&gt;simplify&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;USE.NAMES&lt;/code&gt; arguments, although I will in the future. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="37751" LastActivityDate="2011-01-05T13:10:55.937" Title="R: Creating lapply() type test cases" Tags="&lt;testing&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;lapply&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
