  <row Id="35103" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="35116" CreationDate="2008-08-29T19:27:18.667" Score="9" ViewCount="1358" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to bind a configuration file to my executable. I'd like to do this by storing an MD5 hash of the file inside the executable. This should keep anyone but the executable from modifying the file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Essentially if someone modifies this file outside of the program the program should fail to load it again.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;EDIT: The program processes credit card information so being able to change the configuration in any way could be a potential security risk. This software will be distributed to a large number of clients. Ideally client should have a configuration that is tied directly to the executable. This will hopefully keep a hacker from being able to get a fake configuration into place.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The configuration still needs to be editable though so compiling an individual copy for each customer is not an option.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It's important that this be dynamic. So that I can tie the hash to the configuration file as the configuration changes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2191" OwnerDisplayName="Mykroft" LastEditorUserId="102937" LastEditorDisplayName="Mykroft" LastEditDate="2011-11-18T03:08:09.310" LastActivityDate="2011-11-18T03:08:09.310" Title="How do I store information in my executable in .Net" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="3340582" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3341445" CreationDate="2010-07-27T03:35:56.677" Score="6" ViewCount="2290" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am attempting to bin time-series data from several years of observation by month using the &lt;code&gt;stat_bin&lt;/code&gt; function in &lt;code&gt;ggplot2&lt;/code&gt;.  The code looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;month.breaks&amp;lt;-seq.Date(from=min(afg$DateOccurred),to=max(afg$DateOccurred),by=&quot;month&quot;)  # All months, for breaks&#xA;report.region&amp;lt;-ggplot(afg,aes(x=DateOccurred))+stat_bin(aes(y=..density..,fill=Type),breaks=month.breaks)+facet_wrap(~Region)&#xA;print(report.region)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I run print, however, I get the following error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in `+.Date`(left, right) : binary + is not defined for Date objects&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If I am reading this correctly, the plus operator is not defined for &lt;code&gt;Date&lt;/code&gt; objects and thus it is not possible to perform this type of binning?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="144537" LastActivityDate="2017-03-16T04:21:18.763" Title="Using seq.Date as breaks in stat_bin for time-series" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
