  <row Id="3411201" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3411222" CreationDate="2010-08-05T01:50:14.397" Score="40" ViewCount="39378" Body="&lt;p&gt;Let's say I have a data.frame, like so: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- c(1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10,1:10)&#xA;df &amp;lt;- data.frame(&quot;Label 1&quot;=x,&quot;Label 2&quot;=rnorm(100))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;head(df,3)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;returns:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  Label.1    Label.2&#xA;1       1  1.9825458&#xA;2       2 -0.4515584&#xA;3       3  0.6397516&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do I get R to stop automagically replacing the space with a period in the column name? ie, &quot;Label 1&quot; instead of &quot;Label.1&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170352" LastEditorUserId="202229" LastEditDate="2018-06-27T00:34:57.623" LastActivityDate="2021-06-26T16:49:09.923" Title="Specifying column names in a data.frame changes spaces to &quot;.&quot;" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;&lt;names&gt;&lt;illegal-characters&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
