  <row Id="37067" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="37314" CreationDate="2008-08-31T20:13:52.673" Score="4" ViewCount="732" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've created a model for executing worker tasks in a server application using a thread pool associated with an IO completion port such as shown in the posts below:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://weblogs.asp.net/kennykerr/archive/2008/01/03/parallel-programming-with-c-part-4-i-o-completion-ports.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://weblogs.asp.net/kennykerr/archive/2008/01/03/parallel-programming-with-c-part-4-i-o-completion-ports.aspx&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogs.msdn.com/larryosterman/archive/2004/03/29/101329.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://blogs.msdn.com/larryosterman/archive/2004/03/29/101329.aspx&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are there any classes in boost that can help with this programming model?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3146" OwnerDisplayName="1800 INFORMATION" LastActivityDate="2010-10-04T11:16:31.120" Title="Task oriented thread pooling" Tags="&lt;c++&gt;&lt;multithreading&gt;&lt;boost&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="37069" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="37111" CreationDate="2008-08-31T20:18:13.833" Score="12" ViewCount="22585" Body="&lt;p&gt;On Mac OS X 10.5 I downloaded the latest version of Apache 2.2.9. After the usual configure, make, make install dance I had a build of apache without mod_rewrite. This wasn't statically linked and the module was not built in the /modules folder either.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I had to do the following to build Apache and mod_rewrite:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;./configure --prefix=/usr/local/apache2 --enable-rewrite=shared&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Is there a way to tell Apache to build all modules as Shared Modules (DSOs) so I can control loading from the Apache config?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Now that I have built Apache and the mod_rewrite DSO, how can I build another shared module without building all of Apache?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(The last time I built Apache (2.2.8) on Solaris, by default it built everything as a shared module.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="636" OwnerDisplayName="BrianLy" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2008-09-03T16:12:59.763" LastActivityDate="2012-02-01T11:18:57.030" Title="Apache - how do I build individual and/or all modules as shared modules" Tags="&lt;apache&gt;&lt;unix&gt;&lt;configuration&gt;&lt;mod-rewrite&gt;&lt;build&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="5" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="37070" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="37092" CreationDate="2008-08-31T20:18:34.113" Score="142" ViewCount="43062" Body="&lt;p&gt;This is a somewhat low-level question.  In x86 assembly there are two SSE instructions: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;MOVDQA &lt;i&gt;&lt;em&gt;xmmi, m128&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;MOVNTDQA &lt;i&gt;&lt;em&gt;xmmi, m128&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The IA-32 Software Developer's Manual says that the &lt;em&gt;NT&lt;/em&gt; in MOVNTDQA stands for &lt;em&gt;Non-Temporal&lt;/em&gt;, and that otherwise it's the same as MOVDQA.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My question is, what does &lt;em&gt;Non-Temporal&lt;/em&gt; mean?  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1084" OwnerDisplayName="Nathan Fellman" LastEditorUserId="192221" LastEditorDisplayName="SoapBox" LastEditDate="2012-05-02T11:10:05.043" LastActivityDate="2018-11-08T23:12:05.790" Title="What is the meaning of &quot;non temporal&quot; memory accesses in x86" Tags="&lt;x86&gt;&lt;sse&gt;&lt;assembly&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="4" FavoriteCount="48" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
