  <row Id="3443687" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="12135122" CreationDate="2010-08-09T19:57:41.317" Score="325" ViewCount="719584" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a number, for example 1.128347132904321674821 that I would like to show as only two decimal places when output to screen (or written to a file). How does one do that? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- 1.128347132904321674821&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;EDIT: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The use of: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;options(digits=2)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Has been suggested as a possible answer. Is there a way to specify this within a script for one-time use? When I add it to my script it doesn't seem to do anything different and I'm not interested in a lot of re-typing to format each number (I'm automating a very large report). &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;-- &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Answer: round(x, digits=2)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170352" LastEditorUserId="903061" LastEditDate="2019-09-17T19:23:33.297" LastActivityDate="2021-12-14T02:25:38.313" Title="Formatting Decimal places in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;formatting&gt;&lt;rounding&gt;&lt;r-faq&gt;" AnswerCount="14" CommentCount="6" FavoriteCount="110" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
