  <row Id="3459867" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-08-11T15:12:46.853" Score="4" ViewCount="4429" Body="&lt;p&gt;Say, I am using &lt;code&gt;facet_grid()&lt;/code&gt; in ggplot2 to obtain 2 histograms. Now I want to superimpose these histograms with Poisson curves (having different means for the 2 histogram plots/grids) and a second curve of another distribution (for which I want to manually provide the probability function of values). How can this be done? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Constructing an example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(ggplot2)&#xA;&#xA;value&amp;lt;-c(rpois(500,1.5))&#xA;&#xA;group&amp;lt;-rep(c(&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;),250)&#xA;&#xA;data&amp;lt;-data.frame(value,group)&#xA;&#xA;g1&amp;lt;-ggplot(data,aes(value))&#xA;&#xA;g1+geom_histogram(aes(y=..count..),binwidth=1,position=&quot;identity&quot;)+facet_grid(.~group)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What next?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Alternatively, can it be done using the lattice package?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="417405" LastEditorUserId="250259" LastEditDate="2012-07-25T14:29:42.720" LastActivityDate="2012-07-25T14:29:42.720" Title="How to superimpose distribution curves on histograms using ggplot2 and lattice" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;&lt;lattice&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
