  <row Id="38345" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="71895" CreationDate="2008-09-01T19:59:37.287" Score="27" ViewCount="11166" Body="&lt;p&gt;I recently &quot;needed&quot; a zip function in Perl 5 (while I was thinking about &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/11/how-do-i-calculate-relative-time&quot;&gt;How do I calculate relative time?&lt;/a&gt;), i.e. a function that takes two lists and &quot;zips&quot; them together to one list, interleaving the elements.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Pseudo)example: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;@a=(1, 2, 3);&#xA;@b=('apple', 'orange', 'grape');&#xA;zip @a, @b; # (1, 'apple', 2, 'orange', 3, 'grape');&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.haskell.org/onlinereport/standard-prelude.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Haskell has zip in the Prelude&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;http://ferreira.nfshost.com/perl6/zip.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Perl 6 has a zip operator&lt;/a&gt; built in, but how do you do it in an elegant way in Perl 5?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2905" OwnerDisplayName="asjo" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditorDisplayName="Rich B" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:09:24.100" LastActivityDate="2015-02-02T20:29:26.463" Title="Is there an elegant zip to interleave two lists in Perl 5?" Tags="&lt;perl&gt;&lt;zip&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="13" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
