  <row Id="38370" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="38924" CreationDate="2008-09-01T20:17:28.443" Score="6" ViewCount="3566" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've to admin a small website for my alumni group which is hosted by my ISV. The url is something like www.myIsv.com/myWebSite/ which is quite ugly and very forgetable. The main admin of the webserver has registered a domain name www.mysmallwebsite.com and put a index.html with this content:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;www.mysmallwebsite.com&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&amp;lt;frameset&amp;gt;&#xA;   &amp;lt;frame src=&quot;http://www.myIsv.com/myWebSite/&quot; name=&quot;redir&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;      &amp;lt;noframes&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Original location:&#xA;          &amp;lt;a href=&quot;www.myIsv.com/myWebSite/&quot;&amp;gt;http://www.myIsv.com/myWebSite/&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&#xA;      &amp;lt;/noframes&amp;gt;&#xA; &amp;lt;/frameset&amp;gt;  &#xA;&amp;lt;/html&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It works fine, but some features like PHP Session variables doesn't work anymore! Anyone has a suggestion for correcting that?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit:&#xA;This doesn't work both on IE and on Firefox (no plugins)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1578" OwnerDisplayName="Steve Gury" LastEditorUserId="4248328" LastEditorDisplayName="Steve Gury" LastEditDate="2015-06-05T17:16:14.680" LastActivityDate="2015-06-05T17:16:14.680" Title="PHP : session variable aren't usable when site is redirected" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;session&gt;&lt;session-variables&gt;" AnswerCount="10" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="3466599" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3474049" CreationDate="2010-08-12T10:10:16.210" Score="8" ViewCount="566" Body="&lt;p&gt;How would a person &lt;code&gt;dput()&lt;/code&gt; an S4 object? I tried this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;require(sp)&#xA;require(splancs)&#xA;plot(0, 0, xlim = c(-100, 100), ylim = c(-100, 100))&#xA;poly.d &amp;lt;- getpoly() #draw a pretty polygon - PRETTY!&#xA;poly.d &amp;lt;- rbind(poly.d, poly.d[1,]) # close the polygon because of Polygons() and its kin&#xA;poly.d &amp;lt;- SpatialPolygons(list(Polygons(list(Polygon(poly.d)), ID = 1)))&#xA;poly.d&#xA;dput(poly.d)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Notice that if I &lt;code&gt;dput()&lt;/code&gt; an S4 object, I cannot reconstruct it again. Your thoughts?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="322912" LastEditorUserId="636656" LastEditDate="2012-10-03T19:28:32.997" LastActivityDate="2012-10-03T19:28:32.997" Title="dputting an S4 object" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;s4&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
