  <row Id="39254" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="39645" CreationDate="2008-09-02T11:22:31.733" Score="7" ViewCount="5656" Body="&lt;p&gt;When looking at a SSI printenv dump I see a variable URI_REQUEST.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When reading the Apache mod_include docs I see DOCUMENT_URI which they define as &quot;The (%-decoded) URL path of the document requested by the user.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Anyone know the difference between the two?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;TIA.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2974" OwnerDisplayName="robwells57" LastEditorUserId="2974" LastEditorDisplayName="spider57" LastEditDate="2008-09-20T01:19:13.983" LastActivityDate="2008-09-20T01:19:13.983" Title="What's the difference between DOCUMENT_URI and URI_REQUEST in SSI?" Tags="&lt;apache&gt;&lt;ssi&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
