  <row Id="3574114" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3574473" CreationDate="2010-08-26T10:15:00.010" Score="5" ViewCount="7146" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am using the following code for the Share Price Application I have been developing (with plenty of help from people here that is greatly appreciated!). One of the things it should do is allow the user to pick a company to analyse from stored XML Files, I have been using the following code to do this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;df &amp;lt;- xmlToDataFrame(file.choose())&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Instead of using file.choose () {as apparently the dialogue box reveals to much of the system structure}, it has been suggested to use a drop down menu, with a list of the companies and a link to the file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is such a thing possible in R and is there an easy-ish  way of implementating it?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="386448" LastEditorUserId="881229" LastEditDate="2014-03-25T16:29:25.037" LastActivityDate="2014-09-12T11:33:53.433" Title="Drop down list implementation in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;drop-down-menu&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
