  <row Id="42070" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="42092" CreationDate="2008-09-03T16:30:50.563" Score="9" ViewCount="6377" Body="&lt;p&gt;What's going on here?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;printf.sh:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;#! /bin/sh&#xA;NAME=&quot;George W. Bush&quot;&#xA;printf &quot;Hello, %s\n&quot; $NAME&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Command line session:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$ ./printf.sh&#xA;Hello, George&#xA;Hello, W.&#xA;Hello, Bush&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;UPDATE: &lt;code&gt;printf &quot;Hello, %s\n&quot; &quot;$NAME&quot;&lt;/code&gt; works. For why I'm not using &lt;code&gt;echo&lt;/code&gt;, consider&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;echo.sh:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;#! /bin/sh&#xA;FILE=&quot;C:\tmp&quot;&#xA;echo &quot;Filename: $FILE&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Command-line:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$ ./echo.sh&#xA;Filename: C:    mp&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/009695399/utilities/echo.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;POSIX spec for &lt;code&gt;echo&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; says, &quot;New applications are encouraged to use &lt;code&gt;printf&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;echo&lt;/code&gt;&quot; (for this and other reasons). &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1412" OwnerDisplayName="Chris Conway" LastEditorUserId="1412" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris Conway" LastEditDate="2008-09-03T17:03:20.843" LastActivityDate="2008-09-05T16:38:48.480" Title="Why does the Bourne shell printf iterate over a %s argument?" Tags="&lt;unix&gt;&lt;shell&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3616406" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3616820" CreationDate="2010-09-01T08:55:23.377" Score="5" ViewCount="2930" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying to use the &lt;strong&gt;getURL&lt;/strong&gt; function of &lt;strong&gt;RCurl&lt;/strong&gt; Package in order to access an &lt;strong&gt;ASP&lt;/strong&gt; Webpage as:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;my_url &amp;lt;- &quot;http://www.my_site.org/my_site/main.asp?ID=11&amp;amp;REFID=33&quot;&#xA;webpage &amp;lt;- getURL(my_url)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but I get an &lt;strong&gt;Object Moved&lt;/strong&gt; redirection error message like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;    &quot;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;Object moved&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;\n&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;Object Moved&amp;lt;/h1&amp;gt;&#xA;This object may be found &amp;lt;a HREF=\&quot;/my_site/index.asp\&quot;&amp;gt;here&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;\n&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I followed various suggestions like using the &lt;strong&gt;curlEscape&lt;/strong&gt; URL encoding function or by setting the &lt;strong&gt;CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CCURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST&lt;/strong&gt; Parameters via the  &lt;strong&gt;curlSetOpt&lt;/strong&gt; Function as listed in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1279340/php-ssl-curl-object-moved-error&quot;&gt;php ssl curl : object moved error &lt;/a&gt; link, but the later 2 were not recognized as valid RCurl options.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any suggestions how to overcome the issue?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="274136" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T11:45:58.217" LastActivityDate="2010-09-01T16:47:36.193" Title="&quot;Object Moved&quot; error in using the RCurl getURL function in order to access an ASP Webpage" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;curl&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="7" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" /