  <row Id="3642188" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-09-04T12:09:12.353" Score="6" ViewCount="3874" Body="&lt;p&gt;The following function does not use row pivoting for LU decomposition. Is there an existing function in R that does LU decomposition with &lt;em&gt;row pivot&lt;/em&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; require(Matrix)&#xA;&amp;gt; expand(lu(matrix(rnorm(16),4,4)))&#xA;$L&#xA;4 x 4 Matrix of class &quot;dtrMatrix&quot;&#xA;     [,1]        [,2]        [,3]        [,4]       &#xA;[1,]  1.00000000           .           .           .&#xA;[2,]  0.13812836  1.00000000           .           .&#xA;[3,]  0.27704442  0.39877260  1.00000000           .&#xA;[4,] -0.08512341 -0.24699820  0.04347201  1.00000000&#xA;&#xA;$U&#xA;4 x 4 Matrix of class &quot;dtrMatrix&quot;&#xA;     [,1]       [,2]       [,3]       [,4]      &#xA;[1,]  1.5759031 -0.2074224 -1.5334082 -0.5959756&#xA;[2,]          . -1.3096874 -0.6301727  1.1953838&#xA;[3,]          .          .  1.6316292  0.6256619&#xA;[4,]          .          .          .  0.8078140&#xA;&#xA;$P&#xA;4 x 4 sparse Matrix of class &quot;pMatrix&quot;&#xA;&#xA;[1,] | . . .&#xA;[2,] . | . .&#xA;[3,] . . . |&#xA;[4,] . . | .&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="236215" LastActivityDate="2017-01-10T12:06:44.573" Title="LU decomposition with row pivot" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;linear-algebra&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="42483" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="42540" CreationDate="2008-09-03T20:19:30.280" Score="9" ViewCount="2720" Body="&lt;p&gt;We have a client that has Oracle &lt;em&gt;Standard&lt;/em&gt;, and a project that would be ten times easier addressed using OLAP. However, Oracle only supports OLAP in the &lt;em&gt;Enterprise&lt;/em&gt; version.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Migration to enterprise is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; possible&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm thinking of doing some manual simulation of OLAP, creating relational tables to simulate the technology.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Do you know of some other way I could do this? Maybe an open-source tool for OLAP? Any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1782" OwnerDisplayName="Juan Manuel" LastActivityDate="2010-09-10T09:57:16.310" Title="Simulated OLAP" Tags="&lt;oracle&gt;&lt;olap&gt;&lt;cubes&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="5" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
