  <row Id="43427" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="44711" CreationDate="2008-09-04T09:51:50.543" Score="22" ViewCount="11764" Body="&lt;p&gt;Say I have a site on &lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com&lt;/a&gt;. I would really like allowing bots to see the home page, but any other page need to blocked as it is pointless to spider. In other words&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com&lt;/a&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com/&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com/&lt;/a&gt; should be allowed, but &#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com/anything&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com/anything&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com/someendpoint.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com/someendpoint.aspx&lt;/a&gt; should be blocked.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Further it would be great if I can allow certain query strings to passthrough to the home page:&#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com?okparam=true&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com?okparam=true&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but not&#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;http://example.com?anythingbutokparam=true&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://example.com?anythingbutokparam=true&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2892" OwnerDisplayName="Boaz" LastEditorUserId="1245190" LastEditorDisplayName="Chris" LastEditDate="2014-11-02T12:06:04.640" LastActivityDate="2014-11-02T12:06:04.640" Title="How to set up a robot.txt which only allows the default page of a site" Tags="&lt;web-crawler&gt;&lt;bots&gt;&lt;robots.txt&gt;&lt;googlebot&gt;&lt;slurp&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="6" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="43455" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="43468" CreationDate="2008-09-04T10:28:33.840" Score="27" ViewCount="24547" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have an XML object (loaded using &lt;code&gt;XMLHTTPRequest&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;code&gt;responseXML&lt;/code&gt;).  I have modified the object (using jQuery) and would like to store it as text in a string.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There is apparently a simple way to do it in Firefox et al:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var xmlString = new XMLSerializer().serializeToString( doc );&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(from &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.rosettacode.org/w/index.php?title=DOM_XML_Serialization#JavaScript&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;rosettacode&lt;/a&gt; )&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But how does one do it in &lt;strong&gt;IE6 and other browsers&lt;/strong&gt; (without, of course, breaking Firefox)?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4505" OwnerDisplayName="Eero" LastEditorUserId="92701" LastEditDate="2016-02-08T14:59:23.213" LastActivityDate="2016-02-08T14:59:23.213" Title="How do I serialize a DOM to XML text, using JavaScript, in a cross browser way?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;xml&gt;&lt;dom&gt;&lt;serialization&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="13" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="43458" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-04T10:31:18.827" Score="5" ViewCount="2483" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am trying out the dialog from jquery UI. All the online &lt;a href=&quot;http://dev.jquery.com/view/trunk/ui/demos/functional/#ui.dialog&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;demos&lt;/a&gt; use flora.css.&#xA;I can't get the dialog to display correctly with the css file generated by the &lt;a href=&quot;http://ui.jquery.com/themeroller&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;themeroller&lt;/a&gt; application.&#xA;Am I missing something? Should these things work out of the box?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Update: Thanks Brock. When I cleaned up my code to make a sample, I realized that the HTML in &lt;em&gt;demo.html&lt;/em&gt; (that comes with the themeroller.zip) is a little too verbose.&#xA;All I needed to do was give the dialog div the attribute &lt;code&gt;class=&amp;quot;ui-dialog&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;lang-html prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div id=&amp;quot;SERVICE03_DLG&amp;quot; class=&amp;quot;ui-dialog&amp;quot;&amp;gt;please enter something&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;label for=&amp;quot;something&amp;quot;&amp;gt;somthing:&amp;lt;/label&amp;gt;&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;input name=&amp;quot;something&amp;quot; id=&amp;quot;something&amp;quot; type=&amp;quot;text&amp;quot; maxlength=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; size=&amp;quot;24&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'll accept your answer. Thanks for your time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3751" LastEditorUserId="1681985" LastEditorDisplayName="Ovesh" LastEditDate="2020-08-22T22:39:05.257" LastActivityDate="2020-08-22T22:39:19.913" Title="How do I make the jquery dialog work with the themeroller themes?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;jquery&gt;&lt;dialog&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
