  <row Id="43511" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="43516" CreationDate="2008-09-04T11:27:34.183" Score="21" ViewCount="7292" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have some classes layed out like this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;class A&#xA;{&#xA;    public virtual void Render()&#xA;    {&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;class B : A&#xA;{&#xA;    public override void Render()&#xA;    {&#xA;        // Prepare the object for rendering&#xA;        SpecialRender();&#xA;        // Do some cleanup&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    protected virtual void SpecialRender()&#xA;    {&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;class C : B&#xA;{&#xA;    protected override void SpecialRender()&#xA;    {&#xA;        // Do some cool stuff&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is it possible to prevent the C class from overriding the Render method, without breaking the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;A obj = new C();&#xA;obj.Render();       // calls B.Render -&amp;gt; c.SpecialRender&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3602" OwnerDisplayName="TrolleFar" LastActivityDate="2021-12-27T14:22:57.493" Title="Can I prevent an inherited virtual method from being overridden in subclasses?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;polymorphism&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="43524" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-04T11:34:10.173" Score="3" ViewCount="9441" Body="&lt;p&gt;It is slow to load anything other than a small project. It is slow to quit; it can sometimes take minutes. It can be slow to open new files. The record macro feature used to be useful. It is now so slow to start up it's almost always quicker to do it manually!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;More info would be helpful. How big are your solutions? What platform are you on. What 3rd party plugins are you running? What else is running on your pc? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;3.2GHz P4 Hyperthreaded, 2GB RAM. Running Outlook, Perforce, IE7, directory browsers. Usually have 1-3 instances of VS running. It's much slower than VC6, say. It seems to take a long time to load projects and close down. I'm interested in if people know reasons why this happens, because of the way VS is written. Is it using .net internally and GC slows it down?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3233" OwnerDisplayName="Nick" LastEditorUserId="14444" LastEditorDisplayName="moocha" LastEditDate="2009-03-23T09:19:01.233" LastActivityDate="2014-01-02T11:24:39.373" Title="Why is Visual Studio 2005 so slow?" Tags="&lt;visual-studio&gt;&lt;visual-c++&gt;&lt;visual-studio-2005&gt;" AnswerCount="13" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
