  <row Id="43926" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="43937" CreationDate="2008-09-04T14:53:14.440" Score="24" ViewCount="24550" Body="&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;.container&lt;/code&gt; can contain many &lt;code&gt;.components&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;.components&lt;/code&gt; themselves can contain &lt;code&gt;.containers&lt;/code&gt; (which in turn can contain .components etc. etc.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Given code like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$(&quot;.container .component&quot;).each(function(){&#xA;  $(&quot;.container&quot;, this).css('border', '1px solid #f00');&#xA;});&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What do I need to add to the line within the braces to select only the nested &lt;code&gt;.containers&lt;/code&gt; that have their &lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; in CSS set to &lt;code&gt;auto&lt;/code&gt;?  I'm sure it's something simple, but I haven't really used jQuery all that much.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2268" OwnerDisplayName="Adam Hepton" LastEditorUserId="2756409" LastEditDate="2019-10-18T07:01:06.957" LastActivityDate="2019-10-18T07:01:06.957" Title="Can jQuery select by CSS rule, not class?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;jquery&gt;&lt;css-selectors&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
