  <row Id="43955" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="43959" CreationDate="2008-09-04T15:06:01.133" Score="81" ViewCount="166875" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is it possible to modify the title of the message box the confirm() function opens in JavaScript? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I could create a modal popup box, but I would like to do this as minimalistic as possible.&#xA;I would like to do something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;confirm(&quot;This is the content of the message box&quot;, &quot;Modified title&quot;);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The default title in Internet Explorer is &quot;Windows Internet Explorer&quot; and in Firefox it's &quot;[JavaScript-program].&quot; Not very informative. Though I can understand from a browser security stand point that you shouldn't be able to do this.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2241" OwnerDisplayName="pr0nin" LastEditorUserId="63550" LastEditDate="2009-12-10T22:51:07.920" LastActivityDate="2020-08-21T02:39:03.563" Title="Changing the default title of confirm() in JavaScript?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="10" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="43960" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-04T15:07:30.550" Score="-1" ViewCount="128" Body="&lt;p&gt;Does anyone have any experience with any COTS systems for managing workshops and the associated registrations, courses, communications, etc.?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We have a home-built Perl system that is about 8 years old and is currently embedded as an iframe in a SharePoint portal site (externally facing). Needless to say, it isn't integrated into our site well, looks like crap, needs an overhaul, lacks features, etc. It would be nice to find either a product we can install or a service that provides those features.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3262" OwnerDisplayName="mattsmith321" LastActivityDate="2009-02-27T16:48:18.187" Title="COTS Workshop Registration System" Tags="&lt;cots&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3701170" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3701896" CreationDate="2010-09-13T14:05:14.720" Score="28" ViewCount="84178" Body="&lt;p&gt;I want to perform a &lt;strong&gt;stepwise linear Regression&lt;/strong&gt; using &lt;strong&gt;p-values&lt;/strong&gt; as a selection criterion, e.g.: at each step dropping variables that have the highest i.e. the most insignificant p-values, stopping when all values are significant defined by some threshold &lt;em&gt;alpha&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am totally aware that I should use the AIC (e.g. command &lt;em&gt;step&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;stepAIC&lt;/em&gt;) or some other criterion instead, but my boss has no grasp of statistics and insist on using p-values.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If necessary, I could program my own routine, but I am wondering if there is an already implemented version of this.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="276049" LastEditorUserId="680068" LastEditDate="2018-02-12T10:29:24.500" LastActivityDate="2018-11-23T20:10:45.973" Title="Stepwise regression using p-values to drop variables with nonsignificant p-values" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;&lt;regression&gt;&lt;p-value&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="8" FavoriteCount="37" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="43970" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="107795" CreationDate="2008-09-04T15:10:13.960" Score="8" ViewCount="22162" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm setting up a server which is on a network behind a firewall and I want programs on this computer to be able to use sendmail to send emails to any email address.  We have an SMTP server running on this network (let's call it mailrelay.example.com) which is how we're supposed to get outgoing emails through the firewall.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So how do I configure sendmail to send all mail through mailrelay.example.com?  Googling hasn't given me the answer yet, and has only revealed that sendmail configuration is extremely complex and annoying.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1694" OwnerDisplayName="Eli Courtwright" LastEditorUserId="1902010" LastEditorDisplayName="ceejayoz" LastEditDate="2008-09-04T15:18:19.823" LastActivityDate="2008-09-20T10:05:40.757" Title="Configuring sendmail behind a firewall" Tags="&lt;configuration&gt;&lt;firewall&gt;&lt;sendmail&gt;&lt;smarthost&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3703434" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3703486" CreationDate="2010-09-13T18:51:46.543" Score="2" ViewCount="165" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a dataset that looks like so:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;            x             y&#xA;1       0.0000  0.4459183993&#xA;2     125.1128  0.4068805502&#xA;3     250.2257  0.3678521348&#xA;4     375.3385  0.3294434397&#xA;5     500.4513  0.2922601919&#xA;6     625.5642  0.2566381551&#xA;7     750.6770  0.2229130927&#xA;8     875.7898  0.1914207684&#xA;9    1000.9026  0.1624969456&#xA;10   1126.0155  0.1364773879&#xA;11   1251.1283  0.1136978589&#xA;12   1376.2411  0.0944717371&#xA;13   1501.3540  0.0786550515&#xA;14   1626.4668  0.0656763159&#xA;15   1751.5796  0.0549476349&#xA;16   1876.6925  0.0458811131&#xA;17   2001.8053  0.0378895151&#xA;18   2126.9181  0.0304416321&#xA;19   2252.0309  0.0231041362&#xA;20   2377.1438  0.0154535572&#xA;21   2502.2566  0.0070928195&#xA;22   2627.3694 -0.0020708606&#xA;23   2752.4823 -0.0119351534&#xA;24   2877.5951 -0.0223944877&#xA;25   3002.7079 -0.0332811155&#xA;26   3127.8208 -0.0442410358&#xA;27   3252.9336 -0.0548855203&#xA;...&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Full data available &lt;a href=&quot;http://snipt.org/kOw&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It's easier to see visually by plotting x and y with a zero intercept line:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;ggplot(dat,aes(x,y)) + geom_line() + geom_hline(yintercept=0)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can see the plot &lt;a href=&quot;https://imgur.com/8pUSg.jpg&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; (if you don't want to download the data and plot it yourself.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to pick out 'patches' defined as the distance along x from when the line goes above zero on the y till it goes below zero. This will always happen at least once (since the line starts above zero), but can happen many times.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Picking out the first patch is easy. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;patch1=dat[min(which(dat$y&amp;lt;=0.000001)),]&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But how would I loop through and pick up subsequent patches?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="313163" LastActivityDate="2010-09-13T19:13:12.070" Title="How do I write a generic function to pick out distance between positive values?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="43971" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="43983" CreationDate="2008-09-04T15:10:22.137" Score="10" ViewCount="4668" Body="&lt;p&gt;Let's say I have a web site for hosting community generated content that targets a very specific set of users.  Now, let's say in the interest of fostering a better community I have an off-topic area where community members can post or talk about anything they want, regardless of the site's main theme.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, I &lt;em&gt;want&lt;/em&gt; most of the content to get indexed by Google.  The notable exception is the off-topic content.  Each thread has it's own page, but all the threads are listed in the same folder so I can't just exclude search engines from a folder somewhere.  It has to be per-page.  A traditional robots.txt file would get huge, so how else could I accomplish this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3043" OwnerDisplayName="Joel Coehoorn" LastEditorUserId="3043" LastEditDate="2012-08-19T20:00:39.160" LastActivityDate="2014-11-18T17:08:55.447" Title="Dynamic robots.txt" Tags="&lt;seo&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="43992" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="50977" CreationDate="2008-09-04T15:15:24.137" Score="5" ViewCount="6503" Body="&lt;p&gt;I want to allow my users to embed their own Flash animations in their posts.  Usually the actual file is hosted on some free image hosting site.  I wouldn't actually load the flash unless the user clicked a button to play (so that nothing auto-plays on page load).  I know people can make some really annoying crap in flash, but I can't find any information about potential &lt;em&gt;serious&lt;/em&gt; damage a flash app could cause to the viewer.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is it unsafe to embed just any flash file from the internets?  If so, how can I let users embed innocent animations but still keep out the harmful apps?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;edit:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;From what I can gather, the most obvious threat is for actionscript to redirect you to a malicious site.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Adobe &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.adobe.com/devnet/flashplayer/articles/secure_swf_apps_04.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;says&lt;/a&gt; you can set &lt;strong&gt;allowScriptAccess=never&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;allowNetworking=none&lt;/strong&gt; and the swf should have no access to anything outside of itself.  &lt;strong&gt;Will this solve all my problems?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="744" OwnerDisplayName="dsims" LastEditorUserId="744" LastEditorDisplayName="dsims" LastEditDate="2008-09-17T15:12:39.397" LastActivityDate="2014-02-15T07:07:38.337" Title="How to safely embed any flash file (swf)?" Tags="&lt;security&gt;&lt;flash&gt;&lt;embed&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
