  <row Id="44247" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="44265" CreationDate="2008-09-04T17:30:58.443" Score="1" ViewCount="558" Body="&lt;p&gt;As a project manager, you are required to organize time so that the project meets a deadline.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there some sort of equations to use for estimating how long the development will take?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;let's say the database&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;time = sql storedprocedures * tables manipulated or something similar&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or are you just stuck having to get the experience to get adequate estimations? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4298" OwnerDisplayName="Matt R" LastEditorUserId="6281993" LastEditDate="2016-12-24T07:36:17.607" LastActivityDate="2016-12-24T07:36:17.607" Title="What is the best practice for estimating required time for development of the SDLC phases?" Tags="&lt;project-management&gt;&lt;time-management&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2018-03-30T10:07:43.687" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
