  <row Id="3765950" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3766007" CreationDate="2010-09-22T02:39:49.303" Score="33" ViewCount="33442" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to use R to make a series of boxplots which are sorted by median value. Suppose then I execute:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;boxplot(cost ~ type)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This would give me some boxplots were cost is shown on the y axis and the type category is visible on the x-axis:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;-----     -----&#xA;  |         |&#xA; [ ]        |&#xA;  |        [ ]&#xA;  |         |&#xA;-----     -----&#xA;  A         B&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, what I'd like is the boxplot figures sorted from highest to lowest median value. My suspicion is that what I need to do is change the labels of the type (A or B) to numerically indicate which is the lowest and highest median value, but I wonder if there is a more clever way to solve the problem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="39584" LastEditorUserId="680068" LastEditDate="2017-12-12T20:34:39.267" LastActivityDate="2017-12-12T22:30:24.450" Title="Sorting a boxplot based on median value" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;boxplot&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="11" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
