  <row Id="45122" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="45126" CreationDate="2008-09-05T02:15:33.707" Score="55" ViewCount="52091" Body="&lt;p&gt;Say I have the following file structure:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;app/&#xA;  app.py&#xA;  controllers/&#xA;    __init__.py&#xA;    project.py&#xA;    plugin.py&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If app/controllers/project.py defines a class Project, app.py would import it like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;from app.controllers.project import Project&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'd like to just be able to do:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;from app.controllers import Project&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How would this be done?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1914" OwnerDisplayName="Bill Williams" LastEditorUserId="21632" LastEditorDisplayName="Adam Bellaire" LastEditDate="2008-10-08T19:57:28.283" LastActivityDate="2016-06-30T16:24:53.490" Title="Python packages - import by class, not file" Tags="&lt;python&gt;&lt;packages&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="24" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3782337" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3782694" CreationDate="2010-09-23T20:33:04.810" Score="4" ViewCount="2560" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working on filling in an Rd file for a function.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I use \eqn{2^{x}} in the Details section, then build and install the package, there is no superscripted exponent.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Looking at R-exts.pdf, it points to Poisson.Rd as an example on how to use \eqn or \deqn. In the example in that file, there is a superscripted exponent.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I look at the help file for Poisson (&lt;code&gt;?Poisson&lt;/code&gt;), There are no superscripted exponents.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is this an issue on my computer or is this standard behavior?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; sessionInfo()&#xA;R version 2.11.1 (2010-05-31) &#xA;i386-apple-darwin9.8.0 &#xA;&#xA;locale:&#xA;[1] en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8/C/C/en_US.UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8&#xA;&#xA;attached base packages:&#xA;[1] stats     graphics  grDevices datasets  utils     methods   base     &#xA;&#xA;other attached packages:&#xA;[1] cimis_0.1-3    RLastFM_0.1-4  RCurl_1.4-2    bitops_1.0-4.1 XML_3.1-0      lattice_0.18-8&#xA;&#xA;loaded via a namespace (and not attached):&#xA;[1] grid_2.11.1  tools_2.11.1&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="309600" LastActivityDate="2021-09-17T10:18:28.220" Title="Mathematical notion/superscripts in Rd files" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;documentation&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="45123" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="45138" CreationDate="2008-09-05T02:15:49.040" Score="11" ViewCount="2337" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am designing a new System and I have a lot of Interfaces that will grow over time with the system. What is the best practice to name this interfaces&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;ISomethingV01&#xA;ISomethingV02&#xA;etc&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and I do this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;public interface ISomething{&#xA;      void method();&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;then I have to add method 2 so now what I do?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;public interface ISomethingV2:ISomething{&#xA;      void method2();&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;or same other way?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1154" OwnerDisplayName="Jedi Master Spooky" LastEditorUserId="120292" LastEditorDisplayName="aku" LastEditDate="2009-06-20T16:39:00.230" LastActivityDate="2012-04-02T08:37:06.527" Title="Interfaces and Versioning" Tags="&lt;naming-conventions&gt;&lt;interface&gt;&lt;versioning&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
