  <row Id="45769" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-05T13:12:18.057" Score="3" ViewCount="1356" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm curious about everyones practices when it comes to using or distributing libraries for an application that you write.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First of all, when developing your application do you link the debug or release version of the libraries? (For when you run your application in debug mode)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then when you run your app in release mode just before deploying, which build of the libraries do you use?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do you perform the switch between your debug and release version of the libraries? Do you do it manually, do you use macros, or whatever else is it that you do?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4225" OwnerDisplayName="Dewm Solo" LastEditorUserId="1" LastEditDate="2012-07-03T04:53:38.733" LastActivityDate="2012-07-03T04:53:38.733" Title="Managing/Using libraries with Debug builds vs Release builds" Tags="&lt;release-builds&gt;&lt;debug-build&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
