  <row Id="46130" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="47308" CreationDate="2008-09-05T16:01:35.887" Score="5" ViewCount="332" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a list of &lt;code&gt;Foo&lt;/code&gt;. Foo has properties &lt;code&gt;Bar&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Lum&lt;/code&gt;. Some &lt;code&gt;Foo&lt;/code&gt;s have identical values for &lt;code&gt;Bar&lt;/code&gt;. How can I use lambda/linq to group my &lt;code&gt;Foo&lt;/code&gt;s by &lt;code&gt;Bar&lt;/code&gt; so I can iterate over each grouping's &lt;code&gt;Lum&lt;/code&gt;s?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1946" OwnerDisplayName="Deeno" LastEditorUserId="1621391" LastEditDate="2016-08-14T23:23:32.707" LastActivityDate="2016-08-14T23:23:32.707" Title="How do I group in memory lists?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;linq&gt;&lt;lambda&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="46133" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-05T16:03:46.537" Score="2" ViewCount="715" Body="&lt;p&gt;We generate dynamic reports in all of our business web applications written for .Net and J2EE.  On the server side we use ActiveReports.Net and JasperReports to generate the reports.  We then export them to PDF to send down to the browser.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our clients all use Adobe Reader.  We have endless problems with the different versions of  Adobe Reader and how they are setup on the client.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What file format/readers are others using for their dynamic reports?  We need something that allows for  precise layout as many of the reports are forms that are printed with data from out systems.  HTML is not expressive enough.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4231" OwnerDisplayName="Mike Schall" LastEditorUserId="881229" LastEditDate="2014-01-28T21:42:19.347" LastActivityDate="2014-01-28T21:42:19.347" Title="File format for generating dynamic reports in applications" Tags="&lt;pdf&gt;&lt;adobe-reader&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3828410" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3829122" CreationDate="2010-09-30T06:50:29.543" Score="2" ViewCount="1560" Body="&lt;p&gt;Either it's late, or I've found a bug, or cast doesn't like colnames with &quot;.&quot; in them. This all happens inside a function, but it &quot;doesn't work&quot; outside of a function as much as it doesn't work inside of it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- structure(list(df.q6 = structure(c(1L, 1L, 1L, 11L, 11L, 9L, &#xA;4L, 11L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 11L, 5L, 4L, 9L, 4L, 4L, 1L, 9L, 4L, &#xA;10L, 1L, 11L, 9L), .Label = c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;g&quot;, &#xA;&quot;h&quot;, &quot;i&quot;, &quot;j&quot;, &quot;k&quot;), class = &quot;factor&quot;), df.s5 = structure(c(4L, &#xA;4L, 1L, 2L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 3L, 4L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 4L, 1L, 3L, 4L, &#xA;2L, 2L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 2L, 2L, 1L), .Label = c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &#xA;&quot;e&quot;), class = &quot;factor&quot;)), .Names = c(&quot;df.q6&quot;, &quot;df.s5&quot;), row.names = c(NA, &#xA;25L), class = &quot;data.frame&quot;)&#xA;&#xA;cast(x, df.q6 + df.s5 ~., length)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;No worky. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, if: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;colnames(x) &amp;lt;- c(&quot;variable&quot;, &quot;value&quot;)&#xA;cast(x, variable + value ~., length)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Works like a charm. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170352" LastActivityDate="2010-10-01T23:44:07.757" Title="reshape: cast oddity" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="46136" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="46184" CreationDate="2008-09-05T16:04:36.580" Score="6" ViewCount="1016" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a large codebase that targetted Flash 7, with a &lt;em&gt;lot&lt;/em&gt; of AS2 classes.  I'm hoping that I'll be able to use Flex for any new projects, but a lot of new stuff in our roadmap is additions to the old code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The syntax for AS2 and AS3 is generally the same, so I'm starting to wonder how hard it would be to port the current codebase to Flex/AS3.  I know all the UI-related stuff would be iffy (currently the UI is generated at runtime with a lot of createEmptyMovieClip() and attachMovie() stuff), but the UI and controller/model stuff is mostly separated.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Has anyone tried porting a large codebase of AS2 code to AS3?  How difficult is it?  What kinds of pitfalls did you run into?  Any recommendations for approaches to doing this kind of project?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1409" OwnerDisplayName="Herms" LastActivityDate="2008-09-18T02:21:28.340" Title="What is the best approach to moving a preexisting project from Flash 7/AS2 to Flex/AS3?" Tags="&lt;apache-flex&gt;&lt;flash&gt;&lt;actionscript-3&gt;&lt;porting&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
