  <row Id="46214" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="46253" CreationDate="2008-09-05T16:22:26.837" Score="74" ViewCount="29863" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm looking for any way that I can improve the selector performance of a jQuery call.  Specifically things like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is &lt;code&gt;$(&quot;div.myclass&quot;)&lt;/code&gt; faster than &lt;code&gt;$(&quot;.myclass&quot;)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would think it might be, but I don't know if jQuery is smart enough to limit the search by tag name first, etc.  Anyone have any ideas for how to formulate a jQuery selector string for best performance?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4541" OwnerDisplayName="JC Grubbs" LastEditorUserId="89989" LastEditorDisplayName="Jeff Atwood" LastEditDate="2010-02-13T00:28:47.927" LastActivityDate="2012-07-13T17:37:11.570" Title="Good ways to improve jQuery selector performance?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;jquery&gt;&lt;performance&gt;&lt;css-selectors&gt;" AnswerCount="12" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="32" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
