  <row Id="3843284" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3843365" CreationDate="2010-10-01T21:54:35.877" Score="1" ViewCount="416" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a dataframe:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;priors &amp;lt;- data.frame(dist = c('lnorm', 'beta', 'gamma'),&#xA;                      a   = c(0.5, 1, 10),&#xA;                      b   = c(0.4, 25, 4),&#xA;                      n   = c(100, 100, 100)&#xA;                     )&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and I would like to take n samples from the distribution with parameters a and b.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have written this function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;pr.samp &amp;lt;- function(n,dist,a,b) {eval (parse ( &#xA;                    text = &#xA;                    paste(&quot;r&quot;,dist,&quot;(&quot;,n,&quot;,&quot;,a,&quot;,&quot;,b,&quot;)&quot;,sep = &quot;&quot;)&#xA;                    ))}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would like to know:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;is there a better approach?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;how would I use one of the apply functions to run this on each row?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;do I have to convert the dataframe to a matrix to do this?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks in advance!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="199217" LastActivityDate="2010-10-01T22:21:05.253" Title="how to sample distributions, given n, distribution name, and parameters in a dataframe?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;performance&gt;&lt;apply&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
