  <row Id="3867127" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3867291" CreationDate="2010-10-05T19:44:35.637" Score="2" ViewCount="2811" Body="&lt;p&gt;Suppose I have a data array,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;dat &amp;lt;- array(NA, c(115,45,10))&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can I get a new data array&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;dat1&amp;lt;- array(NA, c(115,45))&lt;/code&gt; by averaging &lt;code&gt;dat&lt;/code&gt; by the third dimension?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="467243" LastEditorUserId="176923" LastEditDate="2010-10-05T20:10:42.903" LastActivityDate="2010-10-05T20:10:42.903" Title="How to reduce the array dimensions in R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3867140" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3867252" CreationDate="2010-10-05T19:46:14.507" Score="4" ViewCount="570" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm interested in experimenting with writing R code on my laptop which I then execute on an Amazon S3 machine. I want the execution to be interactive because I'm building a work flow and the data is only on my EC2 instance, not on my local machine. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I could redirect X11 to put the remove ESS window on my local machine, but I've had some latency issues with that. What I would like to do is just have ESS send the execute command to the remote machine. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Googling around I found a &lt;a href=&quot;http://blog.nguyenvq.com/2009/06/01/run-a-remote-r-session-in-emacs-emacs-ess-r-ssh/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;very interesting blog post&lt;/a&gt; that seems to do exactly this including redirecting graphical output to my local machine. Anyone had experience with this type of work flow on Amazon EC2 and have any tips/tricks/advice? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="37751" LastEditorUserId="143305" LastEditDate="2010-10-05T19:56:41.980" LastActivityDate="2013-08-31T15:46:23.373" Title="Using ESS on my desktop to run R in the cloud" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;amazon-ec2&gt;&lt;cloud&gt;&lt;ess&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="4" CommunityOwnedDate="2010-10-05T19:46:14.507" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
