  <row Id="47005" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="47054" CreationDate="2008-09-05T22:32:26.773" Score="4" ViewCount="1059" Body="&lt;p&gt;Does anyone have any tips or gotcha moments to look out for when trying to migrate MySQL tables from the the default case-insenstive swedish or ascii charsets to utf-8? Some of the projects that I'm involved in are striving for better internationalization and the database is going to be a significant part of this change.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Before we look to alter the database, we are going to convert each site to use UTF-8 character encoding (from least critical to most) to help ensure all input/output is using the same character set.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks for any help&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4563" OwnerDisplayName="Mike H" LastEditorUserId="23855" LastEditorDisplayName="chills42" LastEditDate="2008-11-05T14:39:26.720" LastActivityDate="2008-11-05T14:39:26.720" Title="MySQL UTF/Unicode migration tips" Tags="&lt;mysql&gt;&lt;unicode&gt;&lt;utf-8&gt;&lt;internationalization&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
