  <row Id="47052" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="13180223" CreationDate="2008-09-05T23:08:06.610" Score="8" ViewCount="4288" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm looking to convert a SQL like statement on the fly to the equivalent regex i.e. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;LIKE '%this%'&#xA;LIKE 'Sm_th'&#xA;LIKE '[C-P]arsen'&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What's the best approach to doing this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;P.S. I'm looking to do this on the .Net Framework (C#).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4843" LastEditorUserId="858913" LastEditorDisplayName="Bittercoder" LastEditDate="2017-12-16T23:00:06.863" LastActivityDate="2021-08-19T10:52:19.050" Title="What code would I use to convert a SQL like expression to a regex on the fly?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;sql&gt;&lt;regex&gt;&lt;tsql&gt;&lt;sql-like&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
