  <row Id="47206" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-06T02:39:33.513" Score="1" ViewCount="773" Body="&lt;p&gt;How many rows should be in the (main) buffer of a virtual Listview control?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am witting an application in pure 'c' to the Win32 API.  There is an ODBC connection to a database which will retrieve the items (actually rows).  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The MSDN sample code implies a fixed size buffer of 30 for the end cache (Which would almost certainly not be optimal).  I think the end cache and the main cache should be the same size.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My thinking is that the buffer should be more than the maximum number of items that could be displayed by the list view at one time.  I guess this could be re-calculated each time the Listivew was resized?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or, is it just better to go with a large fixed value.  If so what is that value?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3137" OwnerDisplayName="David Morris" LastEditorUserId="3137" LastEditorDisplayName="David Morris" LastEditDate="2008-09-06T02:46:40.970" LastActivityDate="2010-02-17T00:20:02.847" Title="How many rows should be in the (main) buffer of a virtual Listview control?" Tags="&lt;c&gt;&lt;winapi&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
