  <row Id="3919315" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-10-12T21:49:43.080" Score="6" ViewCount="889" Body="&lt;p&gt;I wish to access my Google Webmaster's tools' API via R.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I see from here:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://code.google.com/apis/webmastertools/docs/2.0/reference.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://code.google.com/apis/webmastertools/docs/2.0/reference.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;That it requires fetching a feed behind https and parsing it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any suggestions on how to do it?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="256662" LastEditorUserId="75801" LastEditDate="2010-10-12T22:04:12.053" LastActivityDate="2014-01-21T10:58:17.927" Title="Suggestions on how to access google webmaster tools' api through R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;curl&gt;&lt;google-api&gt;&lt;google-search-console&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3919621" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3922058" CreationDate="2010-10-12T22:40:55.857" Score="3" ViewCount="1957" Body="&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Possible Duplicate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2096473/r-determine-if-a-script-is-running-in-windows-or-linux&quot;&gt;R: determine if a script is running in Windows or Linux&lt;/a&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can an R script determine what platform it's running on? I'm using R 2.10.1, sometimes on Windows, sometimes on Linux. I would prefer a built-in function over filesystem taxonomy. I've already searched the index of the base package for anything with &quot;os&quot; or &quot;platform&quot; in the description — no dice there, alas.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="473899" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:04:10.023" LastActivityDate="2010-10-13T12:38:15.717" Title="How can I determine in R what platform I'm running on?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;multiplatform&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" ClosedDate="2011-11-26T10:37:22.377" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="3919658" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3919930" CreationDate="2010-10-12T22:49:34.843" Score="4" ViewCount="8302" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a dataframe with millions of rows and three columns labeled Keywords, Impressions, Clicks. I'd like to add a column with values depending on the evaluation of this function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;isType &amp;lt;- function(Impressions, Clicks)&#xA;{ &#xA;if (Impressions &amp;gt;= 1 &amp;amp; Clicks &amp;gt;= 1){return(&quot;HasClicks&quot;)} else if (Impressions &amp;gt;=1 &amp;amp; Clicks == 0){return(&quot;NoClicks&quot;)} else {return(&quot;ZeroImp&quot;)}&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;so far so good. I then try this to create the column but 1) it takes for ever and 2) it marks all the rows has &quot;HasClicks&quot; even the ones where it shouldn't.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;# Creates a dataframe&#xA;Type &amp;lt;- data.frame()&#xA;# Loops until last row and store it in data.frame&#xA;for (i in c(1:dim(Mydf)[1])) {Type &amp;lt;- rbind(Type,isType(Mydf$Impressions[i], Mydf$Clicks[i]))}&#xA;# Add the column to Mydf&#xA;Mydf &amp;lt;- transform(Mydf, Type = Type)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;input data:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Keywords,Impressions,Clicks&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;Hello&quot;,0,0&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;World&quot;,1,0&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;R&quot;,34,23&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Wanted output:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Keywords,Impressions,Clicks,Type&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;Hello&quot;,0,0,&quot;ZeroImp&quot;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;World&quot;,1,0,&quot;NoClicks&quot;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&quot;R&quot;,34,23,&quot;HasClicks&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="450889" LastEditorUserId="450889" LastEditDate="2010-10-12T23:22:40.013" LastActivityDate="2011-03-08T18:40:43.060" Title="adding a column based on other values" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
