  <row Id="3943355" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-10-15T14:49:42.597" Score="3" ViewCount="921" Body="&lt;p&gt;This &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- list(12, 13)&#xA;names(y &amp;lt;- x) &amp;lt;- c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;gives the error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in names(y &amp;lt;- x) &amp;lt;- c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;) : object 'y' not found&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can anyone explain why? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;According to R's rules of evaluation &lt;code&gt;y &amp;lt;- x&lt;/code&gt; should be evaluated  inside the parent frame of names&amp;lt;-. So y should be created in global environment.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[update] If object &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is already present in the global environment, then the error is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error in names(y &amp;lt;- x) &amp;lt;- c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;) : could not find function &quot;&amp;lt;-&amp;lt;-&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[update2] Here it is, another construct, which I encountered today.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;(X &amp;lt;- matrix(0, nrow = 10, ncol = 10))[1:3] &amp;lt;- 3:5&#xA;Error during wrapup: object 'X' not found&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="453735" LastEditorUserId="453735" LastEditDate="2010-10-16T15:44:09.370" LastActivityDate="2010-10-16T15:44:09.370" Title="Creation of an object inside names&lt;-() gives an error. How to explain?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;eval&gt;&lt;variable-assignment&gt;&lt;evaluation&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
