  <row Id="3971844" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="3971855" CreationDate="2010-10-19T19:13:22.940" Score="68" ViewCount="63966" Body="&lt;p&gt;Similar questions have been raised for other languages: &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2911442/access-variable-value-using-string-representing-variables-name-in-c&quot;&gt;C&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2363405/t-sql-get-variable-value-from-string-with-variable-name&quot;&gt;sql&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1655504/use-variable-value-to-get-value-stored-in-other-variable&quot;&gt;java&lt;/a&gt;, etc.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I'm trying to do this in R. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;ret_series &amp;lt;- c(1, 2, 3)&#xA;x &amp;lt;- &quot;ret_series&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do I get &lt;code&gt;(1, 2, 3)&lt;/code&gt; by calling some function / manipulation on &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;, without direct mentioning of &lt;code&gt;ret_series&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="291877" LastEditorUserId="2204410" LastEditDate="2018-10-17T06:23:26.557" LastActivityDate="2018-10-17T06:23:26.557" Title="Access variable value where the name of variable is stored in a string" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;variables&gt;&lt;r-faq&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="11" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
