  <row Id="48215" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="48302" CreationDate="2008-09-07T07:11:51.447" Score="8" ViewCount="400" Body="&lt;p&gt;Trying to make a make generic select &quot;control&quot; that I can dynamically add elements to, but I am having trouble getting functions to work right.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is what I started with.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$select = $(&quot;&amp;lt;select&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/select&amp;gt;&quot;);&#xA;$select.addOption = function(value,text){&#xA;  $(this).append($(&quot;&amp;lt;option&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/option&amp;gt;&quot;).val(value).text(text));&#xA;};&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This worked fine alone but anytime &lt;code&gt;$select&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;.clone(true)&lt;/code&gt;'ed the &lt;code&gt;addOption()&lt;/code&gt; function is lost.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is my object approach but still the function does not work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;function $selectX() {&#xA;  return $(&quot;&amp;lt;select&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/select&amp;gt;&quot;);&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;$selectX.prototype.addOption() = function(value,text){&#xA;  $(this).append($(&quot;&amp;lt;option&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/option&amp;gt;&quot;).val(value).text(text));&#xA;};&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hack solution is to add the function manually after creation:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$nameSelect= new $selectX;&#xA;$nameSelect.addOption = function(value,text){&#xA;  $(this).append($(&quot;&amp;lt;option&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/option&amp;gt;&quot;).val(value).text(text));&#xA;};&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Am I barking up the wrong tree?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1293" OwnerDisplayName="Jason" LastEditorUserId="7079025" LastEditDate="2019-03-22T15:17:30.210" LastActivityDate="2019-03-22T15:17:30.210" Title="jQuery &amp; Objects, trying to make a lightweight widget" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;jquery&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicen