  <row Id="3974488" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-10-20T03:17:02.493" Score="28" ViewCount="22391" Body="&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Possible Duplicate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1401904/painless-way-to-install-a-new-version-of-r&quot;&gt;Painless way to install a new version of R?&lt;/a&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In R, packages are not compatible across upgrades, and must be reinstalled. Is there any way to easily install the same set of packages in the new version as what I had installed in the old version?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: I can't easily access the old version of R, since I upgrade via apt.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="125921" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T10:30:36.940" LastActivityDate="2010-10-20T03:40:10.490" Title="After I upgrade my R version, how can I easily reinstall all the packages that were installed in the old version?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;upgrade&gt;&lt;reinstall&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="9" ClosedDate="2010-10-20T10:50:55.990" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
