  <row Id="48239" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="48684" CreationDate="2008-09-07T08:09:38.610" Score="1057" ViewCount="1453764" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is there any way to get the ID of the element that fires an event?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'm thinking something like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;snippet&quot; data-lang=&quot;js&quot; data-hide=&quot;false&quot; data-console=&quot;false&quot; data-babel=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&quot;snippet-code&quot;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;$(document).ready(function() {&#xD;&#xA;  $(&quot;a&quot;).click(function() {&#xD;&#xA;    var test = caller.id;&#xD;&#xA;    alert(test.val());&#xD;&#xA;  });&#xD;&#xA;});&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; src=&quot;starterkit/jquery.js&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;form class=&quot;item&quot; id=&quot;aaa&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &amp;lt;input class=&quot;title&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/input&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;form class=&quot;item&quot; id=&quot;bbb&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &amp;lt;input class=&quot;title&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/input&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Except of course that the var &lt;code&gt;test&lt;/code&gt; should contain the id &lt;code&gt;&quot;aaa&quot;&lt;/code&gt;, if the event is fired from the first form, and &lt;code&gt;&quot;bbb&quot;&lt;/code&gt;, if the event is fired from the second form.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1090" OwnerDisplayName="Joda" LastEditorUserId="860099" LastEditDate="2020-06-26T20:38:41.207" LastActivityDate="2021-04-12T01:04:34.047" Title="Getting the ID of the element that fired an event" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;j