  <row Id="48574" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="48623" CreationDate="2008-09-07T16:46:48.053" Score="1" ViewCount="347" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a windows service that runs various system monitoring operations.  However, when running &lt;code&gt;SNMP&lt;/code&gt; related checks, I always get a &lt;code&gt;NullReference exception&lt;/code&gt;.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The code runs fine when run through the user interface (under my username and password), but always errors running as the service.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've tried running the service as different user accounts (including mine), with no luck.  I've tried replacing the &lt;code&gt;SNMP&lt;/code&gt; monitoring code with calling the &lt;code&gt;PowerShell cmdlet get-snmp&lt;/code&gt; (from the &lt;code&gt;/n NetCmdlets&lt;/code&gt;), but that yields the same error.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The application I'm working with is &lt;a href=&quot;http://codeplex.com/polymon&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;PolyMon&lt;/a&gt;.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1233" OwnerDisplayName="Steven Murawski" LastEditorUserId="11383441" LastEditDate="2019-12-23T11:00:23.837" LastActivityDate="2019-12-23T11:00:23.837" Title="Troubleshooting a NullReference exception in a service" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;exception&gt;&lt;powershell&gt;&lt;service&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
