  <row Id="48794" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-07T21:16:55.830" Score="8" ViewCount="12085" Body="&lt;p&gt;Here is a scenario: Let's say I have site with two controllers responsible for displaying different type of content - Pages and Articles. I need to embed Partial View into my masterpage that will list pages and articles filtered with some criteria, and be displayed on each page. I cannot set Model on my masterpage (am I right?). How do I solve this task using Html.RenderPartial?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[EDIT]&#xA;Yes, I'd probably create separate partial views for listing articles and pages, but still, there is a barrier that I cannot and shouldn't set model on masterpage. I need somehow to say &quot;here are the pages&quot; as an argument to my renderpartial, and also for articles. Entire concept of renderpartial with data from database in masterpages is a bit blurry to me.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="481" OwnerDisplayName="Dragan Panjkov" LastEditorUserId="481" LastEditorDisplayName="Dragan Panjkov" LastEditDate="2008-09-07T21:48:23.383" LastActivityDate="2010-01-08T10:23:09.607" Title="Html.RenderPartial call from masterpage" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;asp.net-mvc&gt;&lt;master-pages&gt;&lt;renderpartial&gt;&lt;html-helper&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
