  <row Id="49402" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="49540" CreationDate="2008-09-08T10:06:06.903" Score="5" ViewCount="3354" Body="&lt;p&gt;Imagine a DOS style .cmd file which is used to launch interdependent windowed applications in the right order.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;1) Launch a server application by calling an exe with parameters.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;2) Wait for the server to become initialized (or a fixed amount of time).&lt;br&gt;&#xA;3) Launch client application by calling an exe with parameters.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is the simplest way of accomplishing this kind of batch job in PowerShell?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5085" OwnerDisplayName="d91-jal" LastEditorUserId="2844742" LastEditDate="2015-04-16T00:03:38.403" LastActivityDate="2015-04-16T00:03:38.403" Title="Creating batch jobs in PowerShell" Tags="&lt;powershell&gt;&lt;batch-file&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
