  <row Id="49599" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="49654" CreationDate="2008-09-08T12:46:08.873" Score="3" ViewCount="7866" Body="&lt;p&gt;Jquery has a great language construct that looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;$(document).ready(function() {&#xA;    $(&quot;a&quot;).click(function() {&#xA;        alert(&quot;Hello world!&quot;);&#xA;    });&#xA;});&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As you might guess this, once the document has loaded, binds a custom function to the onClick event of all &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;a&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; tags.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The question is, how can I achieve this same kind of behavior in Prototype?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="305" OwnerDisplayName="Mark Biek" LastEditorUserId="938089" LastEditDate="2011-12-28T11:45:36.767" LastActivityDate="2011-12-28T11:45:36.767" Title="Binding custom functions to DOM events in prototype?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;dom&gt;&lt;prototypejs&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
