  <row Id="4066103" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4067676" CreationDate="2010-11-01T01:24:14.897" Score="0" ViewCount="11080" Body="&lt;p&gt;Say I have two factors and I want to graph them on the same plot, both factors have the same levels.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;s1 &amp;lt;- c(rep(&quot;male&quot;,20), rep(&quot;female&quot;, 30))&#xA;s2 &amp;lt;- c(rep(&quot;male&quot;,10), rep(&quot;female&quot;, 40))&#xA;s1 &amp;lt;- factor(s1, levels=c(&quot;male&quot;, &quot;female&quot;))&#xA;s2 &amp;lt;- factor(s2, levels=c(&quot;male&quot;, &quot;female&quot;))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would have thought that using the table function would have produced the correct result for graphing but it pops out.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;table(s1, s2)&#xA;        s2 &#xA;s1       male female   &#xA;male     10     10   &#xA;female    0     30&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So really two questions, what is the table function doing to get this result and what other function can i use to create a graph with 2 series using functions with the same levels?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Also if it is a factor I'm using barplot2 in the gplots package to graph it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="435473" LastEditorUserId="4370109" LastEditDate="2017-05-03T19:23:55.923" LastActivityDate="2017-05-03T19:23:55.923" Title="Plotting Two Factors on the same Graph" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;factors&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
