  <row Id="4121062" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4124762" CreationDate="2010-11-08T03:37:58.407" Score="4" ViewCount="7425" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm having problems getting the y axis on a horizontal barplot() within the plotting region. See this example, I thought that using ylim and/or yaxp would stop this going off the plotting region, but it doesn't seem to work. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've tried to reproduce the set up I've got:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- matrix(abs(rnorm(34)), nrow = 34, ncol = 3)&#xA;rownames(x) &amp;lt;- c(seq(0,6600,200))&#xA;barplot(x[,3], horiz=TRUE, space = 0.4, main = &quot;Title&quot;, las=1, cex.names=0.8, ylab=&quot;y label&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But the axis goes of the plotting region if I add ylim:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;barplot(x[,3], horiz=TRUE, space = 0.4, ylim = c(0,25), yaxp=c(0,25,1), main = &quot;Title&quot;, las=1, cex.names=0.8, ylab=&quot;y label&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="253579" LastActivityDate="2021-07-06T21:10:40.463" Title="Y axis out of plotting region with barplot() in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;plot&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
