  <row Id="4139032" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4139124" CreationDate="2010-11-09T21:50:45.810" Score="4" ViewCount="3450" Body="&lt;p&gt;This is a problem that comes up often when I am importing raw data from data loggers. A temperature logger is set to record temperature every ten minutes, and a separate gas logger is set to record gas used in the last ten minute interval. I want to combine the data from these two loggers into a single data frame for plotting and analysis, but the times are not exactly aligned. I want to have one row in the data frame for each ten minute period, with the datetime showing the beginning of the time period.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The temperature logger data looks like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;           datetime temperature&#xA;2010-09-30 06:58:53 78.996&#xA;2010-09-30 07:08:53 78.645&#xA;2010-09-30 07:18:53 78.514&#xA;2010-09-30 07:28:53 79.173&#xA;2010-09-30 07:38:53 78.602&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The gas logger data looks like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;           datetime gas&#xA;2010-09-30 13:45:00  0&#xA;2010-09-30 13:55:00  1&#xA;2010-09-30 14:05:00  0&#xA;2010-09-30 14:15:00  4&#xA;2010-09-30 14:25:00  2&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to combine the two data frames on ten minute intervals, so that the combined data looks like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;           datetime temperature gas  &#xA;2010-09-30 13:40:00 NA          0&#xA;2010-09-30 13:50:00 78.996      1&#xA;2010-09-30 14:00:00 78.645      0&#xA;2010-09-30 14:10:00 78.514      4&#xA;2010-09-30 14:20:00 79.173      2&#xA;2010-09-30 07:38:53 78.602      NA&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here's some code to get these two data frames:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;temps &amp;lt;- data.frame(datetime=c(&quot;2010-09-30 06:58:53&quot;,&#xA;&quot;2010-09-30 07:08:53&quot;,&quot;2010-09-30 07:18:53&quot;,&#xA;&quot;2010-09-30 07:28:53&quot;,&quot;2010-09-30 07:38:53&quot;),&#xA; temperature=c(78.996,78.645,78.514,79.173,78.602),&#xA;stringsAsFactors=FALSE)&#xA;temps$datetime &amp;lt;- strptime(temps$datetime, format=&quot;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&quot;)&#xA;gas &amp;lt;- data.frame(datetime=c(&quot;2010-09-30 13:45:00&quot;,&#xA;&quot;2010-09-30 13:55:00&quot;,&quot;2010-09-30 14:05:00&quot;,&#xA;&quot;2010-09-30 14:15:00&quot;,&quot;2010-09-30 14:25:00&quot;),&#xA;gas=c(0,1,0,4,2),stringsAsFactors=FALSE)&#xA;gas$datetime &amp;lt;- strptime(temps$datetime, format=&quot;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerDisplayName="user399470" LastEditorUserId="271616" LastEditDate="2010-11-10T04:03:19.050" LastActivityDate="2010-11-10T04:03:19.050" Title="How do I match data frames by time intervals?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;zoo&gt;&lt;xts&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="50853" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-08T22:27:45.620" Score="1" ViewCount="367" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a relationship between two entities (e1 and e2) and e1 has a collection of e2, however I have a similar relationship set up between (e2 and e3), yet e2 does not contain a collection of e3's, any reason why this would happen? Anything I can post to make this easier to figure out?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: I just noticed that the relationship between e1 and e2 is solid and between e2 and e3 is dotted, what causes that? Is it related?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5236" LastEditorDisplayName="user1228" LastEditDate="2008-09-15T17:14:51.633" LastActivityDate="2008-10-06T19:19:12.730" Title="What is a reason that LINQ to SQL wouldn't generate a collection based on a relationship?" Tags="&lt;linq-to-sql&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
