  <row Id="50900" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="50966" CreationDate="2008-09-08T22:57:20.463" Score="8" ViewCount="12222" Body="&lt;p&gt;So I have about 10 short css files that I use with mvc app.&#xA;There are like&#xA;error.css&#xA;login.css&#xA;etc...&#xA;Just some really short css files that make updating and editing easy (At least for me). What I want is something that will optimize the if else branch and not incorporate it within the final bits. I want to do something like this&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;if(Debug.Mode){&#xA;&#xA;&amp;lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;error.css&quot; /&amp;gt; &#xA;&amp;lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;login.css&quot; /&amp;gt; &#xA;&amp;lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;menu.css&quot; /&amp;gt; &#xA;&amp;lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;page.css&quot; /&amp;gt; &#xA;} else {&#xA;&amp;lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;site.css&quot; /&amp;gt; &#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'll have a msbuild task that will combine all the css files, minimize them and all that good stuff. I just need to know if there is a way to remove the if else branch in the final bits.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="438" OwnerDisplayName="jdelator" LastEditorUserId="1965" LastEditorDisplayName="Jonathan Holland" LastEditDate="2008-09-08T23:45:58.553" LastActivityDate="2019-05-06T21:55:20.210" Title="Best way to detect a release build from a debug build? .net" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;debugging&gt;&lt;release&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
