  <row Id="52981" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="53231" CreationDate="2008-09-09T21:36:35.267" Score="1" ViewCount="2634" Body="&lt;p&gt;So, I have 2 database instances, one is for development in general, another was copied from development for unit tests.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Something changed in the development database that I can't figure out, and I don't know how to see what is different.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I try to delete from a particular table, with for example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;delete from myschema.mytable where id = 555&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I get the following normal response from the unit test DB indicating no row was deleted:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;SQL0100W  No row was found for FETCH, UPDATE or DELETE; or the result of a query is an empty table.  SQLSTATE=02000&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, the development database fails to delete at all with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;DB21034E  The command was processed as an SQL statement because it was not a valid Command Line Processor command.  During SQL processing it returned: SQL0440N  No authorized routine named &quot;=&quot; of type &quot;FUNCTION&quot; having compatible arguments was found.  SQLSTATE=42884&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My best guess is there is some trigger or view that was added or changed that is causing the problem, but I have no idea how to go about finding the problem... has anyone had this problem or know how to figure out what the root of the problem is?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(note that this is a DB2 database)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="122" OwnerDisplayName="Mike Stone" LastActivityDate="2008-10-02T16:37:20.063" Title="Cannot delete from the database...?" Tags="&lt;database&gt;&lt;db2&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4295407" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4295569" CreationDate="2010-11-28T04:41:23.917" Score="0" ViewCount="525" Body="&lt;p&gt;I want to parse csv with micro-second timed index. &#xA;So, I wrote code like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;t&amp;lt;-read.zoo(&quot;test&quot;, index.column = 1, sep=&quot;,&quot;,header=TRUE, format=&quot;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS&quot;)&#xA;t.xts&amp;lt;-as.xts(t)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;after then, I tried to display this but I couldn't see time information on the index.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; t.xts[1:10,4]&#xA;           drate  &#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -149&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -269&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -358&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -358&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -239&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -149&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -149&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -149&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -119&quot;&#xA;2010-09-28 &quot; -149&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried options(digits.secs=6) but didn't work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="204260" LastActivityDate="2010-11-28T05:39:29.267" Title="Display time index in R xts" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;xts&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
