  <row Id="4330072" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4330140" CreationDate="2010-12-01T23:08:16.373" Score="22" ViewCount="32881" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is there any way to pass a variable defined within R to the sqlQuery function within the RODBC package?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Specifically, I need to pass such a variable to either a scalar/table-valued function, a stored procedure, and/or perhaps the WHERE clause of a SELECT statement.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, let:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- 1 ## user-defined&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;example &amp;lt;- sqlQuery(myDB,&quot;SELECT * FROM dbo.my_table_fn (x)&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;example2 &amp;lt;- sqlQuery(myDB,&quot;SELECT * FROM dbo.some_random_table AS foo WHERE foo.ID = x&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;example3 &amp;lt;- sqlQuery(myDB,&quot;EXEC dbo.my_stored_proc (x)&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Obviously, none of these work, but I'm thinking that there's something that enables this sort of functionality.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="489426" LastEditorUserId="680068" LastEditDate="2016-11-11T07:39:52.050" LastActivityDate="2017-10-30T20:06:47.747" Title="Pass R variable to RODBC's sqlQuery?" Tags="&lt;sql&gt;&lt;r&gt;&lt;rodbc&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="14" ClosedDate="2017-10-30T20:06:17.110" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="53618" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="53799" CreationDate="2008-09-10T08:26:32.070" Score="0" ViewCount="2977" Body="&lt;p&gt;I found some informations about controlling IIS 5.1 from command line via adsutil.vbs (&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.microsoft.com/technet/prodtechnol/WindowsServer2003/Library/IIS/d3df4bc9-0954-459a-b5e6-7a8bc462960c.mspx?mfr=true&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;http://www.microsoft.com/technet/prodtechnol/WindowsServer2003/Library/IIS/d3df4bc9-0954-459a-b5e6-7a8bc462960c.mspx?mfr=true&lt;/a&gt;). The utility is available at c:\InetPub\AdminScripts.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The utility throw only errors like the following:&#xA;ErrNumber: -2147463164 (0x80005004)&#xA;Error Trying To GET the Schema of the property: IIS://localhost/Schema/ROOT&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can you tell me, how to check if there exists a virtual directory and create it, if it does not exist?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4980" OwnerDisplayName="Thomas A. Hirsch" LastEditorUserId="2432317" LastEditDate="2013-12-02T13:19:16.503" LastActivityDate="2013-12-02T13:19:16.503" Title="How to control IIS 5.1 from command line?" Tags="&lt;iis&gt;&lt;windows-xp&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="53621" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="176457" CreationDate="2008-09-10T08:27:14.843" Score="1" ViewCount="722" Body="&lt;p&gt;What could be the possible causes for the following exception?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.PlatformNotSupportedException: 'ResourcePool' is not supported on the current platform.&#xA;   at System.EnterpriseServices.Platform.Assert(Boolean fSuccess, String function)&#xA;   at System.EnterpriseServices.Platform.Assert(Version platform, String function)&#xA;   at System.EnterpriseServices.ResourcePool..ctor(TransactionEndDelegate cb)&#xA;   at System.Data.SqlClient.ConnectionPool..ctor(DefaultPoolControl ctrl)&#xA;   at System.Data.SqlClient.PoolManager.FindOrCreatePool(DefaultPoolControl ctrl)&#xA;   at System.Data.SqlClient.SqlConnectionPoolManager.GetPooledConnection(SqlConnectionString options, Boolean&amp;amp; isInTransaction)&#xA;   at System.Data.SqlClient.SqlConnection.Open()&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The platform is Windows 2003 Server SP2. The same code has been tested on Windows XP SP2 without any problems. However, it would be interesting to know what reasons cause this exception regardless of the platform. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="966" OwnerDisplayName="Manga Lee" LastEditorUserId="966" LastEditorDisplayName="Manga Lee" LastEditDate="2008-09-11T07:26:13.687" LastActivityDate="2008-10-06T22:27:17.077" Title="Why is the 'Resource Pool' not supported on the current platform?" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;sql-server&gt;&lt;connection-pooling&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
