  <row Id="53719" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="53723" CreationDate="2008-09-10T09:50:49.620" Score="6" ViewCount="95025" Body="&lt;p&gt;It is obviously possible to hide individual data points in an Excel line chart.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Select a data point. &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Right click -&gt; Format Data Point... &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Select Patterns&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Tab Set Line to None&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do you accomplish the same thing in VBA? Intuition tells me there should be a property on the &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/aa174283(office.11).aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Point object&lt;/a&gt; &lt;code&gt;Chart.SeriesCollection(&amp;lt;index&amp;gt;).Points(&amp;lt;index&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; which deals with this...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5085" OwnerDisplayName="d91-jal" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2018-07-09T18:41:45.953" LastActivityDate="2015-07-16T12:42:47.167" Title="Hiding data points in Excel line charts" Tags="&lt;excel&gt;&lt;charts&gt;&lt;vba&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
