  <row Id="54207" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="307039" CreationDate="2008-09-10T14:32:19.553" Score="4" ViewCount="5037" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have an internal enterprise app that currently consumes 10 different web services. They're consumed via old style &quot;Web References&quot; instead of using WCF.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem I'm having is trying to work with the other teams in the company who are authoring the services I'm consuming. I found I needed to capture the exact SOAP messages that I'm sending and receiving.  I did this by creating a new attribute that extends SoapExtensionAttribute. I then just add that attribute to the service method in the generated Reference.cs file. This works, but is painful for two reasons. First, it's a generated file so anything I do in there can be overwritten. Second, I have to remember to remove the attribute before checking in the file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Is There a better way to capture the exact SOAP messages that I am sending and receiving?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2595" OwnerDisplayName="Rob" LastEditorUserId="133" LastEditDate="2016-11-28T10:03:05.767" LastActivityDate="2016-11-28T10:03:05.767" Title="Soap logging in .net" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;web-services&gt;&lt;soap&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="4359310" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4359479" CreationDate="2010-12-05T14:46:51.883" Score="9" ViewCount="6190" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am currently running ANOVA for a project at school that has a large number of possible runs (1400 or so) but some of them aren't able to run ANOVA in R. I wrote a script to run all the ANOVA's, but some of them will not run and the Rout file gives me &#xA;Error in &lt;code&gt;contrasts&amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;(&lt;code&gt;*tmp*&lt;/code&gt;, value = &quot;contr.treatment&quot;) : &#xA;  contrasts can be applied only to factors with 2 or more levels&#xA;Calls: aov ... model.matrix -&gt; model.matrix.default -&gt; contrasts&amp;lt;-&#xA;Execution halted&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there any way to write the script that will make R continue the script despite the error?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My entire script, other then the file loading, attaching, creating a sink, library loading, etc is...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;ss107927468.model&amp;lt;-aov(Race.5~ss107927468, data=snp1)&#xA;summary(ss107927468.model)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any help would be appreciated.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="531249" LastEditorUserId="21234" LastEditDate="2010-12-05T15:09:25.723" LastActivityDate="2013-02-12T20:16:00.257" Title="Is there any way to have R script continue after receiving error messages instead of halting execution?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;statistics&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
