  <row Id="4370379" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4370426" CreationDate="2010-12-06T19:55:19.780" Score="0" ViewCount="191" Body="&lt;p&gt;In the example below, I have two rows where First, Last, and Address 1/2 match. Two different email addreses but with one extra custom field. What I would like to do is systematically select the first row when presented with multiple rows that looks like this. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Lines &amp;lt;- &quot;&#xA;First, Last, Address, Address 2, Email, Custom1, Custom2, Custom3&#xA;A, B, C, D, E@E.com,1,2,3&#xA;A, B, C, D, F@G.com,1,2,&#xA;&quot;&#xA;con &amp;lt;- textConnection(Lines)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In words: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IF First &amp;amp; Last &amp;amp; Address 1 &amp;amp; Address 2 match, choose that one where custom3 is not NA. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How would I go about applying this to a large set of data?  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note: Speed is not important here, an example with plyr would be most useful. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="170352" LastActivityDate="2010-12-06T20:13:07.393" Title="Choosing a Row based on matches and NA in a different field" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
