  <row Id="4371259" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4372177" CreationDate="2010-12-06T21:46:39.370" Score="3" ViewCount="2518" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've been referred to both:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;?URLencode&#xA;#and&#xA;?curlEscape&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I see that both functions work great for English, but fail to provide with the proper translation for Hebrew characters.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, the word&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;שלום&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Peace, in Hebrew)&#xA;Should be this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;%D7%A9%D7%9C%D7%95%D7%9D&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But instead, both commands translate it to:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;URLencode(&quot;שלום&quot;)&#xA;%f9%ec%e5%ed&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What do you suggest?  (write it myself, or is there something pre-made)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks, &#xA;Tal&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Update: My sessionInfo:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; sessionInfo()&#xA;R version 2.12.0 (2010-10-15)&#xA;Platform: i386-pc-mingw32/i386 (32-bit)&#xA;&#xA;locale:&#xA;[1] LC_COLLATE=Hebrew_Israel.1255  LC_CTYPE=Hebrew_Israel.1255   &#xA;[3] LC_MONETARY=Hebrew_Israel.1255 LC_NUMERIC=C                  &#xA;[5] LC_TIME=Hebrew_Israel.1255    &#xA;&#xA;attached base packages:&#xA;[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="256662" LastEditorUserId="256662" LastEditDate="2010-12-07T08:34:41.553" LastActivityDate="2010-12-07T15:15:53.100" Title="Hebrew &quot;URL Encoding&quot; in R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;urlencode&gt;&lt;url-encoding&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="54683" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="54695" CreationDate="2008-09-10T16:56:37.647" Score="22" ViewCount="23118" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm not even sure if it's possible but say I have some XML:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &amp;lt;source&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;list&amp;gt;&#xA;            &amp;lt;element id=&quot;1&quot;/&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;/list&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/source&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And I would like to insert into list:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;element id=&quot;2&quot;/&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can I write an XSLT to do this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4968" OwnerDisplayName="warsze" LastEditorUserId="1987598" LastEditorDisplayName="Brian Warshaw" LastEditDate="2014-03-21T16:08:10.837" LastActivityDate="2014-03-21T16:08:10.837" Title="How Do You Insert XML Into an existing XML node" Tags="&lt;xml&gt;&lt;xslt&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="7" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
