  <row Id="54836" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="54841" CreationDate="2008-09-10T17:48:49.877" Score="5" ViewCount="903" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working on some code that uses the System.Diagnostics.Trace class and I'm wondering how to monitor what is written via calls to Trace.WriteLine() both when running in debug mode in Visual Studio and when running outside the debugger.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="327" OwnerDisplayName="Luke" LastEditorUserId="303" LastEditorDisplayName="NotMyself" LastEditDate="2008-09-10T17:50:43.257" LastActivityDate="2008-09-17T19:42:45.007" Title="How can I monitor trace output of a .Net app?" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;windows&gt;&lt;visual-studio&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4377507" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4377792" CreationDate="2010-12-07T14:11:25.883" Score="0" ViewCount="261" Body="&lt;p&gt;Here is the code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;require(&quot;quantmod&quot;)&#xA;&#xA;getSymbols(&quot;GLD&quot;) &#xA;getSymbols(&quot;SLV&quot;)&#xA;getSymbols(&quot;TLT&quot;)&#xA;&#xA;GSR = GLD/SLV&#xA;&#xA;par(mfrow=c(2,2))&#xA;&#xA;chartSeries (GLD, subset=&quot;2010&quot;, TA = NULL)               &#xA;chartSeries (SLV, subset=&quot;2010&quot;, TA = NULL)               &#xA;chartSeries (TLT, subset=&quot;2010&quot;, TA = NULL)               &#xA;chartSeries (GSR, subset=&quot;2010&quot;, TA = NULL)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When I run this file from TextMate with the Command R keystroke, I get four charts lined up in a 2 x 2 grid, as you'd expect from the par() function. When I source this from the R console, &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; source(&quot;~/myChartSeries.r&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I get a flash of each chart with the last one depicted alone. The last I'd heard, chartSeries() was not compliant with the par() function but chart_Series() is. So the behavior of the console is not surprising. But why does execution from TextMate work? Has chartSeries() been made par() compliant and is the R console execution flawed?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="296155" LastActivityDate="2011-08-09T18:46:48.347" Title="R quantmod package behaves differently when executed from console versus from TextMate" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;console&gt;&lt;textmate&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="5" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
