  <row Id="4430763" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-12-13T16:03:26.477" Score="1" ViewCount="267" Body="&lt;p&gt;Does anyone know of an XPath expression which will allow me to extract all the search results returned from baidu.com?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For example, in R, I would usually do something like this this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;# load libraries    &#xA;library(RCurl)&#xA;library(XML)&#xA;&#xA;# get webpage&#xA;doc &amp;lt;- getURL(&quot;http://www.baidu.com/s?rn=100&amp;amp;bs=chivas+regal&amp;amp;f=8&amp;amp;wd=chivas+regal&quot;)&#xA;&#xA;# html structure&#xA;html &amp;lt;- htmlTreeParse(doc, useInternalNodes = TRUE, error=function(...){})&#xA;&#xA;# use xpath expression to get links&#xA;nodes &amp;lt;- getNodeSet(html, &quot;//a[@href]&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However this only gets about 10 links, when I should have around 100. So I think this means there is something about the baidu html structure which is not clear to me.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Many thanks in advance for your time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="385607" LastEditorDisplayName="user357812" LastEditDate="2010-12-13T16:20:27.907" LastActivityDate="2010-12-13T20:19:16.327" Title="XPath expression to extract weblinks from a chinese search (baidu.com)" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;xpath&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
