  <row Id="55752" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-11T03:23:30.993" Score="3" ViewCount="456" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a very large cascading menu system with over 300 items in it. &lt;em&gt;(I know it's large but it's a requirement.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Currently, it's written in javascript so the external file is cached by browsers.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To improve search engine results I need to convert this to a css menu system.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;I realize the browsers will also cache external stylesheets but, &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;is there a way to cache the menu content (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tags)?  &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If I use javascript (&lt;code&gt;document.write&lt;/code&gt;) to write the content I could have this in an external javascript file, which would be cached locally, but,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;would this be search engine friendly?  &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is the best solution?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4888" OwnerDisplayName="Geri Langlois" LastEditorUserId="1537726" LastEditDate="2015-09-09T10:02:40.893" LastActivityDate="2015-09-09T10:02:40.893" Title="What is the best way to cache a menu system locally, in the browser?" Tags="&lt;css&gt;&lt;menu&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
