  <row Id="56303" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-11T11:27:45.200" Score="17" ViewCount="109279" Body="&lt;p&gt;I need to specify a date value in a sybase where clause. For example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;select * &#xA;from data&#xA;where dateVal &amp;lt; [THE DATE]&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3512" OwnerDisplayName="cmsherratt" LastEditorUserId="1135954" LastEditDate="2012-09-03T13:02:34.560" LastActivityDate="2018-09-15T12:02:41.300" Title="How to convert a string to a date in sybase" Tags="&lt;sybase&gt;&lt;type-conversion&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="10" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56313" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56338" CreationDate="2008-09-11T11:32:16.513" Score="8" ViewCount="5469" Body="&lt;p&gt;ReSharper Code cleanup feature (with &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.jetbrains.com/resharper/features/code_formatting.html#Reordering_Type_Members_C#_only&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;reorder members&lt;/a&gt;&quot; and &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.jetbrains.com/resharper/features/code_formatting.html#Code_Style_Configuration_and_Sharing&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;reformat code&lt;/a&gt;&quot; enabled) is really great. You define a layout template using XML, then a simple key combination reorganizes your whole source file (or folder/project/solution) according to the rules you set in the template.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Anyway, do you think that could be a problem regarding VCS like subversion, cvs, git, etc. ? Is there a chance that it causes many undesired conflicts ?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4687" OwnerDisplayName="Romain Verdier" LastActivityDate="2010-03-23T13:51:06.897" Title="ReSharper Code Cleanup/Reformat Code feature vs Versioning Control Systems" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;version-control&gt;&lt;resharper&gt;" AnswerCount="9" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
