  <row Id="56446" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-11T12:44:49.303" Score="13" ViewCount="5373" Body="&lt;p&gt;Although perhaps a bizare thing to want to do, I need to create an Array in .Net with a lower bound &gt; 0. This at first seems to be possible, using:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Array.CreateInstance(typeof(Object), new int[] {2}, new int[] {9});&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Produces the desired results (an array of objects with a lower bound set to 9). However the created array instance can no longer be passed to other methods expecting &lt;code&gt;Object[]&lt;/code&gt; giving me an error saying that:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.Object[*]&lt;/code&gt; can not be cast into a &lt;code&gt;System.Object[]&lt;/code&gt;. What is this difference in array types and how can I overcome this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: test code = &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Object x = Array.CreateInstance(typeof(Object), new int[] {2}, new int[] {9});&#xA;Object[] y = (Object[])x;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Which fails with: &quot;Unable to cast object of type 'System.Object[*]' to type 'System.Object[]'.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would also like to note that this approach &lt;strong&gt;DOES&lt;/strong&gt; work when using multiple dimensions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Object x = Array.CreateInstance(typeof(Object), new int[] {2,2}, new int[] {9,9});&#xA;Object[,] y = (Object[,])x;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Which works fine.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1111" OwnerDisplayName="DAC" LastEditorUserId="1111" LastEditorDisplayName="DAC" LastEditDate="2008-09-11T13:17:51.067" LastActivityDate="2021-09-07T04:56:06.630" Title=".Net arrays with lower bound &gt; 0" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;arrays&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4474217" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-12-17T19:48:18.323" Score="1" ViewCount="2781" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have two dependents that both depent on two variables AND on each other, can this be modelled in R (must be!) but I can't figure out how, anyone a hint?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In clear terms:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to model my data with the following model:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Y1=X1*coef1+X2*coef2&#xA;Y2=X1*coef2+X2*coef3&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note: coef2 appears in both lines&#xA;Xi, Yi is input and output data respectively&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I got this far:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;lm(Y1~X1+X2,mydata)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;now how do I add the second line of the model including the cross dependency?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your help is greatly appreciated!&#xA;Cheers, Bastiaan&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="546465" LastActivityDate="2010-12-21T02:05:00.470" Title="multivariate regression" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;model&gt;&lt;regression&gt;&lt;linear-regression&gt;&lt;lm&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56472" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61947" CreationDate="2008-09-11T12:53:42.573" Score="11" ViewCount="3599" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to send messages to Objective-C objects in gdb.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;(gdb) p $esi&#xA;$2 = (void *) 0x1268160&#xA;(gdb) po $esi&#xA;&amp;lt;NSArray: 0x1359c0&amp;gt;&#xA;(gdb) po [$esi count]&#xA;Target does not respond to this message selector.&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I can't send any message to it. Am I missing something? Do I really need the symbols, or something else?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5577" OwnerDisplayName="asksol" LastEditorUserId="5299236" LastEditorDisplayName="Bill the Lizard" LastEditDate="2015-12-14T01:37:10.437" LastActivityDate="2015-12-14T01:37:10.437" Title="Sending messages to objects while debugging Objective-C in gdb, without symbols" Tags="&lt;objective-c&gt;&lt;debugging&gt;&lt;macos&gt;&lt;gdb&gt;&lt;reversing&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56478" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56493" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:02:32.367" Score="9" ViewCount="65947" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am looking for a way to interact with a standalone full version of Windows Media Player.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Mostly I need to know the Path of the currently played track.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The iTunes SDK makes this really easy but unfortunately there really isn't any way to do it with Windows Media Player, at least not in .Net(C#) without any heavy use of pinvoke, which I am not really comfortable with.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Just to clearify: I don't want to embedded a new instance of Windows Media Player in my app, but instead control/read the &quot;real&quot; full version of Windows Media Player, started seperatly by the user&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5798" LastEditorUserId="5798" LastEditorDisplayName="oreon" LastEditDate="2008-09-25T20:17:42.847" LastActivityDate="2020-06-11T06:07:56.647" Title="How to interact with Windows Media Player in C#" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;windows&gt;&lt;media&gt;&lt;wmp&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="17" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56479" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56489" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:02:52.507" Score="7" ViewCount="812" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm working with my ASP.NET development team to try and create &quot;better&quot; &lt;em&gt;(i.e. cleaner)&lt;/em&gt; HTML when rendering pages.  At the moment, .NET has a nasty tendency to do things like dump JavaScript into the page, making it a mandatory requirement on form controls and not allowing forms to work when JS isn't available.  In some instances, we're struggling to overcome this without having to add a notable chunk to development time estimates.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've worked with MVC before - via Struts in Java - and found that in that instance, I was able to keep HTML pages exactly as I'd wanted them to be. &lt;em&gt;(This viewpoint is based on the &quot;best case&quot; static HTML I typically developed beforehand, then handed over to the Java programmers to fill in the holes.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This worked out really well and we were able to produce some of the &quot;best&quot; web pages from a CMS that I've seen.  Could .NET MVC give me the separation I need, or would it be a false economy to put aside valuable development time to test this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If .NET MVC isn't going to give me this fine-grained control over separation, any recommendations for .NET coding practices, libraries, etc. which might would be really helpful.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3212" OwnerDisplayName="Wrestlevania" LastEditorUserId="7750640" LastEditDate="2017-06-25T10:01:11.920" LastActivityDate="2017-06-25T10:01:11.920" Title="Will .NET MVC give me the HTML/CSS/JS separation I need?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;css&gt;&lt;asp.net-mvc&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56500" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56514" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:15:18.810" Score="8" ViewCount="6659" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm stuck on a fix to a legacy Visual C++ 6 app. In the C++ DLL source I have put&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;extern &quot;C&quot; _declspec(dllexport) char* MyNewVariable = 0;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;which results in MyNewVariable showing up (nicely undecorated) in the export table (as shown by dumpbin /exports blah.dll). However, I can't figure out how to declare the variable so that I can access it in a C source file. I have tried various things, including&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;_declspec(dllimport) char* MyNewVariable;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but that just gives me a linker error:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;unresolved external symbol &quot;__declspec(dllimport) char * MyNewVariable&quot; (__imp_?MyNewVariable@@3PADA)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;extern &quot;C&quot; _declspec(dllimport) char* MyNewVariable;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;as suggested by Tony (and as I tried before) results in a different expected decoration, but still hasn't removed it:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;unresolved external symbol __imp__MyNewVariable&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do I write the declaration so that the C++ DLL variable is accessible from the C app?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2&gt;The Answer&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As identified by botismarius and others (many thanks to all), I needed to link with the DLL's .lib. To prevent the name being mangled I needed to declare it (in the C source) with no decorators, which means I needed to use the .lib file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5816" LastEditorUserId="500584" LastEditorDisplayName="Ian Horwill" LastEditDate="2011-09-29T14:59:07.383" LastActivityDate="2012-06-28T12:36:42.467" Title="Can't access variable in C++ DLL from a C app" Tags="&lt;c++&gt;&lt;c&gt;&lt;interop&gt;&lt;name-decoration&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56518" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56539" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:25:20.563" Score="52" ViewCount="41584" Body="&lt;p&gt;In C# are the nullable primitive types (i.e. &lt;code&gt;bool?&lt;/code&gt;) just aliases for their corresponding &lt;code&gt;Nullable&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; type or is there a difference between the two?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="93" OwnerDisplayName="MojoFilter" LastEditorUserId="197229" LastEditorDisplayName="samjudson" LastEditDate="2016-07-29T11:07:07.163" LastActivityDate="2016-07-29T11:07:07.163" Title="Is there any difference between type? and Nullable&lt;type&gt;?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;nullable&gt;" AnswerCount="9" CommentCount="3" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56521" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56533" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:26:47.860" Score="2" ViewCount="1029" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a &quot;numeric textbox&quot; in C# .NET which is nothing more than a derivation of Textbox, with some added logic to prevent the user entering anything non-numeric. As part of this, I have added a Value property of type &lt;code&gt;double?&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;Nullable&amp;lt;double&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;). It's nullable to support the case where the user doesn't enter anything.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The control works fine when run, but the Windows Forms designer doesn't seem to like dealing with it much. When the control is added to a form, the following line of code is generated in InitializeComponent():&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;this.numericTextBox1.Value = 1;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Remember 'Value' is of type &lt;code&gt;Nullable&amp;lt;double&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. This generates the following warning whenever I try to reopen the form in the Designer:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Object of type 'System.Int32' cannot be converted to type 'System.Nullable`1[System.Double]'.&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As a result, the form cannot be viewed in the Designer until I manually remove that line and rebuild - after which it's regenerated as soon as I save any changes. Annoying.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any suggestions?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerDisplayName="Angry Albatross" LastActivityDate="2012-10-04T14:35:46.543" Title="Windows Forms Designer upset by a control with a nullable property" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;winforms&gt;&lt;nullable&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56543" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56552" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:38:17.287" Score="7" ViewCount="947" Body="&lt;p&gt;A problem I ran into a while back I never found a good solution for...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Say you have a working copy checked out from subversion at revision 7500, and the disk holding the current repository dies. You've got a backup of the repository at, say, revision 7450. It's easy to restore the repository backup, but any attempt to use the working copy against it gives an error saying that revision 7500 doesn't exist in the repository.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is the best way to check in one gigantic revision to bring the content of the repository up to match the content of the working copy and get he working copy back to a functional state?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(Ideally I'd like something easier than having to check out a brand new working copy and then copying over all the files manually - I think at the time the working copies were used to configuration manage servers, so it was a real pain to have to check out clean working copies)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="797" OwnerDisplayName="Matt Sheppard" LastEditorUserId="1154" LastEditorDisplayName="Jedi Master Spooky" LastEditDate="2008-09-11T13:43:00.553" LastActivityDate="2010-07-20T22:38:35.547" Title="Recovering from a slightly out of date subversion repository backup" Tags="&lt;svn&gt;&lt;version-control&gt;&lt;backup&gt;&lt;sysadmin&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4474671" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4474711" CreationDate="2010-12-17T20:53:04.190" Score="6" ViewCount="2007" Body="&lt;p&gt;This should be an easy thing to do.  The similar examples I have read on here have been a bit more complex and the techniques are not really working for me.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a variable called id_string&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; typeof(id_string)&#xA;[1] &quot;character&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; id_string&#xA;[1] &quot;1,2,5,6,10&quot;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What I want to do is split these values out and store them in a new variable.  Such that, for example:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x[1] = 1&#xA;x[4] = 6&#xA;x[5] = 10&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried to do &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- strsplit(id_string,&quot;,&quot;) &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;to split it by comma but I just get &lt;code&gt;x = &quot;1 2 5 6 10&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I read through &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1676990/split-a-string-vector-r&quot;&gt;this post&lt;/a&gt; on here which is similar and thought that something like &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- read.csv(textConnection(id_string))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;would work but to no avail.  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Perhaps I am over thinking this.  Please let me know if you have any ideas.  Thank you.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="546497" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:22:31.300" LastActivityDate="2010-12-20T09:50:59.353" Title="R strsplit problem (easy fix?)" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4476191" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4476494" CreationDate="2010-12-18T01:56:42.677" Score="2" ViewCount="5311" Body="&lt;p&gt;Suppose we create a data.frame like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; hugs_per_day &amp;lt;- rnorm(10)&#xA;&amp;gt; hugs_per_day &amp;lt;- as.data.frame(hugs_per_day)&#xA;&amp;gt; hugs_per_day&#xA;   hugs_per_day&#xA;1  -2.500457495&#xA;2  -0.204545274&#xA;3  -0.955424927&#xA;4   0.320184701&#xA;5   1.822908001&#xA;6  -0.058679520&#xA;7  -0.276004919&#xA;8   0.175341993&#xA;9  -0.137404974&#xA;10  0.005096691&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And we want to run a function on each day to return a value based on the results, something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;nested_ifelse &amp;lt;- function(x){&#xA;&#xA;ifelse (x &amp;gt; 1,     mood &amp;lt;- &quot;happy&quot;,&#xA;    ifelse(x &amp;lt; 0,  mood &amp;lt;- &quot;sad&quot;, &#xA;                   mood &amp;lt;- &quot;same as yesterday&quot; ))&#xA;&#xA;   return(mood)&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The nested_ifelse() example does what I want and I'm sure sapply() is the correct R function to populate a new column with results from the function, but I just can't put the two together. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="296155" LastEditorUserId="296155" LastEditDate="2010-12-18T02:31:52.970" LastActivityDate="2010-12-18T03:49:53.113" Title="Nested ifelse R function passed to sapply() to create new data.frame" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4477436" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2010-12-18T09:13:08.817" Score="1" ViewCount="4355" Body="&lt;p&gt;The computer I used in office has been recently upgraded to a quad-core one, which is a blessing to me, as sometimes I need to do some explicit loops using R, which the outcomes are based one some logical rules, which I can't figure out how to work this out other than a explicit loop.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For some background information, sometimes I have about 10000-20000 rows, which I need to look at 2 column, and base on their values and some logical rules, to generate value for a new column.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am trying to use the &lt;code&gt;doSNOW&lt;/code&gt; package to better utilize the unused CPU power, I have written a demo script as below, based on the example from &lt;a href=&quot;http://decisionstats.com/2010/09/24/parallel-programming-using-r-in-windows/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library(doSNOW)&#xA;# rm(list=ls())&#xA;&#xA;cl&amp;lt;-makeCluster(2) # I have two cores&#xA;registerDoSNOW(cl)&#xA;&#xA;table &amp;lt;- data.frame(a=rnorm(1000),b=rnorm(1000))&#xA;&#xA;process &amp;lt;- function(table)&#xA;              {for (loop in (1:nrow(table)))&#xA;                   {table[loop,&quot;c&quot;] &amp;lt;- with(table[loop,], a*b)&#xA;                    assign(&quot;table&quot;,table,envir=.GlobalEnv)&#xA;                   }&#xA;              }&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;system.time(process(table))&#xA;&#xA;system.time(foreach(j=1:2 ) %dopar% process(table))&#xA;&#xA;stopCluster(cl)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am using a netbook with ATOM CPU inside to try this out, but the result is weird:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;system.time(process(table))&#xA;user  system elapsed &#xA;2.336   0.028   2.308 &#xA;&#xA;system.time(foreach(j=1:2 ) %dopar% process(table))&#xA;user  system elapsed &#xA;0.160   0.032   3.646 &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;After using doSNOW, time needed for result is even longer than without using doSNOW, I wonder if this is the problem of my ATOM netbook, or did I make anything wrong in the code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="373908" LastEditorUserId="163053" LastEditDate="2010-12-18T13:47:21.493" LastActivityDate="2011-04-04T04:57:44.030" Title="use doSNOW to speed up explicit loop in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;parallel-processing&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="5" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56546" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56578" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:40:04.880" Score="7" ViewCount="2191" Body="&lt;p&gt;Recently thanks to rails' popularity, many people start using activerecord as model. however, before I heard of rails (my peer group was not a fan of open source stuff, we were taught in a .NET school...) and while I was doing my final year project, i found this definition for a model&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;The model represents enterprise data and the business rules that govern access to and updates of this data. Often the model serves as a software approximation to a real-world process, so simple real-world modeling techniques apply when defining the model.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;it doesn't say the model should represent one table as what activerecord does. And normally within a transaction, one may have to query a few unrelated tables and then manipulate data from different tables... so if activerecord is used as model, then either one would have to cram all the logic code into the controller (which is kinda popular in some php frameworks) that makes it difficult to test or hack the activerecord model so that it performs database operation on not only the table it maps to, but also other related tables as well...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;so, what is so great about abusing (IMHO) activerecord as the model in a MVC architectural pattern?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5742" OwnerDisplayName="Jeffrey04" LastActivityDate="2010-11-24T03:00:01.270" Title="activerecord as model, is this a good idea?" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;model-view-controller&gt;&lt;activerecord&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56547" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56612" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:40:19.203" Score="133" ViewCount="59013" Body="&lt;p&gt;How do you perform a CROSS JOIN with LINQ to SQL?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5556" OwnerDisplayName="Luke Smith" LastEditorUserId="60647" LastEditorDisplayName="mwigdahl" LastEditDate="2009-03-24T20:38:12.010" LastActivityDate="2021-09-13T18:55:43.643" Title="How do you perform a CROSS JOIN with LINQ to SQL?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;linq&gt;&lt;linq-to-sql&gt;&lt;cross-join&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="14" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56553" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56952" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:42:34.237" Score="31" ViewCount="48291" Body="&lt;p&gt;I use a MacBook, but I've got a usual keyboard attached to it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The problem is that the keys don't exactly map 1-to-1. One thing is the APPLE and ALT keys. They map to WIN and ALT, but they are usually physically inverted, so if you want to use them with the same layout you have to invert them in the OS.&#xA;The Function keys work differently too. Fx on the external = Fn + Fx on the MacBook keyboard. And then there are all the insert, delete, keys.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So, the question is, how do you come around this? Now I remap all the things I want at the System Preferences panel, but when I unplug the external keyboard it's all messed up. Is there a way to remap keys only for the external one? Some model of keyboard can store it's own mappings without needing the OS? Am I the only one who is bothered by this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(I would like to avoid buying an external mac keyboard, because I wanted to try one of the ergonomic models, and as far as I know, there are no mac ergonomic models)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Update:&#xA;Thanks for the responses, I fixed this.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To set the control keys for different keyboards, you have to go to System Preferences/Modifier Keys, then the drop down menu Select Keyboard allows you to choose one particular keyboard and set these keys. Works after unpluging/pluging it seems&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The suggestion from @Matthew Schinckel seems to work for the rest of the issues (function keys, ...). I didn't try it yet, as the commands keys were my biggest gripe.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3785" OwnerDisplayName="Mario" LastEditorUserId="3785" LastEditorDisplayName="Mario" LastEditDate="2008-09-11T17:17:26.700" LastActivityDate="2008-09-11T17:17:26.700" Title="Using an external &quot;windows&quot;-keyboard under Mac OS X" Tags="&lt;macos&gt;&lt;keyboard&gt;&lt;ergonomics&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="3" ClosedDate="2012-12-01T05:03:56.707" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56554" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56671" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:42:35.157" Score="11" ViewCount="13499" Body="&lt;p&gt;Let's say I want to represent &lt;code&gt;\q&lt;/code&gt; (or any other particular &quot;backslash-escaped character&quot;).  That is, I want to match &lt;code&gt;\q&lt;/code&gt; but not &lt;code&gt;\\q&lt;/code&gt;, since the latter is a backslash-escaped backslash followed by a &lt;code&gt;q&lt;/code&gt;.  Yet &lt;code&gt;\\\q&lt;/code&gt; would match, since it's a backslash-escaped backslash followed by a backslash-escaped &lt;code&gt;q&lt;/code&gt;.  (Well, it would match the &lt;code&gt;\q&lt;/code&gt; at the end, not the &lt;code&gt;\\&lt;/code&gt; at the beginning.)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I know I need a negative lookbehind, but they always tie my head up in knots, especially since the backslashes themselves have to be escaped in the regexp.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1190" OwnerDisplayName="Gaius" LastEditorUserId="1190" LastEditorDisplayName="Gaius" LastEditDate="2008-09-11T13:48:09.963" LastActivityDate="2019-09-04T11:58:28.410" Title="What is the proper regular expression for an unescaped backslash before a character?" Tags="&lt;regex&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56561" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56694" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:45:30.827" Score="45" ViewCount="68323" Body="&lt;p&gt;What is the approved way to convert from char* to System::string and back in C++/CLI? I found a few references to marshal_to&amp;lt;&gt; templated functions on Google, but it appears that this feature never made the cut for Visual Studio 2005 (and isn't in Visual Studio 2008 either, AFAIK). I have also seen some code on &lt;a href=&quot;http://blogs.msdn.com/slippman/archive/2004/06/02/147090.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Stan Lippman's blog&lt;/a&gt;, but it's from 2004. I have also seen Marshal::StringToHGlobalAnsi(). Is there a method that is considered &quot;best practice&quot;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3114" OwnerDisplayName="Brian" LastEditorUserId="3204551" LastEditDate="2015-03-09T12:47:23.103" LastActivityDate="2017-10-06T23:18:06.030" Title="What is the best way to convert between char* and System::String in C++/CLI" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;string&gt;&lt;c++-cli&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="17" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56568" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="201180" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:48:27.873" Score="7" ViewCount="3629" Body="&lt;p&gt;How do you actually perform datetime operations such as adding date, finding difference, find out how many days excluding weekends in an interval? I personally started to pass some of these operations to my postgresql dbms as typically I would only need to issue one sql statement to obtain an answer, however, to do it in PHP way I would have to write a lot more code that means more chances for errors to occur...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are there any libraries in PHP that does datetime operation in a way that don't require a lot of code? that beats sql in a situation where 'Given two dates, how many workdays are there between the two dates? Implement in either SQL, or $pet_lang' that is solved by making this query?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;lang-sql prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SELECT  COUNT(*) AS total_days&#xA;FROM    (SELECT date '2008-8-26' + generate_series(0,&#xA;          (date '2008-9-1' - date '2008-8-26')) AS all_days) AS calendar&#xA;WHERE   EXTRACT(isodow FROM all_days) &amp;lt; 6;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5742" OwnerDisplayName="Jeffrey04" LastEditorDisplayName="user289086" LastEditDate="2014-04-02T14:31:56.730" LastActivityDate="2019-05-29T22:18:22.417" Title="performing datetime related operations in PHP" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;sql&gt;&lt;postgresql&gt;&lt;datetime&gt;" AnswerCount="12" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56574" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56617" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:50:00.020" Score="12" ViewCount="593" Body="&lt;p&gt;A while back I was reading the W3C article on '&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.w3.org/International/articles/text-reuse/&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Re-using Strings in Scripted Content&lt;/a&gt;', which contains some useful advice on internationalisation, but which strikes me as at odds iwth the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle of eliminating repetitive code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To take their example, we might have some code like this...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;print &quot;The printer is &quot;;&#xA;if (printer.working) {&#xA;    print &quot;on.\n&quot;;&#xA;} else {&#xA;    print &quot;off.\n&quot;;&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;print &quot;The stapler is &quot;;&#xA;if (stapler.working) {&#xA;    print &quot;on.\n&quot;;&#xA;} else {&#xA;    print &quot;off.\n&quot;;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My instinct would be to eliminate the repetition roughly as follows...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;report-state(printer, &quot;printer&quot;);&#xA;report-state(stapler, &quot;stapler&quot;);&#xA;&#xA;function report-state(name, object) {&#xA;    print &quot;The &quot;+name+&quot; is &quot;;&#xA;    if (object.working) {&#xA;        print &quot;on\n&quot;;&#xA;    } else {&#xA;        print &quot;off\n&quot;;&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;...but doing so would cause a difficulty in the code if we needed to localise it to Spanish because the word for 'on' is apparently different in those two cases.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So, I guess my question is, how have other developers approached balancing the DRY principle with internationalisation of their code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Part of me wants to argue that internationalisation is one of those extreme programming “&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.extremeprogramming.org/rules/early.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;you arent gonna need it&lt;/a&gt;” situations. On the flip side however, refactoring with the DRY principle in mind is supposed to balance this by making it easy to implement functionality as it’s required, not harder as it does here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="797" OwnerDisplayName="Matt Sheppard" LastEditorUserId="3827" LastEditorDisplayName="eed3si9n" LastEditDate="2008-09-13T20:42:48.233" LastActivityDate="2008-09-19T16:48:33.120" Title="Don't repeat yourself vs Internationalisation" Tags="&lt;internationalization&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56589" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56749" CreationDate="2008-09-11T13:53:31.573" Score="1" ViewCount="838" Body="&lt;p&gt;Does a new &lt;code&gt;SessionFactor&lt;/code&gt;y and &lt;code&gt;Session&lt;/code&gt; object have to be created for each database? I have a data store for my application data, and a separate data store for my employee security, which is used to validate users. Do I have to create a new SessionFactory ans Session object for calls to the 2 different databases?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1284" OwnerDisplayName="Mark Struzinski" LastEditorUserId="5423108" LastEditDate="2017-07-04T10:01:48.020" LastActivityDate="2017-07-16T14:21:49.520" Title="Can you query different databases on the same server using 1 NHibernate Session?" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;nhibernate&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="4477638" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4479478" CreationDate="2010-12-18T10:20:02.177" Score="5" ViewCount="14216" Body="&lt;p&gt;How to grep with &lt;code&gt;fixed=T&lt;/code&gt;, but only at the beginning of the string?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;grep(&quot;a.&quot;, c(&quot;a.b&quot;, &quot;cac&quot;, &quot;sss&quot;, &quot;ca.f&quot;), fixed = T)&#xA;# 1 4&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would like to get only the first occurrence. &#xA;[Edit: the string to match is not known in advance, and can be anything. &quot;a.&quot; is just for the sake of example]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[Edit: I sort of solved it now, but any other ideas are highly welcome. I will accept as an answer any alternative solution.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;s &amp;lt;- &quot;a.&quot;&#xA;res &amp;lt;- grep(s, c(&quot;a.b&quot;, &quot;cac&quot;, &quot;sss&quot;, &quot;ca.f&quot;), fixed = T, value = T)&#xA;res[substring(res, 1, nchar(s)) == s]&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="453735" LastEditorUserId="10248678" LastEditDate="2020-08-14T10:05:02.387" LastActivityDate="2020-08-14T10:05:02.387" Title="grep at the beginning of the string with fixed =T in R?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;regex&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4480049" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4480613" CreationDate="2010-12-18T20:38:43.643" Score="2" ViewCount="599" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have written a program that works with the 3n + 1 problem (aka &quot;wondrous numbers&quot; and various other things).  But it has a double loop.  How could I vectorize it?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;the code is&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;count &amp;lt;- vector(&quot;numeric&quot;, 100000)&#xA;L &amp;lt;- length(count)&#xA;&#xA;for (i in 1:L)&#xA;{&#xA;x &amp;lt;- i&#xA;   while (x &amp;gt; 1)&#xA;   {&#xA;   if (round(x/2) == x/2) &#xA;     {&#xA;     x &amp;lt;- x/2&#xA;     count[i] &amp;lt;- count[i] + 1 &#xA;     } else&#xA;     {&#xA;     x &amp;lt;- 3*x + 1&#xA;     count[i] &amp;lt;- count[i] + 1&#xA;     }&#xA;   }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="228220" LastActivityDate="2010-12-20T08:49:51.260" Title="Advice wanted on getting rid of loops" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;loops&gt;&lt;vectorization&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
