  <row Id="4494861" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4495071" CreationDate="2010-12-20T23:03:12.973" Score="1" ViewCount="329" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have the following function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;library (reshape)&#xA;phenotype &amp;lt;- rnorm (100)&#xA;data &amp;lt;- matrix(rnorm(1000), nrow = 10, ncol=100)&#xA;&#xA;spearman.p &amp;lt;-&#xA;             reshape(&#xA;                     melt(&#xA;                          apply(data, 1, function(y){&#xA;                                        cor.test(y,phenotype,method=&quot;spearman&quot;)&#xA;                                                    }[c(&quot;p.value&quot;, &quot;estimate&quot;)]&#xA;                               )&#xA;                          ), timevar=&quot;L2&quot;, idvar=&quot;L1&quot;, direction=&quot;wide&quot;&#xA;                       )&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;that I would like to know if there is a more efficent way of getting out the p.value and estimate from a &quot;apply&quot;ed cor.test&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can anyone provide some suggestions?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerDisplayName="please delete me" LastEditorDisplayName="please delete me" LastEditDate="2010-12-23T20:22:44.283" LastActivityDate="2010-12-23T20:22:44.283" Title="Optimizing apply function output" Tags="&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
