  <row Id="56729" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="58180" CreationDate="2008-09-11T14:43:18.550" Score="4" ViewCount="1912" Body="&lt;p&gt;Can somebody give me a complete and working example of calling the &lt;code&gt;AllocateAndInitializeSid&lt;/code&gt; function from C# code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I found &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/aa375213(VS.85).aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;this&lt;/a&gt;:  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;BOOL WINAPI AllocateAndInitializeSid(&#xA;  __in   PSID_IDENTIFIER_AUTHORITY pIdentifierAuthority,&#xA;  __in   BYTE nSubAuthorityCount,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority0,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority1,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority2,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority3,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority4,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority5,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority6,&#xA;  __in   DWORD dwSubAuthority7,&#xA;  __out  PSID *pSid&#xA;);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and I don't know how to construct the signature of this method - what should I do with &lt;code&gt;PSID_IDENTIFIER_AUTHORITY&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;PSID&lt;/code&gt; types? How should I pass them - using &lt;code&gt;ref&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;out&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="95" OwnerDisplayName="chopeen" LastEditorUserId="95" LastEditDate="2011-05-05T05:03:03.173" LastActivityDate="2011-05-05T05:03:03.173" Title="How to call the AllocateAndInitializeSid function from C#?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;winapi&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56737" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56815" CreationDate="2008-09-11T14:45:40.090" Score="27" ViewCount="13661" Body="&lt;p&gt;Is the standard Java 1.6 &lt;a href=&quot;http://java.sun.com/javase/6/docs/api/javax/xml/parsers/DocumentBuilder.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder&lt;/a&gt; class thread safe? Is it safe to call the parse() method from several threads in parallel?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The JavaDoc doesn't mention the issue, but the &lt;a href=&quot;http://java.sun.com/j2se/1.4.2/docs/api/javax/xml/parsers/DocumentBuilder.html&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;JavaDoc for the same class&lt;/a&gt; in Java 1.4 specifically says that it &lt;em&gt;isn't&lt;/em&gt; meant to be concurrent; so can I assume that in 1.6 it is?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The reason is that I have several million tasks running in an ExecutorService, and it seems expensive to call DocumentBuilderFactory.newDocumentBuilder() every time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1605" OwnerDisplayName="Avi" LastEditorUserId="543969" LastEditorDisplayName="Avi" LastEditDate="2012-11-15T03:18:09.543" LastActivityDate="2014-03-05T16:35:40.167" Title="Is DocumentBuilder.parse() thread safe?" Tags="&lt;java&gt;&lt;thread-safety&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="8" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
