  <row Id="56974" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56987" CreationDate="2008-09-11T15:58:55.030" Score="209" ViewCount="84162" Body="&lt;p&gt;In the following snippet:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;public class a {&#xA;    public void otherMethod(){}&#xA;    public void doStuff(String str, InnerClass b){}&#xA;    public void method(a){&#xA;        doStuff(&quot;asd&quot;,&#xA;            new InnerClass(){&#xA;                public void innerMethod(){&#xA;                    otherMethod();&#xA;                }&#xA;            }&#xA;        );&#xA;    }&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there a keyword to refer to the outer class from the inner class?  Basically what I want to do is &lt;code&gt;outer.otherMethod()&lt;/code&gt;, or something of the like, but can't seem to find anything.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="292" OwnerDisplayName="shs" LastEditorUserId="3453226" LastEditorDisplayName="Ryan Farley" LastEditDate="2015-09-17T16:31:52.297" LastActivityDate="2015-09-17T16:31:52.297" Title="Keyword for the outer class from an anonymous inner class" Tags="&lt;java&gt;&lt;anonymous-inner-class&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="43" ClosedDate="2017-02-15T21:50:48.833" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="56975" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="56988" CreationDate="2008-09-11T15:59:06.683" Score="5" ViewCount="2807" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm currently looping through a datareader and calling the System.Net.Mail.SmtpClient's Send() method. The problem with this is that it's slow. Each email takes about 5-10 seconds to send (it's possible this is just an issue with my host). I had to override the executionTimeout default in my web.config file (it defaults to 90 seconds) like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; &amp;lt;httpRuntime executionTimeout=&quot;3000&quot; /&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One caveat: I'm on a shared host, so I don't think it is possible for me to send using the PickupDirectoryFromIis option (at least, it gave me errors when I turned it on).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4965" OwnerDisplayName="amdfan" LastActivityDate="2008-09-11T16:10:32.757" Title="What is the best way to send large batches of emails in ASP.NET?" Tags="&lt;asp.net&gt;&lt;email&gt;&lt;batch-file&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="56981" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-11T16:01:03.810" Score="1" ViewCount="2581" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm creating a web site where all pages hang off a database-driven tree-hierarchy.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;All but one node has a parent node.  Nodes may have role-based read permissions.  Some nodes may have special rules (such as: don't display within navigation menus).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Nodes may represent links to other nodes (like a shortcut in Windows).  Nodes typically represent pages.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pages present either HTML content or &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56770/dynamic-navigation-and-web-applications&quot;&gt;execute programming&lt;/a&gt;.  Some pages may be roots of subtrees (alternate masterpages and stylesheets).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please help me setup my nodes database in Microsoft SQL Server for use by Linq to SQL.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've got three ideas:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many lightweight tables with almost&#xA;zero nullalbe fields.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/Fze57.gif&quot; alt=&quot;#1 Many lightweight tables with almost zero nullalbe fields&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Heavyweight Node table with lots of&#xA;nullalbe fields.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/Yf5Gn.gif&quot; alt=&quot;#2 Heavyweight Node table with lots of nullalbe fields&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Best (or worst) of both: Lots of&#xA;nullalbe foreign keys to many&#xA;lightweight tables.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.stack.imgur.com/8xc8W.gif&quot; alt=&quot;#3 Lots of nullalbe foreign keys to many lightweight tables&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Which do you feel best represents the data?  Which will be easiest to use with Linq to SQL?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can I keep my data integrity rules within the database?  How do I best enforce them within my programming?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nodes must be either (but not both)&#xA;links or pages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pages must be either (but not both) html or code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Links may not be roots, html, nor code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can I make an ASP.NET Site Map Provider with such a structure?  Should I?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Update: I've asked a more general question:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56770/dynamic-navigation-and-web-applications&quot;&gt;What’s the best way to handle one-to-one relationships in SQL?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Related question:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/86181/how-do-i-enforce-data-integrity-rules-in-my-database&quot;&gt;How do I enforce data integrity rules in my database?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="83" OwnerDisplayName="Zack" LastEditorUserId="4751173" LastEditorDisplayName="Zack" LastEditDate="2018-12-28T07:45:08.063" LastActivityDate="2018-12-28T07:45:08.063" Title="Which is the best database schema for my navigation?" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;sql&gt;&lt;database&gt;&lt;linq-to-sql&gt;&lt;database-design&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2020-09-16T18:30:39.690" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
