  <row Id="4651428" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4651761" CreationDate="2011-01-10T20:56:27.877" Score="13" ViewCount="38217" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm using the following data structure to try and make a stacked area chart:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;df &amp;lt;- data.frame(PopDen = c( 0.002279892, 0.002885407, 0.004291351, 0.002457731, 0.006631572, 0.007578882, 0.004465446, 0.007436628, 0.009001456, 0.006951703, 0.003602076, 0.005695585, 0.005819783, 0.007412274, 0.004931548, 0.006257411, 0.008635908, 0.005438558, 0.002251421,0.006438558), DomArea = c( 253500, 135270, 197180, 131590, 142210, 166920, 125640, 184600, 139940, 126280, 127760, 190940, 133440, 143510, 117260, 69340, 143620, 127480, 181970,164180), PR_Cat = c( &quot;High&quot;, &quot;High&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;High&quot;, &quot;High&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, &quot;Medium&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;, &quot;Low&quot;,&quot;Low&quot;) )&#xA;&#xA;p &amp;lt;- ggplot(df, aes(PopDen, order(DomArea), colour = PR_Cat))  &#xA;p + geom_area(aes(colour = PR_Cat, fill= PR_Cat), position = 'stack')&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, I don't understand how to stack the areas on top of each other; at the moment they are overlapping. I assume that I need a &lt;code&gt;position = 'stack'&lt;/code&gt; argument here, but the plot looks the same whether it is included or not.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Also, is it possible to order &lt;code&gt;DomArea&lt;/code&gt; by one of the categories in &lt;code&gt;PR_Cat&lt;/code&gt;or would I need to reorganize my data?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="258755" LastEditorUserId="258755" LastEditDate="2011-01-10T21:25:40.173" LastActivityDate="2011-01-10T22:43:59.760" Title="Making a stacked area plot using ggplot2" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount=