  <row Id="58757" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="58775" CreationDate="2008-09-12T11:45:38.830" Score="4" ViewCount="750" Body="&lt;p&gt;We are currently developing a server whereby a client requests interest in changes to specific data elements and when that data changes the server pushes the data back to the client. There has vigorous debate at work about whether or not it would be better for the client to poll for this data. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is considered to be the ideal method, in terms of performance, scalability and network load, of data transfer in a near real time environment? &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;Here's a &lt;a href=&quot;http://ayende.com/Blog/archive/2009/02/16/pull-vs.-push-models-for-ui-updates.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt; that gives some food for thought with regards to UI updates.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="6065" LastEditorUserId="6065" LastEditorDisplayName="Darren" LastEditDate="2009-02-17T01:19:52.120" LastActivityDate="2009-02-17T01:19:52.120" Title="Push or Pull for a near real time automation server?" Tags="&lt;performance&gt;&lt;automation&gt;&lt;networking&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="58768" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="58772" CreationDate="2008-09-12T11:56:26.853" Score="1" ViewCount="691" Body="&lt;p&gt;I need to add DVD writing functionality to an application I'm working on. However it needs to be able to write out files that are being grabbed &quot;live&quot; from a camera, over a long period of time. I can't wait until all the files are captured before I start writing them to the DVD, I need to write them out in chunks as I go along.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've looked at &lt;a href=&quot;http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/aa364806(VS.85).aspx&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;IMAPI v2&lt;/a&gt;, but the main problems seems to be that you need to point it to all the files you plan to write out to disk before you start the burning process. I know it has to concept of &quot;sessions&quot;, which means you can write to the DVD in several parts, before you finally &quot;close&quot; it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I was wondering if there were any other DVD writing SDK's that allow you to be constantly writing files to a DVD and in particular files that are only in memory. It would be more efficient if I didn't have to write the captured images out to hard before they are burned to DVD.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The solution needs to work under .NET on Windows XP and vista&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4500" OwnerDisplayName="matt" LastActivityDate="2013-11-16T17:38:56.653" Title="SDK for writing DVD's" Tags="&lt;.net&gt;&lt;sdk&gt;&lt;image-capture&gt;&lt;dvd-burning&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2018-07-02T23:58:58.613" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
