  <row Id="59166" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="59172" CreationDate="2008-09-12T14:45:45.697" Score="43" ViewCount="33033" Body="&lt;p&gt;So I have an object which has some fields, doesn't really matter what.&#xA;I have a generic list of these objects.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;List&amp;lt;MyObject&amp;gt; myObjects = new List&amp;lt;MyObject&amp;gt;();&#xA;myObjects.Add(myObject1);&#xA;myObjects.Add(myObject2);&#xA;myObjects.Add(myObject3);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So I want to remove objects from my list based on some criteria.&#xA;For instance, &lt;code&gt;myObject.X &amp;gt;= 10.&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;I would like to use the &lt;code&gt;RemoveAll(Predicate&amp;lt;T&amp;gt; match)&lt;/code&gt; method for to do this.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I know I can define a delegate which can be passed into RemoveAll, but I would like to know how to define this inline with an anonymous delegate, instead of creating a bunch of delegate functions which are only used in once place.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="454247" OwnerDisplayName="Curtis" LastEditorUserId="4298200" LastEditorDisplayName="aku" LastEditDate="2020-08-19T23:50:30.940" LastActivityDate="2020-08-19T23:56:11.587" Title="How do you declare a Predicate Delegate inline?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;delegates&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="13" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="59175" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-12T14:49:12.553" Score="19" ViewCount="3509" Body="&lt;p&gt;What's the difference between the inner workings of Java's JVM and .NET's CLR?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Perhaps a starting point would be, are they basically the same thing in their respective environments (Java &gt; JVM &gt; Machine code) (C# &gt; CLR &gt; IL).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt;  Several people have alluded to the points I was trying to cover:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Garbage Collection &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Boxing/Unboxing&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;JIT debugging &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Generics/Templates&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Please feel free to suggest other good topics that differentiate the two.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/users/5056/george-mauer&quot;&gt;@George Mauer&lt;/a&gt; - this sounds very interesting:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Already posted this once but here is a &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.artima.com/intv/anders.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;series of interviews&lt;/a&gt; with c# chief language designer Anders Hejlsberg. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4575" OwnerDisplayName="SteveDuitsman" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditorDisplayName="Steve Duitsman" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T10:29:36.727" LastActivityDate="2013-04-07T11:47:05.337" Title="What's the difference between the inner workings of Java's JVM and .NET's CLR?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;java&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;clr&gt;&lt;jvm&gt;" AnswerCount="8" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
