  <row Id="59380" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-12T15:50:38.023" Score="5" ViewCount="2118" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a wildcard subdomain enabled and dynamically parse the URL by passing it as-is to my &lt;code&gt;index.php&lt;/code&gt; (ex. &lt;code&gt;somecity.domain.com&lt;/code&gt;).  &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, I wish to create a few subdomains that are static where I can install different application and not co-mingle with my current one (ex. &lt;code&gt;blog.domain.com&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My &lt;code&gt;.htaccess&lt;/code&gt; currently reads:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;RewriteEngine On&#xA;RewriteBase /&#xA;RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f&#xA;RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d&#xA;RewriteRule . /index.php [L]&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can I manipulate this &lt;code&gt;.htaccess&lt;/code&gt; to achieve what I need? Can it be done through Apache?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="6140" OwnerDisplayName="GiladG" LastEditorUserId="367456" LastEditorDisplayName="GiladG" LastEditDate="2011-11-13T14:40:44.873" LastActivityDate="2018-04-04T12:33:52.970" Title="Wildcard Subdomain Exceptions" Tags="&lt;php&gt;&lt;apache&gt;&lt;.htaccess&gt;&lt;wildcard-subdomain&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="59390" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="59554" CreationDate="2008-09-12T15:57:04.857" Score="5" ViewCount="1706" Body="&lt;p&gt;In a ColdFusion Component (CFC), is it necessary to use fully qualified names for variables-scoped variables?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Am I going to get myself into trouble if I change this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;cfcomponent&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;cfset variables.foo = &quot;a private instance variable&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;cffunction name = &quot;doSomething&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;cfset var bar = &quot;a function local variable&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;cfreturn &quot;I have #variables.foo# and #bar#.&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/cffunction&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/cfcomponent&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;to this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;cfcomponent&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;cfset foo = &quot;a private instance variable&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &amp;lt;cffunction name = &quot;doSomething&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;cfset var bar = &quot;a function local variable&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;cfreturn &quot;I have #foo# and #bar#.&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/cffunction&amp;gt;&#xA;&amp;lt;/cfcomponent&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="437" OwnerDisplayName="Patrick McElhaney" LastEditorUserId="437" LastEditorDisplayName="Patrick McElhaney" LastEditDate="2008-09-12T20:04:58.443" LastActivityDate="2015-06-19T20:12:40.227" Title="ColdFusion: Is it safe to leave out the variables keyword in a CFC?" Tags="&lt;coldfusion&gt;&lt;cfc&gt;" AnswerCount="9" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="59392" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="59400" CreationDate="2008-09-12T15:58:19.360" Score="25" ViewCount="19777" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm a single developer looking to get off of Visual Source Safe and move to svn.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A quick search brings up several tools, but I don't see a clear winner and I can't afford to spend a lot of time testing different tools.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Has anyone done this successfully, and can recommend a method?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1204" OwnerDisplayName="Sam" LastEditorUserId="1204" LastEditorDisplayName="Sam Williamson" LastEditDate="2008-09-15T00:46:27.907" LastActivityDate="2020-07-24T10:58:47.653" Title="Best way to migrate from VSS to Subversion?" Tags="&lt;svn&gt;&lt;version-control&gt;&lt;visual-sourcesafe&gt;" AnswerCount="10" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="7" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="59396" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="867435" CreationDate="2008-09-12T16:00:23.210" Score="2" ViewCount="2563" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a Data Access Object TransactionDao.  When you call TransactionDao.Save(transaction) I would like for it to setting a transaction.IsSaved=true flag (this is a simplification the actual thing I'm trying to do is not quite so banal).  So when mocking my TransactionDao with RhinoMocks how can I indicate that it should transform its input?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Ideally I would like to write something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;Expect.Call(delegate {dao.Save(transaction);}).Override(x =&amp;gt; x.IsSaved=true);&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Does anyone know how to do this?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Though I got a hint how to do it from the answer specified below the actual type signature is off, you have to do something like this:&#xA;Because of what Mark Ingram posted, seems like the best answer, though nobody's explicitly said it, is to do this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;public delegate void FakeSave(Transaction t);&#xA;...&#xA;Expect.Call(delegate {dao.Save(t); }).Do( new FakeSave(delegate(Transaction t2) { t.IsSaved = true; }));&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5056" OwnerDisplayName="George Mauer" LastEditorUserId="5056" LastEditorDisplayName="George Mauer" LastEditDate="2008-09-12T17:36:34.197" LastActivityDate="2009-05-15T07:44:14.640" Title="Rhino Mocks: How can I mock out a method that transforms its input?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;.net&gt;&lt;rhino-mocks&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
