  <row Id="4731807" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4732247" CreationDate="2011-01-19T04:42:05.787" Score="13" ViewCount="4080" Body="&lt;p&gt;I don't have experience with Fortran, but I am trying to run a very simple loop in that language by calling it from R via the .Fortran() function. Whenever I run the last line of the R code that is pasted below, the R gui crashes and I get no result. I am interest in bringing back the vector of real values x from Fortran into R for further analysis. g is a numeric value between 0 and 1, and n an integer, and they are both supplied by the user in R.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any help would be much appreciated! Best, &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Vincent&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fortran code saved in bar.f: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;    subroutine bar(n, g, x)&#xA;&#xA;      integer n&#xA;      double precision g&#xA;      double precision x(n)&#xA;      integer i&#xA;      x(1)=1&#xA;      do 100 i = 2, n&#xA;          x(i) = x(i-1) * g + 1&#xA;  100 continue&#xA;&#xA;      end&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Compiling the DLL in Cygwin with gfortran: &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;gfortran -shared -obar.dll bar.f&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;R code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;dyn.load(&quot;d:/bar.dll&quot;)&#xA;is.loaded(&quot;bar&quot;)&#xA;.Fortran(&quot;bar&quot;, n=as.integer(15), g=as.double(5), x=as.double(rnorm(5)))&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="342331" LastActivityDate="2021-07-29T18:36:39.123" Title="R &amp; Fortran call" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;fortran&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
