  <row Id="4733182" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4733446" CreationDate="2011-01-19T08:33:31.040" Score="37" ViewCount="20893" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have a few signals sampled over time which I plot in R using continuous lines. Additionally, I would like to highlight several specific time ranges on the plot. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My current approach is to draw full-height transparent rectangles with appropriate width and horizontal position which match the time range. I think this is a good representation, as it clearly separates points inside the range from those outside of it; but are there better ones?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;And the second, practical part of the question. Now I'm plotting the signals like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;p &amp;lt;- ggplot(data=gs, mapping=aes(x=frameno, y=value, col=variable)) +&#xA;       geom_line()&#xA;p&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have tried to draw an alpha blended rectangle manually:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;p + geom_rect(aes(xmin=600, xmax=650, ymin=-3, ymax=3),&#xA;              colour=alpha(&quot;grey20&quot;, 0.5), fill.alpha=0.5)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;— but no success so far. Any hints?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="531179" LastEditorUserId="1315749" LastEditDate="2015-03-28T23:39:15.427" LastActivityDate="2015-03-28T23:39:15.427" Title="How to highlight time ranges on a plot?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;ggplot2&gt;&lt;plot&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="15" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
