  <row Id="60438" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="60449" CreationDate="2008-09-13T09:37:02.157" Score="2" ViewCount="7522" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am using jQuery. I call a JavaScript function with next html:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;a href=&quot;javascript:uncheckEl('tagVO-$id')&quot;&amp;gt;$tagname&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I would like to remove the &lt;code&gt;li&lt;/code&gt; element and I thought this would be easy with the &lt;code&gt;$(this)&lt;/code&gt; object. This is my JavaScript function:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;function uncheckEl(id) {&#xA;    $(&quot;#&quot;+id+&quot;&quot;).attr(&quot;checked&quot;,&quot;&quot;);&#xA;    $(&quot;#&quot;+id+&quot;&quot;).parent(&quot;li&quot;).css(&quot;color&quot;,&quot;black&quot;);                 &#xA;    $(this).parent(&quot;li&quot;).remove();  // This is not working&#xA;    retrieveItems();&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But &lt;code&gt;$(this)&lt;/code&gt; is undefined. Any ideas?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2138" OwnerDisplayName="Sergio del Amo" LastEditorUserId="7079025" LastEditDate="2019-03-22T15:23:33.153" LastActivityDate="2019-03-22T15:23:33.153" Title="access $(this) with href=&quot;javascript:...&quot; in jQuery" Tags="&lt;jquery&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
