  <row Id="4745475" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4746078" CreationDate="2011-01-20T09:39:24.960" Score="4" ViewCount="471" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like a function, that when passed a string containing only letters, rotates each letter in the string through the alphabet by X characters, where X is a parameter of the function. The famous instance of this is when X=13, which is called &lt;a href=&quot;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ROT13&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;ROT-13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;function &amp;lt;- ROTx(str,x) {&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;??&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;}&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It's the kind of thing that I'd expect an R wizard could do in just a few lines, whereas I'd end up with 10 or more.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="302378" LastActivityDate="2011-01-20T10:45:58.833" Title="Implement ROT-13 in R" Tags="&lt;string&gt;&lt;r&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
