or something. So state.region must be its own object. So I do a str() on it:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;1&amp;gt; str(state.region)&#xA; Factor w/ 4 levels &quot;Northeast&quot;,&quot;South&quot;,..: 2 4 4 2 4 4 1 2 2 2 ...&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It looks like state.region is just a factor. Somehow there HAS to be a connection between state.region and state.x77 in order for aggregate() to group state.x77 by state.region. But that connection is a mystery to me. Can you help me fill in my obvious misunderstandings?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="37751" LastActivityDate="2011-01-20T18:26:50.053" Title="Aggregate() example in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;aggregate&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="3" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
