  <row Id="60932" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:19:34.693" Score="5" ViewCount="7741" Body="&lt;p&gt;Choosing the correct lifecycle and methodology isn't as easy as it was before when there weren't so many methodologies, this days a new one emerges every day.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I've found that most projects require a certain level of evolution and that each project is different from the rest. That way, extreme programming works with for a project for a given company with 15 employees but doesn't quite work with a 100 employee company or doesn't work for a given project type (for example real time application, scientific application, etc).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I'd like to have a list of experiences, mostly stating the project type, the project size (number of people working on it), the project time (real or planned), the project lifecycle and methodology and if the project succeded or failed. Any other data will be appreciated, I think we might find some patterns if there's enough data. Of course, comments are welcomed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;PS: Very large, PT: Very long, LC:&#xA;Incremental-CMMI, PR: Success&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;PS: Very large, PT: Very long, LC:&#xA;Waterfall-CMMI, PR: Success&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edit:&lt;/strong&gt; I'll be constructing a &quot;summary&quot; with the stats of all answers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2695" OwnerDisplayName="Jorge" LastEditorUserId="21234" LastEditorDisplayName="Jorge" LastEditDate="2011-07-25T22:33:16.643" LastActivityDate="2011-07-25T22:33:16.643" Title="Real life examples of methodologies and lifecycles" Tags="&lt;methodology&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="2" ClosedDate="2017-01-21T21:26:11.277" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="60939" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="60965" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:27:38.247" Score="24" ViewCount="3673" Body="&lt;p&gt;When you are starting a personal programming project, what is your first step? I'm trying to start a project thats just an idea at the moment. I get lots of these and I dive right into the code and after a while just completely lose interest and or just forget about the project.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When you are starting, what is your first step? do you plan out the project? make a diagram? write some code on paper? How do you start a project in a manner that you know you will succeed?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2128" OwnerDisplayName="The.Anti.9" LastEditorUserId="1471" LastEditorDisplayName="Outlaw Programmer" LastEditDate="2008-09-14T05:04:30.120" LastActivityDate="2016-06-15T03:43:36.450" Title="The best way to start a project" Tags="&lt;project-management&gt;&lt;projects&gt;&lt;project-planning&gt;" AnswerCount="14" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="11" ClosedDate="2016-06-15T08:55:05.063" CommunityOwnedDate="2009-02-22T16:39:47.093" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60942" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="60955" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:28:36.590" Score="83" ViewCount="30258" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to redirect the stdout of process proc1 to two processes proc2 and proc3:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;         proc2 -&amp;gt; stdout&#xA;       /&#xA; proc1&#xA;       \ &#xA;         proc3 -&amp;gt; stdout&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; proc1 | (proc2 &amp;amp; proc3)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;but it doesn't seem to work, i.e.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; echo 123 | (tr 1 a &amp;amp; tr 1 b)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;writes&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; b23&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;to stdout instead of &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; a23&#xA; b23&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4085" OwnerDisplayName="secr" LastEditorUserId="6899" LastEditorDisplayName="ΤΖΩΤΖΙΟΥ" LastEditDate="2008-10-10T10:47:06.880" LastActivityDate="2020-06-04T06:37:01.980" Title="How can I send the stdout of one process to multiple processes using (preferably unnamed) pipes in Unix (or Windows)?" Tags="&lt;windows&gt;&lt;bash&gt;&lt;unix&gt;&lt;shell&gt;&lt;pipe&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="33" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4767701" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4768084" CreationDate="2011-01-22T12:03:51.930" Score="4" ViewCount="1344" Body="&lt;p&gt;I have an object of type data.frame like this, but much bigger:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt; head(mydf)  &#xA;   id1     id2   n  &#xA;1    0 1032142   3  &#xA;2    0 1072163   1  &#xA;3    0  119323   2  &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I need to print to a file columns &lt;code&gt;a1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;a1&lt;/code&gt;, each of them &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt; times. So that I could get a file like that:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;0 1032142  &#xA;0 1032142  &#xA;0 1032142  &#xA;0 1072163  &#xA;0  119323  &#xA;0  119323  &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried the following solutions, but they make use of explicit &lt;code&gt;for&lt;/code&gt; loops and are incredibly slow (it take few days to finish them with my data...):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (j in 1:(nrow(mydf))) for (i in 1:(mydf[j,&quot;n&quot;])) write.table( mydf[j,c(&quot;id1&quot;,&quot;id2&quot;)], file=&quot;trials&quot;, append=T, row.names= F, col.names=F )&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The other tries to build a new data.frame with multiplied rows, but it is even slower to run.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;towrite=data.frame(); for (j in 1:(nrow(mydf))) for (i in 1:(mydf[j,&quot;n&quot;])) towrite=rbind(towrite,mydf[j,c(&quot;id1&quot;,&quot;id2&quot;)])&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is the simplest and fastest way of resolving this under R?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="213683" LastActivityDate="2011-01-22T16:12:50.007" Title="R: Fast multiply selected rows in data.frame (or other data structure)" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;dataframe&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="4770515" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2011-01-22T20:53:33.443" Score="4" ViewCount="2139" Body="&lt;p&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;tk_choose.files&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;file.choose&lt;/code&gt; I am able to select a file interactively. Is there an analogous function wherein I can allow a user to interactively decide where to save the output of a write.table?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="313163" LastEditorUserId="491785" LastEditDate="2011-01-22T20:58:48.520" LastActivityDate="2017-09-25T12:25:05.797" Title="Save a file interactively?" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;file-io&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60944" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61029" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:29:57.213" Score="0" ViewCount="2208" Body="&lt;p&gt;The below HTML/CSS/Javascript (jQuery) code displays the &lt;code&gt;#makes&lt;/code&gt; select box. Selecting an option displays the &lt;code&gt;#models&lt;/code&gt; select box with relevant options. The &lt;code&gt;#makes&lt;/code&gt; select box sits off-center and the &lt;code&gt;#models&lt;/code&gt; select box fills the empty space when it is displayed. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How do you style the form so that the &lt;code&gt;#makes&lt;/code&gt; select box is centered when it is the only form element displayed, but when both select boxes are displayed, they are both centered within the container?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;snippet&quot; data-lang=&quot;js&quot; data-hide=&quot;false&quot; data-console=&quot;true&quot; data-babel=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&quot;snippet-code&quot;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;var cars = [&#xD;&#xA;  {&#xD;&#xA;    &quot;makes&quot;  : &quot;Honda&quot;,&#xD;&#xA;    &quot;models&quot;  : ['Accord','CRV','Pilot']&#xD;&#xA;  }, &#xD;&#xA;  {&#xD;&#xA;    &quot;makes&quot;   :&quot;Toyota&quot;,&#xD;&#xA;    &quot;models&quot;  : ['Prius','Camry','Corolla']&#xD;&#xA;  }&#xD;&#xA;];&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;$(function() {&#xD;&#xA;  vehicles = [] ;&#xD;&#xA;  for(var i = 0; i &amp;lt; cars.length; i++) {&#xD;&#xA;    vehicles[cars[i].makes] = cars[i].models ;&#xD;&#xA;  }&#xD;&#xA;  var options = '';&#xD;&#xA;  for (var i = 0; i &amp;lt; cars.length; i++) {&#xD;&#xA;    options += '&amp;lt;option value=&quot;' + cars[i].makes + '&quot;&amp;gt;' + cars[i].makes + '&amp;lt;/option&amp;gt;';&#xD;&#xA;  }&#xD;&#xA;  $(&quot;#make&quot;).html(options);   // populate select box with array&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  $(&quot;#make&quot;).bind(&quot;click&quot;, function() {&#xD;&#xA;    $(&quot;#model&quot;).children().remove() ;   // clear select box&#xD;&#xA;    var options = '';&#xD;&#xA;    for (var i = 0; i &amp;lt; vehicles[this.value].length; i++) {&#xD;&#xA;      options += '&amp;lt;option value=&quot;' + vehicles[this.value][i] + '&quot;&amp;gt;' +&#xD;&#xA;        vehicles[this.value][i] +&#xD;&#xA;        '&amp;lt;/option&amp;gt;';&#xD;&#xA;    }&#xD;&#xA;    $(&quot;#model&quot;).html(options);   // populate select box with array&#xD;&#xA;    $(&quot;#models&quot;).addClass(&quot;show&quot;);&#xD;&#xA;  });     // bind end&#xD;&#xA;});&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;.hide {&#xD;&#xA;  display: none;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;.show {&#xD;&#xA;  display: inline;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;fieldset {&#xD;&#xA;  border: #206ba4 1px solid;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;fieldset legend {&#xD;&#xA;  margin-top: -.4em;&#xD;&#xA;  font-size: 20px;&#xD;&#xA;  font-weight: bold;&#xD;&#xA;  color: #206ba4;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;fieldset fieldset {&#xD;&#xA;  position: relative;&#xD;&#xA;  margin-top: 25px;&#xD;&#xA;  padding-top: .75em;&#xD;&#xA;  background-color: #ebf4fa;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;body {&#xD;&#xA;  margin: 0;&#xD;&#xA;  padding: 0;&#xD;&#xA;  font-family: Verdana;&#xD;&#xA;  font-size: 12px;&#xD;&#xA;  text-align: center;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#wrapper {&#xD;&#xA;  margin: 40px auto 0;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#myFieldset {&#xD;&#xA;  width: 213px;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#area {&#xD;&#xA;  margin: 20px;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#area select {&#xD;&#xA;  width: 75px;&#xD;&#xA;  float: left;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#area label {&#xD;&#xA;  display: block;&#xD;&#xA;  font-size: 1.1em;&#xD;&#xA;  font-weight: bold;&#xD;&#xA;  color: #000;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#area #selection {&#xD;&#xA;  display: block;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#makes {&#xD;&#xA;  margin: 5px;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;#models {&#xD;&#xA;  margin: 5px;&#xD;&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&quot;snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.8.0/jquery.min.js&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;div id=&quot;wrapper&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &amp;lt;fieldset id=&quot;myFieldset&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &amp;lt;legend&amp;gt;Cars&amp;lt;/legend&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &amp;lt;fieldset id=&quot;area&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &amp;lt;label&amp;gt;Select Make:&amp;lt;/label&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &amp;lt;div id=&quot;selection&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &amp;lt;div id=&quot;makes&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;          &amp;lt;select id=&quot;make&quot;size=&quot;2&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/select&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &amp;lt;div class=&quot;hide&quot; id=&quot;models&quot;&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;          &amp;lt;select id=&quot;model&quot; size=&quot;3&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/select&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &amp;lt;/fieldset&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &amp;lt;/fieldset&amp;gt;&#xD;&#xA;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2755" OwnerDisplayName="CarolinaJay65" LastEditorUserId="2571493" LastEditDate="2016-12-03T18:58:40.627" LastActivityDate="2016-12-03T18:58:40.627" Title="What are the CSS secrets to a flexible/fluid HTML form?" Tags="&lt;javascript&gt;&lt;jquery&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;css&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="4770606" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4771064" CreationDate="2011-01-22T21:11:43.413" Score="2" ViewCount="246" Body="&lt;p&gt;I would like to find all of the Tuesdays between two dates. But if the Tuesday falls on a user-defined list of holidays, then I would like Wednesday instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This code works in my tests, but it is pretty janky and I am afraid it will fail silently.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;low.date &amp;lt;- &quot;1996-01-01&quot;&#xA;high.date &amp;lt;- &quot;1997-01-01&quot;&#xA;holidays = c(&quot;01-01&quot;, &quot;07-04&quot;, &quot;12-25&quot;)&#xA;tues &amp;lt;- seq(as.Date(low.date), as.Date(high.date), by = 1) &#xA;tues &amp;lt;- subset(tues, format(tues, &quot;%a&quot;) == &quot;Tue&quot;)&#xA;tues &amp;lt;- ifelse(format(tues, &quot;%m-%d&quot;) %in% holidays, tues + 1, tues)&#xA;tues &amp;lt;- as.Date(tues, origin = &quot;1970-01-01&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks! I see answers pointing to the &lt;code&gt;timeDate&lt;/code&gt; package, but I only see methods for finding business days or holidays. Is there a cleaner/safer logic than what I'm using?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="334755" LastEditorUserId="334755" LastEditDate="2011-01-22T23:03:19.460" LastActivityDate="2011-01-23T18:32:32.660" Title="Get vector of Tuesdays, but if Tuesday falls on a holiday, then replace it with Wednesday in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;date&gt;&lt;dayofweek&gt;" AnswerCount="2" CommentCount="2" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60950" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="10904494" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:33:26.313" Score="316" ViewCount="315355" Body="&lt;p&gt;I find working on the command line in Windows frustrating, primarily because the console window is wretched to use compared to terminal applications on linux and OS X such as &quot;rxvt&quot;, &quot;xterm&quot;, or &quot;Terminal&quot;.  Major complaints:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;No standard copy/paste.  You have to turn on &quot;mark&quot; mode and it's only available from a multi-level popup triggered by the (small) left hand corner button.  Then copy and paste need to be invoked from the same menu&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can't arbitrarily resize the window by dragging, you need to set a preference (back to the multi-level popup) each time you want to resize a window&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can only make the window so big before horizontal scroll bars enter the picture. Horizontal scroll bars suck.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;With the cmd.exe shell, you can't navigate to folders with \\netpath notation (UNC?), you need to map a network drive.  This sucks when working on multiple machines that are going to have different drives mapped&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Are there any tricks or applications, (paid or otherwise), that address these issue?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4668" OwnerDisplayName="Alan Storm" LastEditorUserId="7211" LastEditorDisplayName="ΤΖΩΤΖΙΟΥ" LastEditDate="2013-03-13T09:47:17.500" LastActivityDate="2017-01-28T19:37:28.113" Title="Is there a better Windows Console Window?" Tags="&lt;windows&gt;&lt;command-line&gt;&lt;console&gt;&lt;terminal&gt;&lt;command-line-interface&gt;" AnswerCount="15" CommentCount="13" FavoriteCount="256" ClosedDate="2012-12-17T23:17:46.177" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="60967" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61144" CreationDate="2008-09-13T22:59:54.300" Score="1" ViewCount="344" Body="&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, my question is not as simple as keeping track of two windows created by the same process.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here is what I have:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Two users, Jack and Jim are remotely logged in to the same Unix system and run X servers&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Jack runs an application, 'AwesomeApp', that opens a GUI in a X window&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Jim runs another instance of this application, opening his own GUI window&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Now, Jack runs a supervisor application that will communicate with the process owning the first window (eg 'AwesomeApp') because it's HIS instance of 'AwesomeApp'&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;How can his instance of the supervisor find which instance of 'AwesomeApp' window is his own?&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Aaaahhhh...looking it up on a per-user basis yes that could work.&#xA;As long as I tell the users that they cannot log in with the same user account from two different places.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="6253" OwnerDisplayName="Fusion" LastEditorUserId="1288" LastEditDate="2011-11-25T01:24:14.613" LastActivityDate="2011-11-25T01:24:14.613" Title="How do I keep track of related windows in X11?" Tags="&lt;x11&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="4770648" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4770982" CreationDate="2011-01-22T21:17:41.327" Score="3" ViewCount="444" Body="&lt;p&gt;Suppose I want to create n=3 random walk paths (pathlength = 100) given a pre-generated matrix (100x3) of plus/minus ones. The first path will start at 10, the second at 20, the third at 30:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;&#xA;set.seed(123) &lt;br&gt;&#xA;given.rand.matrix &amp;lt;- replicate(3,sign(rnorm(100))) &lt;br&gt;&#xA;path &amp;lt;- matrix(NA,101,3) &lt;br&gt;&#xA;path[1,] = c(10,20,30)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;for (j in 2:101) {&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&amp;nbsp; path[j,]&amp;lt;-path[j-1,]+given.rand.matrix[j-1,]&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The end values (given the seed and rand matrix) are 14, 6, 34... which is the desired result... but...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question&lt;/strong&gt;: Is there a way to vectorize the for loop? The problem is that the path matrix is not yet fully populated when calculating. Thus, replacing the loop with&#xA;&lt;code&gt;&#xA;path[2:101,]&amp;lt;-path[1:100,]+given.rand.matrix &#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;returns mostly NAs. I just want to know if this type of for loop is avoidable in R.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thank you very much in advance.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="585899" LastEditorUserId="415690" LastEditDate="2011-01-22T22:59:16.007" LastActivityDate="2011-01-22T22:59:16.007" Title="vectorize this for loop (current row is dependent on row above)" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;vectorization&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60972" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61304" CreationDate="2008-09-13T23:14:51.380" Score="2" ViewCount="5370" Body="&lt;p&gt;How do you create a database from an Entity Data Model.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So I created a database using the EDM Designer in VisualStudio 2008, and now I want to generate the SQL Server Schema to create storage in SQL Server. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2744" OwnerDisplayName="mrbradleyt" LastActivityDate="2011-04-07T23:16:49.660" Title="How do you create a database from an EDM?" Tags="&lt;sql&gt;&lt;entity-framework&gt;&lt;ado.net&gt;" AnswerCount="5" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60973" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="60999" CreationDate="2008-09-13T23:15:24.513" Score="-1" ViewCount="270" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am upgrading an asp.net 2.0 site to 3.5 and visual studio 2008.  What would be the one thing that you would recommend looking into for upgrade to benefit the site?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4653" OwnerDisplayName="akantro" LastEditorUserId="881229" LastEditDate="2014-01-23T16:50:56.710" LastActivityDate="2014-01-23T16:50:56.710" Title="Whats your favorite new feature in asp.net 3.5?" Tags="&lt;c#&gt;&lt;asp.net&gt;" AnswerCount="3" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="1" ClosedDate="2014-08-17T07:04:11.410" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="60977" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61105" CreationDate="2008-09-13T23:19:40.510" Score="0" ViewCount="282" Body="&lt;p&gt;Sometimes I have to work on code that moves the computer clock forward. In this case some .cpp or .h files get their latest modification date set to the future time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Later on, when my clock is fixed, and I compile my sources, system rebuilds most of the project because some of the latest modification dates are in the future.  Each subsequent recompile has the same problem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Solution that I know are:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;a) Find the file that has the future time and re-save it. This method is not ideal because the project is very big and it takes time even for windows advanced search to find the files that are changed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;b) Delete the whole project and re-check it out from svn.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Does anyone know how I can get around this problem?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there perhaps a setting in visual studio that will allow me to tell the compiler to use the archive bit instead of the last modification date to detect source file changes?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Or perhaps there is a recursive modification date reset tool that can be used in this situation?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="3153" OwnerDisplayName="Brian R. Bondy" LastEditorUserId="1459996" LastEditorDisplayName="Brian R. Bondy" LastEditDate="2017-02-07T03:37:12.027" LastActivityDate="2017-02-07T03:37:12.027" Title="Resetting detection of source file changes" Tags="&lt;c++&gt;&lt;visual-studio&gt;&lt;svn&gt;&lt;time&gt;&lt;timezone&gt;" AnswerCount="6" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 3.0" />
  <row Id="60995" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2008-09-13T23:47:04.810" Score="1" ViewCount="5173" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to verify when the OAB (Offline Address Book) root folder for a new OAB is created with powershell.  Is there a WMI class that exposes this?  I'm using powershell, but any examples or links will do.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="1635" OwnerDisplayName="slipsec" LastEditorUserId="1635" LastEditorDisplayName="slipsec" LastEditDate="2008-09-15T18:16:32.983" LastActivityDate="2008-10-02T20:36:58.037" Title="How do I access the non-IPM_SUBTREE Public Folder Tree with WMI?" Tags="&lt;powershell&gt;&lt;scripting&gt;&lt;wmi&gt;&lt;exchange-server&gt;" AnswerCount="1" CommentCount="0" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="61000" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="4540307" CreationDate="2008-09-14T00:01:15.510" Score="6" ViewCount="8249" Body="&lt;p&gt;I am wondering what  directory structure are commonly used in development projects. I mean with the idea of facilitating builds, deploys release, and etc.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I recently used a &lt;a href=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/guides/introduction/introduction-to-the-standard-directory-layout.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Maven structure&lt;/a&gt; for a java project, but I am not sure it's the best structure for a non-maven driven project.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So, I have two questions: When you guys start new projects, what structure you use? And: What if you need to integrate two different languages, like for example java classes into a PHP application; PHP files are source files, web files, you you use a /src, /classes, webapps/php ? What are your choices in such scenarios. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As a note: I am wondering also what are you choices for directories names. I like the 3-letters names (src, lib, bin, web, img, css, xml, cfg) but what are your opinions about descriptive names like libraris, sources or htdocs/public_html ?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="2274" OwnerDisplayName="Fernando Barrocal" LastEditorUserId="2274" LastEditorDisplayName="Fernando Barrocal" LastEditDate="2008-09-15T01:53:39.443" LastActivityDate="2011-12-16T16:55:25.070" Title="Development directory Structure" Tags="&lt;directory-structure&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="4" ClosedDate="2011-12-16T17:26:58.873" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
  <row Id="61002" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="62303" CreationDate="2008-09-14T00:02:41.420" Score="82" ViewCount="49828" Body="&lt;p&gt;I'd like to script, preferably in rake, the following actions into a single command:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Get the version of my local git repository.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Git pull the latest code.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Git diff from the version I extracted in step #1 to what is now in my local repository.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In other words, I want to get the latest code form the central repository and immediately generate a diff of what's changed since the last time I pulled.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="4061" OwnerDisplayName="Teflon Ted" LastActivityDate="2010-05-14T00:31:19.463" Title="How can I generate a git diff of what's changed since the last time I pulled?" Tags="&lt;git&gt;&lt;diff&gt;&lt;rake&gt;&lt;pull&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="43" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
