  <row Id="61008" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="61019" CreationDate="2008-09-14T00:13:07.073" Score="10" ViewCount="5652" Body="&lt;p&gt;I know this is a broad question, but I've inherited several poor performers and need to optimize them badly. I was wondering what are the most common steps involved to optimize. So, what steps do some of you guys take when faced with the same situation?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Related Question:&lt;br&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/39331/what-generic-techniques-can-be-applied-to-optimize-sql-queries&quot;&gt;What generic techniques can be applied to optimize SQL queries?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="5469" OwnerDisplayName="Kilhoffer" LastEditorUserId="-1" LastEditorDisplayName="Jeff Atwood" LastEditDate="2017-05-23T12:08:35.993" LastActivityDate="2017-07-04T10:18:48.557" Title="What steps should be necessary to optimize a poorly performing query?" Tags="&lt;sql-server&gt;&lt;optimization&gt;" AnswerCount="7" CommentCount="1" FavoriteCount="4" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
