  <row Id="61456" PostTypeId="1" AcceptedAnswerId="66527" CreationDate="2008-09-14T16:43:56.147" Score="14" ViewCount="23567" Body="&lt;p&gt;After trying to avoid JavaScript for years, Iv started using Query for &lt;a href=&quot;http://bassistance.de/jquery-plugins/jquery-plugin-validation/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;validation&lt;/a&gt; in MVC asp.net, as there does not seem to be an official way of doing validation, Iv been surprised how good jQuery is. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Firstly is there a way to get intellisense working for jQuery and its validation plugin, so that i don have to learn the api?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Secondly how do I create a validation summary for this, it currently appends the error to the right of the text box.:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&amp;gt;&#xA;$().ready(function() {&#xA;$(&quot;#CreateLog&quot;).validate({&#xA;        rules: {            &#xA;            UserName: {&#xA;                required: true,&#xA;                minLength: 2,&#xA;&#xA;            }&#xA;        },&#xA;        messages: {&#xA;&#xA;            UserName: {&#xA;                required: &quot;Please enter a username&quot;,&#xA;                minLength: &quot;Your username must consist of at least 2 characters&quot;,&#xA;&#xA;            }&#xA;        }&#xA;    });&#xA;});&#xA;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&#xA;&#xA;&amp;lt;form id=&quot;CreateLog&quot; action=&quot;Create&quot; method=&quot;post&quot; /&amp;gt;   &#xA;        &amp;lt;label&amp;gt;UserName&amp;lt;/label&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;%=Html.TextBox(&quot;UserName&quot;)%&amp;gt; &#xA;         &amp;lt;br /&amp;gt;  &#xA;          &amp;lt;div class=&quot;error&quot;&amp;gt; &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xA;        &amp;lt;input  type=submit value=Save /&amp;gt;&#xA;       &amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I tried adding this to the script:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt; errorLabelContainer: $(&quot;#CreateLog div.error&quot;)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;and this to the html:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  &amp;lt;div class=&quot;error&quot;&amp;gt; &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But this didn't work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="230" OwnerDisplayName="Dan" LastEditorUserId="7079025" LastEditorDisplayName="Dan" LastEditDate="2019-03-22T15:19:23.773" LastActivityDate="2019-03-22T15:21:15.560" Title="MVC.net jQuery Validation" Tags="&lt;jquery&gt;&lt;asp.net-mvc&gt;&lt;validation&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="0" FavoriteCount="12" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <row Id="4795982" PostTypeId="1" CreationDate="2011-01-25T16:17:56.173" Score="34" ViewCount="4458" Body="&lt;p&gt;I've been given a big chunk of poorly formatted monolithic R code with plenty of functions, and I'd like to work out what functions call what functions. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I thought I could use roxygen's @callGraph stuff, but a) the code needs to be in a package, which will be a headache with this code, and b) it doesn't even seem to work when I do run it on a simple package of mine. I see a posting from one of the Roxygen authors saying call graph generation is disabled because of the Rgraphviz dependency, but the code is there. Anyway.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Anyone got a better way of quickly working out that foo calls bar, baz, and qux, and that qux calls quux?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit: Solutions based on R's profiling system are great, assuming you can actually run the code... Half the stuff in the files doesn't get run, and I don't know what it does... Static analysis is too much to hope for, I guess.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit 2: Roxygen's call graph stuff seems to do a static analysis, based on recursive descent of the expression of the function and checking for is.callable. It would be lovely to be able to run this on any function... I may play with this tomorrow...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;" OwnerUserId="211116" LastEditorUserId="1243762" LastEditDate="2012-08-08T21:26:55.923" LastActivityDate="2017-06-04T17:21:41.507" Title="Generating a Call Graph in R" Tags="&lt;r&gt;&lt;call-graph&gt;" AnswerCount="4" CommentCount="4" FavoriteCount="11" ContentLicense="CC BY-SA 2.5" />
